{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824283336,"sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9d732400019LvRYEZeUdD4gO","sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","messageID":"msg_0b9d72d65001ZK25cJk5457Xeo","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ET_u471GQBXuRlM6FK2z6K60401","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt","limit":400},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt, lines 1-400\n1: \n2: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n3: \n4: Table of Contents\n5: MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\n6: 404 Wyman Street, Suite 400\n7: Waltham, Massachusetts 02451\n8: December 4, 2013\n9: Dear\n10: Stockholder:\n11: You\n12: are cordially invited to attend a special meeting of stockholders of Mac-Gray Corporation (\"Mac-Gray\" or the \"Company\") to be held on Wednesday, January 8, 2014, at\n13: 10:00 a.m. local time, at the Goodwin Procter\n14: LLP\n15: Conference Center, Second Floor, Exchange Place, 53 State Street, Boston, Massachusetts 02109\n16: (the \"special meeting\").\n17: At\n18: the special meeting, you will be asked to consider and vote upon a proposal to adopt a merger agreement pursuant to which Mac-Gray would be acquired by Spin Holdco Inc. a\n19: wholly-owned subsidiary of CSC ServiceWorks, Inc., and other related proposals. We entered into the merger agreement on October 14, 2013. If the merger is completed, you will be entitled\n20: to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest and less any applicable withholding taxes, for each share of Mac-Gray common stock that you own.\n21: The\n22: Mac-Gray Board of Directors formed a special committee of six disinterested and independent directors to, among other things, review and evaluate the merger agreement proposal,\n23: consider and evaluate alternatives available to Mac-Gray and alleviate any potential conflicts of interest. After careful consideration, our Board of Directors, upon the unanimous recommendation of\n24: the special committee, unanimously approved the merger agreement and determined that the merger and the other transactions contemplated by the merger agreement are advisable and in the best interests\n25: of Mac-Gray and our stockholders. Our Board of Directors unanimously recommends that you vote \"FOR\" the adoption of the merger agreement.\n26: At\n27: the special meeting, in addition to the approval of the merger agreement, you will be asked to cast an advisory (non-binding) vote on the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or\n28: that could become payable to the named executive officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant to the terms of the merger agreement and pre-existing arrangements. Our Board of Directors\n29: unanimously recommends that you vote \"FOR\" approval, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, of the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable to the named executive officers of\n30: Mac-Gray in connection with the merger.\n31: Your vote is important, regardless of the number of shares of Mac-Gray common stock you own.\n32: We cannot consummate the merger unless the\n33: merger\n34: agreement is adopted by the affirmative vote of a majority of the outstanding shares of Mac-Gray common stock entitled to vote at the special meeting. If you abstain from voting, fail to cast your\n35: vote, in person or by proxy, or fail to give voting instructions to your brokerage firm, bank, trust or other nominee, it will have the same effect as a vote against the proposal to adopt the merger\n36: agreement.\n37: The\n38: attached proxy statement provides you with detailed information about the special meeting, the merger agreement and the merger. A copy of the merger agreement is attached as\n39: Annex A to the proxy statement. We encourage you to read the proxy statement and the merger agreement carefully and in their entirety. You may also obtain more information about Mac-Gray from\n40: documents we have filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission.\n41: On\n42: behalf of your Board of Directors, thank you for your continued support and interest in Mac-Gray Corporation. I look forward to seeing you at the meeting on January 8, 2014.\n43: Very\n44: truly yours,\n45: STEWART GRAY MACDONALD, JR.\n46: Chief Executive Officer\n47: \n48: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n49: \n50: Table of Contents\n51: Your vote is very important regardless of the number of shares you own. At your earliest convenience, please vote by telephone or via the Internet according to\n52: the instructions provided on the enclosed proxy card or complete, sign, date and return the enclosed proxy card, which requires no postage if mailed in the United States.\n53: Stockholders with questions or requiring assistance voting their shares may contact MacKenzie Partners, Inc., our proxy solicitor:\n54: 105\n55: Madison Avenue\n56: New York, NY 10016\n57: proxy@mackenziepartners.com\n58: (212) 929-5500 (Call Collect)\n59: or\n60: TOLL FREE 1-800-322-2885\n61: Neither the Securities and Exchange Commission nor any state securities regulatory agency has approved or disapproved the merger, passed upon the merits or\n62: fairness of the merger or passed upon the adequacy or accuracy of the disclosure in this document. Any representation to the contrary is a criminal offense.\n63: This\n64: proxy statement is dated December 4, 2013 and is first being mailed to stockholders on or about December 4, 2013.\n65: \n66: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n67: \n68: Table of Contents\n69: MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\n70: 404 Wyman Street, Suite 400\n71: Waltham, Massachusetts 02451\n72: (781) 487-7600\n73: NOTICE OF THE SPECIAL MEETING OF STOCKHOLDERS\n74: TO BE HELD ON JANUARY 8, 2014\n75: NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that a special meeting of stockholders of Mac-Gray Corporation, a Delaware corporation (\"Mac-Gray\" or the \"Company\"), will be held on\n76: Wednesday, January 8, 2014 at 10:00 a.m., local time, at the Goodwin Procter\n77: LLP\n78: Conference Center, Second Floor, Exchange Place, 53 State Street,\n79: Boston, Massachusetts 02109 (together with adjournments or postponements thereof, the \"special meeting\") for the following purposes:\n80: 1.     To\n81: consider and vote on a proposal to adopt the Agreement and Plan of Merger, dated as of October 14, 2013, by and among CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc., a\n82: Delaware corporation (\"Holdings\"), CSC ServiceWorks, Inc., a Delaware corporation and wholly-owned subsidiary of Holdings (\"CSC\"), Spin Holdco Inc., a Delaware corporation and\n83: wholly-owned subsidiary of CSC (\"Parent\" and, together with Holdings and CSC, the \"Buyer Entities\") and CSC Fenway, Inc., a Delaware corporation and a wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent (\"Merger\n84: Subsidiary\") and Mac-Gray, as it may be amended from time to time, pursuant to which Mac-Gray will be merged with Merger Subsidiary with Mac-Gray surviving the merger as a wholly-owned subsidiary of\n85: Parent;\n86: 2.     To\n87: consider and vote on an advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable to the named executive\n88: officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant to the terms of the merger agreement and pre-existing severance arrangements;\n89: 3.     To\n90: consider and vote on a proposal to approve one or more adjournments or postponements of the special meeting, if necessary, to solicit additional proxies if Mac-Gray\n91: has not obtained sufficient affirmative stockholder votes to adopt the merger agreement; and\n92: 4.     To\n93: transact such other business as may properly come before the special meeting or any adjournment or postponement of the special meeting.\n94: The\n95: Board of Directors has fixed the close of business on November 27, 2013 as the record date for determination of stockholders entitled to notice of and to vote at the special meeting\n96: and any adjournments or postponements thereof. Only holders of Mac-Gray's common stock of record at the close of business on that date will be entitled to notice of and to vote at the special meeting\n97: and any adjournments or postponements thereof.\n98: Under\n99: Delaware law, Mac-Gray stockholders who do not vote in favor of the adoption of the merger agreement will have the right to seek appraisal of the fair value of their shares as\n100: determined by the\n101: Delaware Court of Chancery if the merger is completed, but only if they submit a written demand for such an appraisal prior to the vote on the adoption of the merger agreement and comply with the\n102: other Delaware law procedures explained in the section entitled \"Appraisal Rights\" beginning on page 85 of the accompanying proxy statement.\n103: Directions\n104: to the Goodwin Procter\n105: LLP\n106: Conference Center are included on the outside back cover of the Proxy Statement for the special\n107: meeting of Stockholders to be held on January 8, 2014.\n108: THE MAC-GRAY BOARD OF DIRECTORS UNANIMOUSLY RECOMMENDS THAT YOU VOTE \"FOR\" THE PROPOSAL TO ADOPT THE MERGER AGREEMENT, \"FOR\" THE PROPOSAL TO APPROVE, ON AN\n109: ADVISORY (NON-BINDING) BASIS, THE \"GOLDEN PARACHUTE\" COMPENSATION PAYABLE OR THAT COULD BECOME PAYABLE TO THE NAMED EXECUTIVE OFFICERS OF MAC-GRAY IN CONNECTION WITH THE MERGER AND \"FOR\" THE\n110: ADJOURNMENT PROPOSAL.\n111: \n112: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n113: \n114: Table of Contents\n115: By\n116: Order of the Board of Directors,\n117: LINDA A. SERAFINI\n118: Secretary\n119: Waltham,\n120: Massachusetts\n121: December\n122: 4, 2013\n123: WHETHER OR NOT YOU PLAN TO ATTEND THE SPECIAL MEETING IN PERSON, YOU ARE REQUESTED TO VOTE BY TELEPHONE OR VIA THE INTERNET ACCORDING TO THE INSTRUCTIONS ON THE\n124: PROXY CARD OR TO COMPLETE, DATE, SIGN AND RETURN THE ENCLOSED PROXY CARD IN THE ENCLOSED ENVELOPE, WHICH REQUIRES NO POSTAGE IF MAILED IN THE UNITED STATES. IF YOU ATTEND THE SPECIAL MEETING, YOU MAY\n125: VOTE IN PERSON IF YOU WISH, EVEN IF YOU HAVE PREVIOUSLY RETURNED YOUR PROXY CARD OR VOTED BY TELEPHONE OR VIA THE INTERNET.\n126: Important Notice Regarding the Availability of Proxy Materials for the\n127: Special Meeting of Stockholders to be held on January 8, 2014:\n128: These\n129: proxy materials are being made available to stockholders on or about December 4, 2013 at: www.macgray.com/proxy\n130: \n131: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n132: \n133: Table of Contents\n134: Table of Contents\n135: Page\n136: SPECIAL NOTE REGARDING FORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS\n137: 1\n138: SUMMARY TERM SHEET\n139: 2\n140: QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGER AND THE SPECIAL MEETING\n141: 13\n142: THE SPECIAL MEETING\n143: 20\n144: Date, Time, Place and Purpose of the Special Meeting\n145: 20\n146: Record Date and Quorum\n147: 20\n148: Vote Required for Approval\n149: 20\n150: Voting and Proxies\n151: 21\n152: Revocation of Proxies\n153: 22\n154: Postponement and Adjournments\n155: 22\n156: Solicitation of Proxies\n157: 23\n158: Stockholder List\n159: 23\n160: Questions and Additional Information\n161: 23\n162: PROPOSALS SUBMITTED TO MAC-GRAY STOCKHOLDERS\n163: 24\n164: The Merger Agreement Proposal\n165: 24\n166: The \"Golden Parachute\" Proposal\n167: 24\n168: The Adjournment Proposal\n169: 25\n170: THE COMPANIES\n171: 26\n172: THE MERGER\n173: 27\n174: Background of the Merger\n175: 27\n176: Reasons for the Merger and Recommendation of our Board of Directors\n177: 42\n178: Opinion of Mac-Gray's Financial Advisor\n179: 45\n180: Projected Financial Information\n181: 52\n182: Interests of Mac-Gray's Directors and Executive Officers in the Merger\n183: 54\n184: Financing of the Merger\n185: 58\n186: THE MERGER AGREEMENT\n187: 60\n188: The Merger\n189: 60\n190: The Merger Consideration and the Conversion of Capital Stock\n191: 60\n192: Mac-Gray Equity-Based Awards\n193: 61\n194: Mac-Gray Employee Stock Purchase Plan\n195: 61\n196: Payment Procedures\n197: 61\n198: Mac-Gray Representations and Warranties\n199: 62\n200: Conduct of Mac-Gray's Business During the Pendency of the Merger\n201: 65\n202: Mac-Gray Stockholders Meeting\n203: 68\n204: Non-Solicitation; Competing Acquisition Proposals\n205: 69\n206: Mac-Gray Board Recommendation\n207: 70\n208: Mac-Gray Employee Compensation and Benefits\n209: 73\n210: Other Covenants and Agreements\n211: 74\n212: Financing Cooperation\n213: 75\n214: Reasonable Best Efforts\n215: 75\n216: Conditions to the Merger\n217: 77\n218: Termination of the Merger Agreement\n219: 78\n220: Termination Fees and Expenses\n221: 79\n222: Buyer Entity Guarantees\n223: 81\n224: Governing Law\n225: 81\n226: THE VOTING AGREEMENTS\n227: 82\n228: MATERIAL U.S. FEDERAL INCOME TAX CONSIDERATIONS WITH RESPECT TO THE MERGER\n229: 82\n230: REGULATORY MATTERS\n231: 85\n232: LITIGATION RELATED TO THE MERGER\n233: 85\n234: APPRAISAL RIGHTS\n235: 85\n236: CURRENT MARKET PRICE OF COMMON STOCK\n237: 89\n238: SECURITY OWNERSHIP OF MANAGEMENT AND CERTAIN BENEFICIAL OWNERS\n239: 91\n240: FUTURE STOCKHOLDER PROPOSALS\n241: 95\n242: WHERE YOU CAN FIND MORE INFORMATION\n243: 95\n244: MULTIPLE STOCKHOLDERS SHARING ONE ADDRESS\n245: 96\n246: \n247: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n248: \n249: Table of Contents\n250: SPECIAL NOTE REGARDING FORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS\n251: This proxy statement and the documents to which we refer you in this proxy statement contain forward-looking statements within the\n252: meaning of Section 27A of the Securities Act of 1933, as amended, which we refer to as the Securities Act, and Section 21E of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended, which we\n253: refer to as the Exchange Act, including statements regarding the proposed transaction, the anticipated results of the proposed transaction and the timing of the proposed transaction. Mac-Gray intends\n254: such forward-looking statements to be covered by the Safe Harbor provisions for forward-looking statements contained in the Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995, and is including this\n255: statement for purposes of complying with these Safe Harbor provisions.\n256: These\n257: forward-looking statements contain projections of our future results of operations or financial position or state other forward-looking information. In some cases you can identify\n258: these statements by forward-looking words such as \"anticipate,\" \"believe,\" \"could,\" \"estimate,\" \"expect,\" \"intend,\" \"may,\" \"plan,\" \"predict,\" \"should,\" \"target,\" \"will\" and \"would,\" or similar words.\n259: You should not rely on forward-looking statements because they involve known and unknown risks, uncertainties, and other factors, some of which are beyond our control. These risks, uncertainties, and\n260: other factors may cause our actual results, performance or achievements to differ materially from the anticipated future results,\n261: performance or achievements expressed or implied by the forward-looking statements. Some of the factors that might cause these differences are as\n262: follows:\n263: •\n264: the possibility that any of the closing conditions to the consummation of the merger will not be satisfied and the merger\n265: will not be completed;\n266: •\n267: the possibility that Mac-Gray stockholders will not adopt the merger agreement under applicable law and the merger\n268: agreement;\n269: •\n270: the inability to obtain regulatory approvals required for the merger or the imposition of certain regulatory conditions on\n271: the Buyer Entities;\n272: •\n273: the occurrence of any event, change or other circumstance that could give rise to the termination of the merger agreement;\n274: •\n275: the impact of the announcement of the merger on Mac-Gray's operating results and relationships with its employees,\n276: partners, suppliers and customers;\n277: •\n278: the impact of the pending merger on Mac-Gray's strategic plans and operations and Mac-Gray's ability to respond\n279: effectively to competitive pressures, industry developments and future opportunities; and\n280: •\n281: other risks detailed in Mac-Gray's filings with the Securities and Exchange Commission, or SEC, including Mac-Gray's\n282: Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended December 31, 2012 and in other reports filed with the SEC. See \"Where You Can Find More Information\" on page 94 of this proxy\n283: statement.\n284: You\n285: should not place undue reliance on forward-looking statements. We cannot guarantee any future results, levels of activity, performance or achievements. The statements made in this\n286: proxy statement are based on the information available to us as of the date of this proxy statement, and you should not assume that the statements made in this proxy statement remain accurate as of\n287: any future date. Moreover, except as required by law, we assume no obligation to update forward-looking statements or update the reasons actual results could differ materially from those anticipated\n288: in forward-looking statements. All forward-looking statements in this document are qualified in their entirety by this cautionary statement.\n289: 1\n290: \n291: <<<PAGE folio=1>>>\n292: \n293: Table of Contents\n294: SUMMARY TERM SHEET\n295: The following summary highlights information in this proxy statement and may not contain all the information\n296: that is important to you. Accordingly, we encourage you to read carefully this entire proxy statement, its annexes and the documents referred to in this proxy statement. Each item in this summary\n297: includes a page reference directing you to a more complete description of the item in this proxy statement.\n298: In this proxy statement, the terms \"we,\" \"us,\" \"our company,\" and \"Mac-Gray\" refer to Mac-Gray Corporation, the term \"Parent\" refers to Spin Holdco Inc.,\n299: the term \"Merger Subsidiary\" refers to CSC Fenway, Inc., the term \"Holdings\" refers to CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc., the term \"CSC\" refers to CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. the term\n300: \"Buyer Entity\" refers to any of Parent, Holdings or CSC, as applicable, the term Pamplona refers to Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. and the term \"merger agreement\" refers to the Agreement\n301: and Plan of Merger, dated as of October 14, 2013, by and among Mac-Gray, Parent, Merger Subsidiary, Holdings and CSC, as it may be amended from time to time.\n302: The Companies (Page 26)\n303: Mac-Gray Corporation\n304: , founded in 1927, is the second largest laundry facilities\n305: management contractor in the United States. Through our portfolio of card- and\n306: coin-operated laundry equipment located in laundry facilities across the country, we provide laundry convenience to residents of multi-unit housing such as apartment buildings, condominiums, colleges\n307: and university residence halls, public housing complexes, and hotels and motels. Based on our ongoing survey of colleges and universities, we believe that we are the largest provider of such services\n308: to the college and university market in the United States. We manage laundry rooms in 44 states and the District of Columbia. We also sell and service commercial laundry equipment to retail\n309: laundromats and other customers through our product sales division.\n310: Mac-Gray\n311: Corporation\n312: 404 Wyman Street, Suite 400\n313: Waltham, Massachusetts 02451\n314: (781) 487-7600\n315: CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.,\n316: with over one million machines in service, is the leading provider of multi-family housing and commercial\n317: laundry solutions as well as the industry leader in air vending services at convenience stores and gas stations. CSC's family of businesses includes: Coinmach Corp., ASI Campus Laundry Solutions, SDI\n318: Laundry Solutions, Sparkle Solutions Corp., Appliance Warehouse of America, AIR-serv, AirValet and Super Laundry. CSC has a workforce of over 2,250 dedicated professionals throughout the United\n319: States, Canada and Europe.\n320: CSC\n321: ServiceWorks, Inc.\n322: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n323: Plainview, New York 11803\n324: (516) 349-8555\n325: CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.\n326: is a Delaware corporation and the sole stockholder of CSC.\n327: CSC\n328: ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.\n329: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n330: Plainview, New York 11803\n331: (516) 349-8555\n332: 2\n333: \n334: <<<PAGE folio=2>>>\n335: \n336: Table of Contents\n337: Spin Holdco Inc.\n338: is a Delaware corporation and a wholly-owned subsidiary of CSC.\n339: Spin\n340: Holdco Inc.\n341: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n342: Plainview, New York 11803\n343: (516) 349-8555\n344: CSC Fenway, Inc.\n345: is a Delaware corporation and a wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent.\n346: CSC\n347: Fenway, Inc.\n348: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n349: Plainview, New York 11803\n350: (516) 349-8555\n351: The Special Meeting (Page 20)\n352: Date, Time and Place.\n353: The special meeting will be held on Wednesday, January 8, 2014 at 10:00 a.m., local time, at the\n354: Goodwin Procter\n355: LLP\n356: Conference Center, Second Floor, Exchange Place, 53 State Street, Boston, Massachusetts 02109.\n357: Purpose.\n358: At the special meeting, you will be asked to consider and vote upon (1) a proposal to adopt the merger agreement,\n359: (2) an\n360: advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable to the named executive officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant\n361: to the terms of the merger agreement and pre-existing severance arrangements, (3) a proposal to approve one or more adjournments or postponements of the special meeting, if necessary, to\n362: solicit additional proxies if Mac-Gray has not obtained sufficient affirmative stockholder votes to adopt the merger agreement and (4) such other business as may properly come before the\n363: special meeting or any adjournments or postponements of the special meeting. We are currently not aware of any other business to come before the special meeting.\n364: Record Date and Quorum.\n365: You are entitled to vote at the special meeting if you owned shares of Mac-Gray common stock at the\n366: close of business on\n367: November 27, 2013, the record date for the special meeting. You will have one vote for each share of Mac-Gray common stock that you owned on the record date. As of November 27, 2013,\n368: there were 14,758,306 shares of Mac-Gray common stock issued and outstanding and entitled to vote. A majority of Mac-Gray common stock issued, outstanding and entitled to vote at the special meeting,\n369: present in person or represented by proxy, constitutes a quorum for the purpose of the special meeting.\n370: Voting and Proxies.\n371: Any stockholder of record entitled to vote at the special meeting may submit a proxy by telephone, via the\n372: Internet, by returning\n373: the enclosed proxy card by mail, or by voting in person at the special meeting. If you intend to submit your proxy by telephone or via the Internet, you must do so no later than the date and time\n374: indicated on the applicable proxy card(s). If you intend to vote by returning the enclosed proxy card by mail, please do so as soon as possible to ensure your vote is received in advance of the\n375: special meeting. Even if you plan to attend the special meeting, if on the record date you held shares of Mac-Gray common stock in your own name as the stockholder of record, please vote your shares\n376: by completing, signing, dating and returning the enclosed proxy card or by using the telephone number printed on your proxy card or by using the Internet voting instructions printed on your proxy\n377: card.\n378: If\n379: you give your proxy, but do not indicate how you wish to vote, your shares will be voted \"\n380: FOR\n381: \" the proposal to adopt the merger\n382: agreement, \"\n383: FOR\n384: \" the proposal to approve, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable\n385: to the named executive officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant to the terms of the merger agreement and pre-existing severance arrangements and\n386: \"\n387: FOR\n388: \" the adjournment proposal.\n389: 3\n390: \n391: <<<PAGE folio=3>>>\n392: \n393: Table of Contents\n394: If\n395: your shares of Mac-Gray common stock are held in \"street name,\" you should instruct your brokerage firm, bank, trust or other nominee on how to vote such shares of common stock using\n396: the instructions provided by your broker or nominee. If your shares of Mac-Gray common stock are held in \"street name,\" you must obtain a legal proxy from such nominee in order to vote in person at\n397: the special meeting. If you fail to provide your nominee with instructions on how to vote your shares of Mac-Gray common stock, your nominee will not be able to vote such shares at the special\n398: meeting.\n399: Vote Required.\n400: The adoption of the merger agreement requires the affirmative vote of a majority of the outstanding shares of\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 401]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt, lines 1-400\n1: \n2: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n3: \n4: Table of Contents\n5: MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\n6: 404 Wyman Street, Suite 400\n7: Waltham, Massachusetts 02451\n8: December 4, 2013\n9: Dear\n10: Stockholder:\n11: You\n12: are cordially invited to attend a special meeting of stockholders of Mac-Gray Corporation (\"Mac-Gray\" or the \"Company\") to be held on Wednesday, January 8, 2014, at\n13: 10:00 a.m. local time, at the Goodwin Procter\n14: LLP\n15: Conference Center, Second Floor, Exchange Place, 53 State Street, Boston, Massachusetts 02109\n16: (the \"special meeting\").\n17: At\n18: the special meeting, you will be asked to consider and vote upon a proposal to adopt a merger agreement pursuant to which Mac-Gray would be acquired by Spin Holdco Inc. a\n19: wholly-owned subsidiary of CSC ServiceWorks, Inc., and other related proposals. We entered into the merger agreement on October 14, 2013. If the merger is completed, you will be entitled\n20: to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest and less any applicable withholding taxes, for each share of Mac-Gray common stock that you own.\n21: The\n22: Mac-Gray Board of Directors formed a special committee of six disinterested and independent directors to, among other things, review and evaluate the merger agreement proposal,\n23: consider and evaluate alternatives available to Mac-Gray and alleviate any potential conflicts of interest. After careful consideration, our Board of Directors, upon the unanimous recommendation of\n24: the special committee, unanimously approved the merger agreement and determined that the merger and the other transactions contemplated by the merger agreement are advisable and in the best interests\n25: of Mac-Gray and our stockholders. Our Board of Directors unanimously recommends that you vote \"FOR\" the adoption of the merger agreement.\n26: At\n27: the special meeting, in addition to the approval of the merger agreement, you will be asked to cast an advisory (non-binding) vote on the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or\n28: that could become payable to the named executive officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant to the terms of the merger agreement and pre-existing arrangements. Our Board of Directors\n29: unanimously recommends that you vote \"FOR\" approval, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, of the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable to the named executive officers of\n30: Mac-Gray in connection with the merger.\n31: Your vote is important, regardless of the number of shares of Mac-Gray common stock you own.\n32: We cannot consummate the merger unless the\n33: merger\n34: agreement is adopted by the affirmative vote of a majority of the outstanding shares of Mac-Gray common stock entitled to vote at the special meeting. If you abstain from voting, fail to cast your\n35: vote, in person or by proxy, or fail to give voting instructions to your brokerage firm, bank, trust or other nominee, it will have the same effect as a vote against the proposal to adopt the merger\n36: agreement.\n37: The\n38: attached proxy statement provides you with detailed information about the special meeting, the merger agreement and the merger. A copy of the merger agreement is attached as\n39: Annex A to the proxy statement. We encourage you to read the proxy statement and the merger agreement carefully and in their entirety. You may also obtain more information about Mac-Gray from\n40: documents we have filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission.\n41: On\n42: behalf of your Board of Directors, thank you for your continued support and interest in Mac-Gray Corporation. I look forward to seeing you at the meeting on January 8, 2014.\n43: Very\n44: truly yours,\n45: STEWART GRAY MACDONALD, JR.\n46: Chief Executive Officer\n47: \n48: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n49: \n50: Table of Contents\n51: Your vote is very important regardless of the number of shares you own. At your earliest convenience, please vote by telephone or via the Internet according to\n52: the instructions provided on the enclosed proxy card or complete, sign, date and return the enclosed proxy card, which requires no postage if mailed in the United States.\n53: Stockholders with questions or requiring assistance voting their shares may contact MacKenzie Partners, Inc., our proxy solicitor:\n54: 105\n55: Madison Avenue\n56: New York, NY 10016\n57: proxy@mackenziepartners.com\n58: (212) 929-5500 (Call Collect)\n59: or\n60: TOLL FREE 1-800-322-2885\n61: Neither the Securities and Exchange Commission nor any state securities regulatory agency has approved or disapproved the merger, passed upon the merits or\n62: fairness of the merger or passed upon the adequacy or accuracy of the disclosure in this document. Any representation to the contrary is a criminal offense.\n63: This\n64: proxy statement is dated December 4, 2013 and is first being mailed to stockholders on or about December 4, 2013.\n65: \n66: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n67: \n68: Table of Contents\n69: MAC-GRAY CORPORATION\n70: 404 Wyman Street, Suite 400\n71: Waltham, Massachusetts 02451\n72: (781) 487-7600\n73: NOTICE OF THE SPECIAL MEETING OF STOCKHOLDERS\n74: TO BE HELD ON JANUARY 8, 2014\n75: NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that a special meeting of stockholders of Mac-Gray Corporation, a Delaware corporation (\"Mac-Gray\" or the \"Company\"), will be held on\n76: Wednesday, January 8, 2014 at 10:00 a.m., local time, at the Goodwin Procter\n77: LLP\n78: Conference Center, Second Floor, Exchange Place, 53 State Street,\n79: Boston, Massachusetts 02109 (together with adjournments or postponements thereof, the \"special meeting\") for the following purposes:\n80: 1.     To\n81: consider and vote on a proposal to adopt the Agreement and Plan of Merger, dated as of October 14, 2013, by and among CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc., a\n82: Delaware corporation (\"Holdings\"), CSC ServiceWorks, Inc., a Delaware corporation and wholly-owned subsidiary of Holdings (\"CSC\"), Spin Holdco Inc., a Delaware corporation and\n83: wholly-owned subsidiary of CSC (\"Parent\" and, together with Holdings and CSC, the \"Buyer Entities\") and CSC Fenway, Inc., a Delaware corporation and a wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent (\"Merger\n84: Subsidiary\") and Mac-Gray, as it may be amended from time to time, pursuant to which Mac-Gray will be merged with Merger Subsidiary with Mac-Gray surviving the merger as a wholly-owned subsidiary of\n85: Parent;\n86: 2.     To\n87: consider and vote on an advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable to the named executive\n88: officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant to the terms of the merger agreement and pre-existing severance arrangements;\n89: 3.     To\n90: consider and vote on a proposal to approve one or more adjournments or postponements of the special meeting, if necessary, to solicit additional proxies if Mac-Gray\n91: has not obtained sufficient affirmative stockholder votes to adopt the merger agreement; and\n92: 4.     To\n93: transact such other business as may properly come before the special meeting or any adjournment or postponement of the special meeting.\n94: The\n95: Board of Directors has fixed the close of business on November 27, 2013 as the record date for determination of stockholders entitled to notice of and to vote at the special meeting\n96: and any adjournments or postponements thereof. Only holders of Mac-Gray's common stock of record at the close of business on that date will be entitled to notice of and to vote at the special meeting\n97: and any adjournments or postponements thereof.\n98: Under\n99: Delaware law, Mac-Gray stockholders who do not vote in favor of the adoption of the merger agreement will have the right to seek appraisal of the fair value of their shares as\n100: determined by the\n101: Delaware Court of Chancery if the merger is completed, but only if they submit a written demand for such an appraisal prior to the vote on the adoption of the merger agreement and comply with the\n102: other Delaware law procedures explained in the section entitled \"Appraisal Rights\" beginning on page 85 of the accompanying proxy statement.\n103: Directions\n104: to the Goodwin Procter\n105: LLP\n106: Conference Center are included on the outside back cover of the Proxy Statement for the special\n107: meeting of Stockholders to be held on January 8, 2014.\n108: THE MAC-GRAY BOARD OF DIRECTORS UNANIMOUSLY RECOMMENDS THAT YOU VOTE \"FOR\" THE PROPOSAL TO ADOPT THE MERGER AGREEMENT, \"FOR\" THE PROPOSAL TO APPROVE, ON AN\n109: ADVISORY (NON-BINDING) BASIS, THE \"GOLDEN PARACHUTE\" COMPENSATION PAYABLE OR THAT COULD BECOME PAYABLE TO THE NAMED EXECUTIVE OFFICERS OF MAC-GRAY IN CONNECTION WITH THE MERGER AND \"FOR\" THE\n110: ADJOURNMENT PROPOSAL.\n111: \n112: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n113: \n114: Table of Contents\n115: By\n116: Order of the Board of Directors,\n117: LINDA A. SERAFINI\n118: Secretary\n119: Waltham,\n120: Massachusetts\n121: December\n122: 4, 2013\n123: WHETHER OR NOT YOU PLAN TO ATTEND THE SPECIAL MEETING IN PERSON, YOU ARE REQUESTED TO VOTE BY TELEPHONE OR VIA THE INTERNET ACCORDING TO THE INSTRUCTIONS ON THE\n124: PROXY CARD OR TO COMPLETE, DATE, SIGN AND RETURN THE ENCLOSED PROXY CARD IN THE ENCLOSED ENVELOPE, WHICH REQUIRES NO POSTAGE IF MAILED IN THE UNITED STATES. IF YOU ATTEND THE SPECIAL MEETING, YOU MAY\n125: VOTE IN PERSON IF YOU WISH, EVEN IF YOU HAVE PREVIOUSLY RETURNED YOUR PROXY CARD OR VOTED BY TELEPHONE OR VIA THE INTERNET.\n126: Important Notice Regarding the Availability of Proxy Materials for the\n127: Special Meeting of Stockholders to be held on January 8, 2014:\n128: These\n129: proxy materials are being made available to stockholders on or about December 4, 2013 at: www.macgray.com/proxy\n130: \n131: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n132: \n133: Table of Contents\n134: Table of Contents\n135: Page\n136: SPECIAL NOTE REGARDING FORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS\n137: 1\n138: SUMMARY TERM SHEET\n139: 2\n140: QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGER AND THE SPECIAL MEETING\n141: 13\n142: THE SPECIAL MEETING\n143: 20\n144: Date, Time, Place and Purpose of the Special Meeting\n145: 20\n146: Record Date and Quorum\n147: 20\n148: Vote Required for Approval\n149: 20\n150: Voting and Proxies\n151: 21\n152: Revocation of Proxies\n153: 22\n154: Postponement and Adjournments\n155: 22\n156: Solicitation of Proxies\n157: 23\n158: Stockholder List\n159: 23\n160: Questions and Additional Information\n161: 23\n162: PROPOSALS SUBMITTED TO MAC-GRAY STOCKHOLDERS\n163: 24\n164: The Merger Agreement Proposal\n165: 24\n166: The \"Golden Parachute\" Proposal\n167: 24\n168: The Adjournment Proposal\n169: 25\n170: THE COMPANIES\n171: 26\n172: THE MERGER\n173: 27\n174: Background of the Merger\n175: 27\n176: Reasons for the Merger and Recommendation of our Board of Directors\n177: 42\n178: Opinion of Mac-Gray's Financial Advisor\n179: 45\n180: Projected Financial Information\n181: 52\n182: Interests of Mac-Gray's Directors and Executive Officers in the Merger\n183: 54\n184: Financing of the Merger\n185: 58\n186: THE MERGER AGREEMENT\n187: 60\n188: The Merger\n189: 60\n190: The Merger Consideration and the Conversion of Capital Stock\n191: 60\n192: Mac-Gray Equity-Based Awards\n193: 61\n194: Mac-Gray Employee Stock Purchase Plan\n195: 61\n196: Payment Procedures\n197: 61\n198: Mac-Gray Representations and Warranties\n199: 62\n200: Conduct of Mac-Gray's Business During the Pendency of the Merger\n201: 65\n202: Mac-Gray Stockholders Meeting\n203: 68\n204: Non-Solicitation; Competing Acquisition Proposals\n205: 69\n206: Mac-Gray Board Recommendation\n207: 70\n208: Mac-Gray Employee Compensation and Benefits\n209: 73\n210: Other Covenants and Agreements\n211: 74\n212: Financing Cooperation\n213: 75\n214: Reasonable Best Efforts\n215: 75\n216: Conditions to the Merger\n217: 77\n218: Termination of the Merger Agreement\n219: 78\n220: Termination Fees and Expenses\n221: 79\n222: Buyer Entity Guarantees\n223: 81\n224: Governing Law\n225: 81\n226: THE VOTING AGREEMENTS\n227: 82\n228: MATERIAL U.S. FEDERAL INCOME TAX CONSIDERATIONS WITH RESPECT TO THE MERGER\n229: 82\n230: REGULATORY MATTERS\n231: 85\n232: LITIGATION RELATED TO THE MERGER\n233: 85\n234: APPRAISAL RIGHTS\n235: 85\n236: CURRENT MARKET PRICE OF COMMON STOCK\n237: 89\n238: SECURITY OWNERSHIP OF MANAGEMENT AND CERTAIN BENEFICIAL OWNERS\n239: 91\n240: FUTURE STOCKHOLDER PROPOSALS\n241: 95\n242: WHERE YOU CAN FIND MORE INFORMATION\n243: 95\n244: MULTIPLE STOCKHOLDERS SHARING ONE ADDRESS\n245: 96\n246: \n247: <<<PAGE folio=blank>>>\n248: \n249: Table of Contents\n250: SPECIAL NOTE REGARDING FORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS\n251: This proxy statement and the documents to which we refer you in this proxy statement contain forward-looking statements within the\n252: meaning of Section 27A of the Securities Act of 1933, as amended, which we refer to as the Securities Act, and Section 21E of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended, which we\n253: refer to as the Exchange Act, including statements regarding the proposed transaction, the anticipated results of the proposed transaction and the timing of the proposed transaction. Mac-Gray intends\n254: such forward-looking statements to be covered by the Safe Harbor provisions for forward-looking statements contained in the Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995, and is including this\n255: statement for purposes of complying with these Safe Harbor provisions.\n256: These\n257: forward-looking statements contain projections of our future results of operations or financial position or state other forward-looking information. In some cases you can identify\n258: these statements by forward-looking words such as \"anticipate,\" \"believe,\" \"could,\" \"estimate,\" \"expect,\" \"intend,\" \"may,\" \"plan,\" \"predict,\" \"should,\" \"target,\" \"will\" and \"would,\" or similar words.\n259: You should not rely on forward-looking statements because they involve known and unknown risks, uncertainties, and other factors, some of which are beyond our control. These risks, uncertainties, and\n260: other factors may cause our actual results, performance or achievements to differ materially from the anticipated future results,\n261: performance or achievements expressed or implied by the forward-looking statements. Some of the factors that might cause these differences are as\n262: follows:\n263: •\n264: the possibility that any of the closing conditions to the consummation of the merger will not be satisfied and the merger\n265: will not be completed;\n266: •\n267: the possibility that Mac-Gray stockholders will not adopt the merger agreement under applicable law and the merger\n268: agreement;\n269: •\n270: the inability to obtain regulatory approvals required for the merger or the imposition of certain regulatory conditions on\n271: the Buyer Entities;\n272: •\n273: the occurrence of any event, change or other circumstance that could give rise to the termination of the merger agreement;\n274: •\n275: the impact of the announcement of the merger on Mac-Gray's operating results and relationships with its employees,\n276: partners, suppliers and customers;\n277: •\n278: the impact of the pending merger on Mac-Gray's strategic plans and operations and Mac-Gray's ability to respond\n279: effectively to competitive pressures, industry developments and future opportunities; and\n280: •\n281: other risks detailed in Mac-Gray's filings with the Securities and Exchange Commission, or SEC, including Mac-Gray's\n282: Annual Report on Form 10-K for the year ended December 31, 2012 and in other reports filed with the SEC. See \"Where You Can Find More Information\" on page 94 of this proxy\n283: statement.\n284: You\n285: should not place undue reliance on forward-looking statements. We cannot guarantee any future results, levels of activity, performance or achievements. The statements made in this\n286: proxy statement are based on the information available to us as of the date of this proxy statement, and you should not assume that the statements made in this proxy statement remain accurate as of\n287: any future date. Moreover, except as required by law, we assume no obligation to update forward-looking statements or update the reasons actual results could differ materially from those anticipated\n288: in forward-looking statements. All forward-looking statements in this document are qualified in their entirety by this cautionary statement.\n289: 1\n290: \n291: <<<PAGE folio=1>>>\n292: \n293: Table of Contents\n294: SUMMARY TERM SHEET\n295: The following summary highlights information in this proxy statement and may not contain all the information\n296: that is important to you. Accordingly, we encourage you to read carefully this entire proxy statement, its annexes and the documents referred to in this proxy statement. Each item in this summary\n297: includes a page reference directing you to a more complete description of the item in this proxy statement.\n298: In this proxy statement, the terms \"we,\" \"us,\" \"our company,\" and \"Mac-Gray\" refer to Mac-Gray Corporation, the term \"Parent\" refers to Spin Holdco Inc.,\n299: the term \"Merger Subsidiary\" refers to CSC Fenway, Inc., the term \"Holdings\" refers to CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc., the term \"CSC\" refers to CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. the term\n300: \"Buyer Entity\" refers to any of Parent, Holdings or CSC, as applicable, the term Pamplona refers to Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. and the term \"merger agreement\" refers to the Agreement\n301: and Plan of Merger, dated as of October 14, 2013, by and among Mac-Gray, Parent, Merger Subsidiary, Holdings and CSC, as it may be amended from time to time.\n302: The Companies (Page 26)\n303: Mac-Gray Corporation\n304: , founded in 1927, is the second largest laundry facilities\n305: management contractor in the United States. Through our portfolio of card- and\n306: coin-operated laundry equipment located in laundry facilities across the country, we provide laundry convenience to residents of multi-unit housing such as apartment buildings, condominiums, colleges\n307: and university residence halls, public housing complexes, and hotels and motels. Based on our ongoing survey of colleges and universities, we believe that we are the largest provider of such services\n308: to the college and university market in the United States. We manage laundry rooms in 44 states and the District of Columbia. We also sell and service commercial laundry equipment to retail\n309: laundromats and other customers through our product sales division.\n310: Mac-Gray\n311: Corporation\n312: 404 Wyman Street, Suite 400\n313: Waltham, Massachusetts 02451\n314: (781) 487-7600\n315: CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.,\n316: with over one million machines in service, is the leading provider of multi-family housing and commercial\n317: laundry solutions as well as the industry leader in air vending services at convenience stores and gas stations. CSC's family of businesses includes: Coinmach Corp., ASI Campus Laundry Solutions, SDI\n318: Laundry Solutions, Sparkle Solutions Corp., Appliance Warehouse of America, AIR-serv, AirValet and Super Laundry. CSC has a workforce of over 2,250 dedicated professionals throughout the United\n319: States, Canada and Europe.\n320: CSC\n321: ServiceWorks, Inc.\n322: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n323: Plainview, New York 11803\n324: (516) 349-8555\n325: CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.\n326: is a Delaware corporation and the sole stockholder of CSC.\n327: CSC\n328: ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.\n329: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n330: Plainview, New York 11803\n331: (516) 349-8555\n332: 2\n333: \n334: <<<PAGE folio=2>>>\n335: \n336: Table of Contents\n337: Spin Holdco Inc.\n338: is a Delaware corporation and a wholly-owned subsidiary of CSC.\n339: Spin\n340: Holdco Inc.\n341: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n342: Plainview, New York 11803\n343: (516) 349-8555\n344: CSC Fenway, Inc.\n345: is a Delaware corporation and a wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent.\n346: CSC\n347: Fenway, Inc.\n348: 303 Sunnyside Boulevard #70\n349: Plainview, New York 11803\n350: (516) 349-8555\n351: The Special Meeting (Page 20)\n352: Date, Time and Place.\n353: The special meeting will be held on Wednesday, January 8, 2014 at 10:00 a.m., local time, at the\n354: Goodwin Procter\n355: LLP\n356: Conference Center, Second Floor, Exchange Place, 53 State Street, Boston, Massachusetts 02109.\n357: Purpose.\n358: At the special meeting, you will be asked to consider and vote upon (1) a proposal to adopt the merger agreement,\n359: (2) an\n360: advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable to the named executive officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant\n361: to the terms of the merger agreement and pre-existing severance arrangements, (3) a proposal to approve one or more adjournments or postponements of the special meeting, if necessary, to\n362: solicit additional proxies if Mac-Gray has not obtained sufficient affirmative stockholder votes to adopt the merger agreement and (4) such other business as may properly come before the\n363: special meeting or any adjournments or postponements of the special meeting. We are currently not aware of any other business to come before the special meeting.\n364: Record Date and Quorum.\n365: You are entitled to vote at the special meeting if you owned shares of Mac-Gray common stock at the\n366: close of business on\n367: November 27, 2013, the record date for the special meeting. You will have one vote for each share of Mac-Gray common stock that you owned on the record date. As of November 27, 2013,\n368: there were 14,758,306 shares of Mac-Gray common stock issued and outstanding and entitled to vote. A majority of Mac-Gray common stock issued, outstanding and entitled to vote at the special meeting,\n369: present in person or represented by proxy, constitutes a quorum for the purpose of the special meeting.\n370: Voting and Proxies.\n371: Any stockholder of record entitled to vote at the special meeting may submit a proxy by telephone, via the\n372: Internet, by returning\n373: the enclosed proxy card by mail, or by voting in person at the special meeting. If you intend to submit your proxy by telephone or via the Internet, you must do so no later than the date and time\n374: indicated on the applicable proxy card(s). If you intend to vote by returning the enclosed proxy card by mail, please do so as soon as possible to ensure your vote is received in advance of the\n375: special meeting. Even if you plan to attend the special meeting, if on the record date you held shares of Mac-Gray common stock in your own name as the stockholder of record, please vote your shares\n376: by completing, signing, dating and returning the enclosed proxy card or by using the telephone number printed on your proxy card or by using the Internet voting instructions printed on your proxy\n377: card.\n378: If\n379: you give your proxy, but do not indicate how you wish to vote, your shares will be voted \"\n380: FOR\n381: \" the proposal to adopt the merger\n382: agreement, \"\n383: FOR\n384: \" the proposal to approve, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, the \"golden parachute\" compensation payable or that could become payable\n385: to the named executive officers of Mac-Gray in connection with the merger pursuant to the terms of the merger agreement and pre-existing severance arrangements and\n386: \"\n387: FOR\n388: \" the adjournment proposal.\n389: 3\n390: \n391: <<<PAGE folio=3>>>\n392: \n393: Table of Contents\n394: If\n395: your shares of Mac-Gray common stock are held in \"street name,\" you should instruct your brokerage firm, bank, trust or other nominee on how to vote such shares of common stock using\n396: the instructions provided by your broker or nominee. If your shares of Mac-Gray common stock are held in \"street name,\" you must obtain a legal proxy from such nominee in order to vote in person at\n397: the special meeting. If you fail to provide your nominee with instructions on how to vote your shares of Mac-Gray common stock, your nominee will not be able to vote such shares at the special\n398: meeting.\n399: Vote Required.\n400: The adoption of the merger agreement requires the affirmative vote of a majority of the outstanding shares of\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 401]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt\", \"limit\": 400}"},"time":{"start":1789824283200,"end":1789824283336}}}}
