{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824325018,"sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9d7d1b9001PdrJgAKT5tWaDj","sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","messageID":"msg_0b9d7c98a001MqKAqHzPyQTekF","type":"tool","id":"call_00_XIhjcVvVMRw59B19il6j2475","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /home/uctpiaj/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\nhtml = open('raw_filing/mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm', encoding='utf-8', errors='replace').read()\nmarkers = [m for m in re.finditer(r'<!--\\s*ZEQ\\.=\\d+,SEQ=\\d+,.*?-->', html)]\n# get component boundaries\nstarts = [0] + [m.end() for m in markers]\n# component index where folio='14' and '15' occur\nfor idx, m in enumerate(markers):\n    fol = re.search(r\"FOLIO='([^']*)'\", m.group(0)).group(1)\n    if fol in ('14','15','13'):\n        comp = idx  # marker ends component idx\n        s = starts[idx-1] if idx>0 else 0\n        e = m.start()\n        body = html[s:e]\n        text = re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', ' ', body)\n        text = re.sub(r'\\s+', ' ', text)\n        print(\"=== folio\", fol, \"len\", len(body), \"text len\", len(text))\n        print(text[:800])\n        print()\nEOF"},"output":"=== folio 13 len 10958 text len 6910\n Table of Contents Mac-Gray Equity-Based Awards (Page 54) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cashed Out Equity Awards. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Each Mac-Gray stock option, whether or not vested and exercisable, that is outstanding and unexercised immediately prior to the effective time of the merger will be automatically converted into the right to receive an amount in cash (less applicable tax withholdings) equal to the product obtained by multiplying (1)&nbsp;the excess, if any, of $21.25 over the per share exercise price of such stock option by (2)&nbsp;the aggregate number of shares of Mac-Gray common stock that were issuable upon exercise or settlement of such stock option immediately prior to the effective time of the merger. From and after the effective time of the merge\n\n=== folio 14 len 12739 text len 7250\n Table of Contents QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGER AND THE SPECIAL MEETING &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The following questions and answers address briefly some questions you may have regarding the merger agreement, the merger and the special meeting. These questions and answers may not address all questions that may be important to you as a holder of shares of Mac-Gray common stock. For important additional information, please refer to the more detailed discussion contained elsewhere in this proxy statement, the annexes to this proxy statement and the documents referred to in this proxy statement, including the merger agreement. Q: What is the effect of the merger? A: Mac-Gray, the Buyer Entities and Merger Subsidiary have entered into the merger agreement. Subj\n\n=== folio 15 len 12200 text len 7709\n Table of Contents Q: When do you expect the merger to be completed? A: We currently expect the merger to be completed in January 2014. However, the merger is subject to various closing conditions, including Mac-Gray stockholder and regulatory approvals, and it is possible that the failure to timely meet these closing conditions or other factors outside of our control could delay the completion of the merger. We cannot assure you that we will complete the merger on this schedule or at all. Q: Why am I receiving this proxy statement? A: You are receiving this proxy statement because you were a stockholder of Mac-Gray as of November&nbsp;27, 2013, the record date for the special meeting. The adoption of the merger agreement requires the affirmative vote of a majority of the outstanding share\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== folio 13 len 10958 text len 6910\n Table of Contents Mac-Gray Equity-Based Awards (Page 54) &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Cashed Out Equity Awards. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Each Mac-Gray stock option, whether or not vested and exercisable, that is outstanding and unexercised immediately prior to the effective time of the merger will be automatically converted into the right to receive an amount in cash (less applicable tax withholdings) equal to the product obtained by multiplying (1)&nbsp;the excess, if any, of $21.25 over the per share exercise price of such stock option by (2)&nbsp;the aggregate number of shares of Mac-Gray common stock that were issuable upon exercise or settlement of such stock option immediately prior to the effective time of the merger. From and after the effective time of the merge\n\n=== folio 14 len 12739 text len 7250\n Table of Contents QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGER AND THE SPECIAL MEETING &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; The following questions and answers address briefly some questions you may have regarding the merger agreement, the merger and the special meeting. These questions and answers may not address all questions that may be important to you as a holder of shares of Mac-Gray common stock. For important additional information, please refer to the more detailed discussion contained elsewhere in this proxy statement, the annexes to this proxy statement and the documents referred to in this proxy statement, including the merger agreement. Q: What is the effect of the merger? A: Mac-Gray, the Buyer Entities and Merger Subsidiary have entered into the merger agreement. Subj\n\n=== folio 15 len 12200 text len 7709\n Table of Contents Q: When do you expect the merger to be completed? A: We currently expect the merger to be completed in January 2014. However, the merger is subject to various closing conditions, including Mac-Gray stockholder and regulatory approvals, and it is possible that the failure to timely meet these closing conditions or other factors outside of our control could delay the completion of the merger. We cannot assure you that we will complete the merger on this schedule or at all. Q: Why am I receiving this proxy statement? A: You are receiving this proxy statement because you were a stockholder of Mac-Gray as of November&nbsp;27, 2013, the record date for the special meeting. The adoption of the merger agreement requires the affirmative vote of a majority of the outstanding share\n\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/uctpiaj/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport re\\nhtml = open('raw_filing/mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm', encoding='utf-8', errors='replace').read()\\nmarkers = [m for m in re.finditer(r'<!--\\\\s*ZEQ\\\\.=\\\\d+,SEQ=\\\\d+,.*?-->', html)]\\n# get component boundaries\\nstarts = [0] + [m.end() for m in markers]\\n# component index where folio='14' and '15' occur\\nfor idx, m in enumerate(markers):\\n    fol = re.search(r\\\"FOLIO='([^']*)'\\\", m.group(0)).group(1)\\n    if fol in ('14','15','13'):\\n        comp = idx  # marker ends component idx\\n        s = starts[idx-1] if idx>0 else 0\\n        e = m.start()\\n        body = html[s:e]\\n        text = re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', ' ', body)\\n        text = re.sub(r'\\\\s+', ' ', text)\\n        print(\\\"=== folio\\\", fol, \\\"len\\\", len(body), \\\"text len\\\", len(text))\\n        print(text[:800])\\n        print()\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824324025,"end":1789824325018}}}}
