{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824356872,"sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9d85156001HFBWqt3uQafoyn","sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","messageID":"msg_0b9d848e7001AmtqZjXOruSMaW","type":"tool","id":"call_00_4eycQDZzlQGhyes42vqQ8794","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":240,"offset":2474,"path":"/tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt"},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt, lines 2474-2713\n2474: <<<PAGE 58 folio=52>>>\n2475: Table of Contents\n2476: customers\n2477: or manage funds that invest, make or hold long or short positions, finance positions or trade or otherwise effect transactions in the equity, debt or other securities or financial\n2478: instruments (including derivatives, bank loans or other obligations) of Mac-Gray, the Buyer Entities and certain of their respective affiliates.\n2479: BofA\n2480: Merrill Lynch and its affiliates in the past have provided, currently are providing, and in the future may provide, investment banking, commercial banking and other financial\n2481: services to Mac-Gray and have received or in the future may receive compensation for the rendering of these services, including in the past two years (i) having acted or acting as\n2482: administrative agent, collateral agent, sole lead arranger, and sole bookrunner for, and a lender (including a letter of credit lender and a swing line lender) under, Mac-Gray's amended and restated\n2483: senior secured credit agreement and (ii) having provided or providing certain treasury and trade management services and products to Mac-Gray. From January 1, 2011 through\n2484: September 30, 2013, BofA Merrill Lynch and its affiliates derived aggregate revenues of approximately $3.8 million from Mac-Gray and its affiliates for commercial, corporate or\n2485: investment banking services unrelated to the merger.\n2486: In\n2487: addition, BofA Merrill Lynch and its affiliates in the past have provided, currently are providing, and in the future may provide, investment banking, commercial banking and other\n2488: financial services to Pamplona and certain of its affiliates and portfolio companies, including the Buyer Entities, and have received or in the future may receive compensation for the rendering of\n2489: these services, including in the past two years (i) having acted or acting as a lender under various term loans and other credit facilities of certain of Pamplona's affiliates and portfolio\n2490: companies, including certain of the Buyer Entities, (ii) having acted as manager or underwriter for one or more debt and/or equity offerings of certain of Pamplona's affiliates and portfolio\n2491: companies, and (iii) having provided or providing certain treasury and trade management services and products to certain of Pamplona's affiliates and portfolio companies, including certain of\n2492: the Buyer Entities. From January 1, 2011 through September 30, 2013, BofA Merrill Lynch and its affiliates derived aggregate revenues of approximately $2.2 million from the Buyer\n2493: Entities, Pamplona and certain of its affiliates and portfolio companies identified to BofA Merrill Lynch by the Buyer Entities for commercial, corporate or investment banking services unrelated to\n2494: the merger.\n2495: Projected Financial Information\n2496: Our senior management does not as a matter of course make public projections as to future performance or earnings beyond the current\n2497: fiscal year and generally does not make public projections for extended periods due to the unpredictability of the underlying assumptions and estimates. However, in connection with the exploration of\n2498: strategic alternatives as described in this proxy statement, management prepared a set of financial projections (the Projections) for the remainder of 2013 and calendar years 2014 through 2018, and\n2499: these Projections were provided to the Special Committee and BofA Merrill Lynch. We have included below these Projections concerning our total revenue, EBITDA, GAAP earnings per share and capital\n2500: expenditures. The first set of Projections below— Management Financial Projections without Acquisitions —assumes that Mac-Gray\n2501: makes no acquisitions of facilities management businesses, which we refer to as the Without Acquisitions Case. The second set of Projections below— Management\n2502: Financial Projections with Acquisitions —assumes that Mac-Gray acquires, each year commencing in 2013, laundry facilities management businesses operating a total of\n2503: between 10,000 and 26,000 machines, at certain prices and within Mac-Gray's existing geographies, which we refer to as the With Acquisitions Case.\n2504: These\n2505: Projections were developed from historical financial statements and did not give effect to any changes or expenses as a result of the merger or any other effects of the merger. The\n2506: Projections included below were prepared solely for internal use and were not prepared with a view toward public disclosure or compliance with published guidelines of the American Institute of\n2507: Certified Public Accountants for preparation and presentation of prospective financial information or GAAP. The inclusion of this information should not be regarded as an indication that the Board,\n2508: BofA Merrill\n2509: 52\n2510: \n2511: <<<PAGE 59 folio=53>>>\n2512: Table of Contents\n2513: Lynch\n2514: or any other recipient of this information considered, or now considers, it to be a reliable prediction of future results. Our independent registered certified public accounting firm,\n2515: McGladrey LLP, has neither examined nor compiled this prospective financial information and, accordingly, McGladrey LLP does not express an opinion or any other form of assurance with\n2516: respect to this information. None of us, BofA Merrill Lynch, the Buyer Entities, any of our or their respective affiliates or any other person assumes any responsibility for the validity,\n2517: reasonableness, accuracy or completeness of the Projections described below.\n2518: Furthermore,\n2519: while presented with numerical specificity, the Projections necessarily are based on numerous assumptions, many of which are beyond our control and difficult to predict,\n2520: including with respect to industry performance, competitive factors, industry consolidation, general business, economic, regulatory, market and financial conditions, as well as matters specific to our\n2521: business, such as lease renewal rates, vend prices and vacancy rates, which assumptions may not prove to have been, or may no longer be, accurate. The Projections do not take into account any\n2522: circumstances or events occurring after the date they were prepared, including the October 15, 2013 announcement of the merger agreement. In addition, the Projections do not take into account\n2523: the effect of any failure of the merger to occur and should not be viewed as accurate or continuing in that context or otherwise.\n2524: The\n2525: Projections were prepared in June 2013 in the context of the business, economic, regulatory, market and financial conditions that existed at that time, and have not been updated to\n2526: reflect revised prospects for our business, changes in general business, economic, regulatory, market and financial conditions, or any other transaction or event that has occurred or that may occur\n2527: and that was not anticipated at the time the projections were prepared. The Projections are not necessarily indicative of future performance, which may be significantly more favorable or less\n2528: favorable than as set forth below. The Projections cover multiple years, and such information by its nature becomes less reliable with each successive year. They should not be utilized as public\n2529: guidance and will not be provided in the ordinary course of our business in the future.\n2530: For\n2531: the foregoing and other reasons, readers of this proxy statement are cautioned that the inclusion of the Projections in this proxy statement should not be regarded as a\n2532: representation or guarantee that the targets will be achieved and that they should not rely on the Projections. The Projections constitute forward-looking statements and are subject to risks and\n2533: uncertainties that could cause actual results to differ materially from the results projected in such projections, including, but not limited, to general economic conditions, changes in multi-housing\n2534: vacancy rates and our ability to renew long-term customer contracts. See also the section entitled \"Special Note Regarding Forward-Looking Statements\" in this proxy statement.\n2535: Management Financial Projections without Acquisitions\n2536: ($ in millions, except earnings per share)\n2537: 2013\n2538: Forecast\n2539: 2014\n2540: Projection\n2541: 2015\n2542: Projection\n2543: 2016\n2544: Projection\n2545: 2017\n2546: Projection\n2547: 2018\n2548: Projection\n2549: Total Revenue\n2550: $\n2551: 333\n2552: $\n2553: 348\n2554: $\n2555: 364\n2556: $\n2557: 382\n2558: $\n2559: 401\n2560: $\n2561: 423\n2562: EBITDA(1)\n2563: $\n2564: 71\n2565: $\n2566: 79\n2567: $\n2568: 85\n2569: $\n2570: 92\n2571: $\n2572: 99\n2573: $\n2574: 107\n2575: GAAP Earnings per share(2)\n2576: $\n2577: 0.80\n2578: $\n2579: 1.20\n2580: $\n2581: 1.41\n2582: $\n2583: 1.57\n2584: $\n2585: 1.78\n2586: $\n2587: 2.02\n2588: Capital Expenditures(3)\n2589: $\n2590: 42\n2591: $\n2592: 43\n2593: $\n2594: 45\n2595: $\n2596: 44\n2597: $\n2598: 46\n2599: $\n2600: 50\n2601: (1)\n2602: Defined\n2603: as GAAP operating income plus depreciation, amortization and non-recurring items and is post stock-based compensation.\n2604: (2)\n2605: GAAP\n2606: earnings per share adjusted for non-recurring items.\n2607: (3)\n2608: Capital\n2609: expenditures include incentive payments.\n2610: 53\n2611: \n2612: <<<PAGE 60 folio=54>>>\n2613: Table of Contents\n2614: Management Financial Projections with Acquisitions\n2615: ($ in millions, except earnings per share)\n2616: 2013\n2617: Forecast\n2618: 2014\n2619: Projection\n2620: 2015\n2621: Projection\n2622: 2016\n2623: Projection\n2624: 2017\n2625: Projection\n2626: 2018\n2627: Projection\n2628: Total Revenue\n2629: $\n2630: 344\n2631: $\n2632: 381\n2633: $\n2634: 413\n2635: $\n2636: 440\n2637: $\n2638: 470\n2639: $\n2640: 501\n2641: EBITDA(1)\n2642: $\n2643: 75\n2644: $\n2645: 87\n2646: $\n2647: 99\n2648: $\n2649: 109\n2650: $\n2651: 122\n2652: $\n2653: 134\n2654: GAAP Earnings per share(2)\n2655: $\n2656: 0.90\n2657: $\n2658: 1.29\n2659: $\n2660: 1.62\n2661: $\n2662: 1.84\n2663: $\n2664: 2.25\n2665: $\n2666: 2.59\n2667: Capital Expenditures(3)\n2668: $\n2669: 59\n2670: $\n2671: 85\n2672: $\n2673: 73\n2674: $\n2675: 60\n2676: $\n2677: 62\n2678: $\n2679: 66\n2680: (1)\n2681: Defined\n2682: as GAAP operating income plus depreciation, amortization and non-recurring items and is post stock-based compensation.\n2683: (2)\n2684: GAAP\n2685: earnings per share adjusted for non-recurring items.\n2686: (3)\n2687: Capital\n2688: expenditures include incentive payments.\n2689: Interests of Mac-Gray's Directors and Executive Officers in the Merger\n2690: In considering the recommendation of our Board of Directors with respect to the merger agreement and the merger, you should be aware\n2691: that Mac Gray's executive officers and directors have economic interests in the merger that are different from, or in addition to,\n2692: those of Mac-Gray stockholders generally. These interests may create potential conflicts of interest. Our Board of Directors was aware of and considered these interests, among other matters, in\n2693: reaching its decision to approve, and declare advisable, the merger agreement and the merger. The material interests are summarized below.\n2694: Equity-Based Awards\n2695: The following table identifies for each of our executive officers and directors the number of shares subject to his or her outstanding\n2696: equity awards (stock options and restricted stock units), the weighted average exercise price, if any, of all equity awards and the value of such equity awards in the merger. All equity awards,\n2697: including those held by our executive officers and directors, will be cashed out in connection with the merger. The following table assumes that the closing of the merger occurs on March 1,\n2698: 2014 and that no options are exercised, no restricted stock units are settled or forfeited and\n2699: 54\n2700: \n2701: <<<PAGE 61 folio=55>>>\n2702: Table of Contents\n2703: no\n2704: dividends are paid with respect to the common stock between the date hereof and the closing of the merger.\n2705: Vested Options\n2706: Unvested Options\n2707: Restricted Stock\n2708: Units\n2709: Aggregate\n2710: Number of\n2711: Shares\n2712: Subject to\n2713: Outstanding\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2714]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt, lines 2474-2713\n2474: <<<PAGE 58 folio=52>>>\n2475: Table of Contents\n2476: customers\n2477: or manage funds that invest, make or hold long or short positions, finance positions or trade or otherwise effect transactions in the equity, debt or other securities or financial\n2478: instruments (including derivatives, bank loans or other obligations) of Mac-Gray, the Buyer Entities and certain of their respective affiliates.\n2479: BofA\n2480: Merrill Lynch and its affiliates in the past have provided, currently are providing, and in the future may provide, investment banking, commercial banking and other financial\n2481: services to Mac-Gray and have received or in the future may receive compensation for the rendering of these services, including in the past two years (i) having acted or acting as\n2482: administrative agent, collateral agent, sole lead arranger, and sole bookrunner for, and a lender (including a letter of credit lender and a swing line lender) under, Mac-Gray's amended and restated\n2483: senior secured credit agreement and (ii) having provided or providing certain treasury and trade management services and products to Mac-Gray. From January 1, 2011 through\n2484: September 30, 2013, BofA Merrill Lynch and its affiliates derived aggregate revenues of approximately $3.8 million from Mac-Gray and its affiliates for commercial, corporate or\n2485: investment banking services unrelated to the merger.\n2486: In\n2487: addition, BofA Merrill Lynch and its affiliates in the past have provided, currently are providing, and in the future may provide, investment banking, commercial banking and other\n2488: financial services to Pamplona and certain of its affiliates and portfolio companies, including the Buyer Entities, and have received or in the future may receive compensation for the rendering of\n2489: these services, including in the past two years (i) having acted or acting as a lender under various term loans and other credit facilities of certain of Pamplona's affiliates and portfolio\n2490: companies, including certain of the Buyer Entities, (ii) having acted as manager or underwriter for one or more debt and/or equity offerings of certain of Pamplona's affiliates and portfolio\n2491: companies, and (iii) having provided or providing certain treasury and trade management services and products to certain of Pamplona's affiliates and portfolio companies, including certain of\n2492: the Buyer Entities. From January 1, 2011 through September 30, 2013, BofA Merrill Lynch and its affiliates derived aggregate revenues of approximately $2.2 million from the Buyer\n2493: Entities, Pamplona and certain of its affiliates and portfolio companies identified to BofA Merrill Lynch by the Buyer Entities for commercial, corporate or investment banking services unrelated to\n2494: the merger.\n2495: Projected Financial Information\n2496: Our senior management does not as a matter of course make public projections as to future performance or earnings beyond the current\n2497: fiscal year and generally does not make public projections for extended periods due to the unpredictability of the underlying assumptions and estimates. However, in connection with the exploration of\n2498: strategic alternatives as described in this proxy statement, management prepared a set of financial projections (the Projections) for the remainder of 2013 and calendar years 2014 through 2018, and\n2499: these Projections were provided to the Special Committee and BofA Merrill Lynch. We have included below these Projections concerning our total revenue, EBITDA, GAAP earnings per share and capital\n2500: expenditures. The first set of Projections below— Management Financial Projections without Acquisitions —assumes that Mac-Gray\n2501: makes no acquisitions of facilities management businesses, which we refer to as the Without Acquisitions Case. The second set of Projections below— Management\n2502: Financial Projections with Acquisitions —assumes that Mac-Gray acquires, each year commencing in 2013, laundry facilities management businesses operating a total of\n2503: between 10,000 and 26,000 machines, at certain prices and within Mac-Gray's existing geographies, which we refer to as the With Acquisitions Case.\n2504: These\n2505: Projections were developed from historical financial statements and did not give effect to any changes or expenses as a result of the merger or any other effects of the merger. The\n2506: Projections included below were prepared solely for internal use and were not prepared with a view toward public disclosure or compliance with published guidelines of the American Institute of\n2507: Certified Public Accountants for preparation and presentation of prospective financial information or GAAP. The inclusion of this information should not be regarded as an indication that the Board,\n2508: BofA Merrill\n2509: 52\n2510: \n2511: <<<PAGE 59 folio=53>>>\n2512: Table of Contents\n2513: Lynch\n2514: or any other recipient of this information considered, or now considers, it to be a reliable prediction of future results. Our independent registered certified public accounting firm,\n2515: McGladrey LLP, has neither examined nor compiled this prospective financial information and, accordingly, McGladrey LLP does not express an opinion or any other form of assurance with\n2516: respect to this information. None of us, BofA Merrill Lynch, the Buyer Entities, any of our or their respective affiliates or any other person assumes any responsibility for the validity,\n2517: reasonableness, accuracy or completeness of the Projections described below.\n2518: Furthermore,\n2519: while presented with numerical specificity, the Projections necessarily are based on numerous assumptions, many of which are beyond our control and difficult to predict,\n2520: including with respect to industry performance, competitive factors, industry consolidation, general business, economic, regulatory, market and financial conditions, as well as matters specific to our\n2521: business, such as lease renewal rates, vend prices and vacancy rates, which assumptions may not prove to have been, or may no longer be, accurate. The Projections do not take into account any\n2522: circumstances or events occurring after the date they were prepared, including the October 15, 2013 announcement of the merger agreement. In addition, the Projections do not take into account\n2523: the effect of any failure of the merger to occur and should not be viewed as accurate or continuing in that context or otherwise.\n2524: The\n2525: Projections were prepared in June 2013 in the context of the business, economic, regulatory, market and financial conditions that existed at that time, and have not been updated to\n2526: reflect revised prospects for our business, changes in general business, economic, regulatory, market and financial conditions, or any other transaction or event that has occurred or that may occur\n2527: and that was not anticipated at the time the projections were prepared. The Projections are not necessarily indicative of future performance, which may be significantly more favorable or less\n2528: favorable than as set forth below. The Projections cover multiple years, and such information by its nature becomes less reliable with each successive year. They should not be utilized as public\n2529: guidance and will not be provided in the ordinary course of our business in the future.\n2530: For\n2531: the foregoing and other reasons, readers of this proxy statement are cautioned that the inclusion of the Projections in this proxy statement should not be regarded as a\n2532: representation or guarantee that the targets will be achieved and that they should not rely on the Projections. The Projections constitute forward-looking statements and are subject to risks and\n2533: uncertainties that could cause actual results to differ materially from the results projected in such projections, including, but not limited, to general economic conditions, changes in multi-housing\n2534: vacancy rates and our ability to renew long-term customer contracts. See also the section entitled \"Special Note Regarding Forward-Looking Statements\" in this proxy statement.\n2535: Management Financial Projections without Acquisitions\n2536: ($ in millions, except earnings per share)\n2537: 2013\n2538: Forecast\n2539: 2014\n2540: Projection\n2541: 2015\n2542: Projection\n2543: 2016\n2544: Projection\n2545: 2017\n2546: Projection\n2547: 2018\n2548: Projection\n2549: Total Revenue\n2550: $\n2551: 333\n2552: $\n2553: 348\n2554: $\n2555: 364\n2556: $\n2557: 382\n2558: $\n2559: 401\n2560: $\n2561: 423\n2562: EBITDA(1)\n2563: $\n2564: 71\n2565: $\n2566: 79\n2567: $\n2568: 85\n2569: $\n2570: 92\n2571: $\n2572: 99\n2573: $\n2574: 107\n2575: GAAP Earnings per share(2)\n2576: $\n2577: 0.80\n2578: $\n2579: 1.20\n2580: $\n2581: 1.41\n2582: $\n2583: 1.57\n2584: $\n2585: 1.78\n2586: $\n2587: 2.02\n2588: Capital Expenditures(3)\n2589: $\n2590: 42\n2591: $\n2592: 43\n2593: $\n2594: 45\n2595: $\n2596: 44\n2597: $\n2598: 46\n2599: $\n2600: 50\n2601: (1)\n2602: Defined\n2603: as GAAP operating income plus depreciation, amortization and non-recurring items and is post stock-based compensation.\n2604: (2)\n2605: GAAP\n2606: earnings per share adjusted for non-recurring items.\n2607: (3)\n2608: Capital\n2609: expenditures include incentive payments.\n2610: 53\n2611: \n2612: <<<PAGE 60 folio=54>>>\n2613: Table of Contents\n2614: Management Financial Projections with Acquisitions\n2615: ($ in millions, except earnings per share)\n2616: 2013\n2617: Forecast\n2618: 2014\n2619: Projection\n2620: 2015\n2621: Projection\n2622: 2016\n2623: Projection\n2624: 2017\n2625: Projection\n2626: 2018\n2627: Projection\n2628: Total Revenue\n2629: $\n2630: 344\n2631: $\n2632: 381\n2633: $\n2634: 413\n2635: $\n2636: 440\n2637: $\n2638: 470\n2639: $\n2640: 501\n2641: EBITDA(1)\n2642: $\n2643: 75\n2644: $\n2645: 87\n2646: $\n2647: 99\n2648: $\n2649: 109\n2650: $\n2651: 122\n2652: $\n2653: 134\n2654: GAAP Earnings per share(2)\n2655: $\n2656: 0.90\n2657: $\n2658: 1.29\n2659: $\n2660: 1.62\n2661: $\n2662: 1.84\n2663: $\n2664: 2.25\n2665: $\n2666: 2.59\n2667: Capital Expenditures(3)\n2668: $\n2669: 59\n2670: $\n2671: 85\n2672: $\n2673: 73\n2674: $\n2675: 60\n2676: $\n2677: 62\n2678: $\n2679: 66\n2680: (1)\n2681: Defined\n2682: as GAAP operating income plus depreciation, amortization and non-recurring items and is post stock-based compensation.\n2683: (2)\n2684: GAAP\n2685: earnings per share adjusted for non-recurring items.\n2686: (3)\n2687: Capital\n2688: expenditures include incentive payments.\n2689: Interests of Mac-Gray's Directors and Executive Officers in the Merger\n2690: In considering the recommendation of our Board of Directors with respect to the merger agreement and the merger, you should be aware\n2691: that Mac Gray's executive officers and directors have economic interests in the merger that are different from, or in addition to,\n2692: those of Mac-Gray stockholders generally. These interests may create potential conflicts of interest. Our Board of Directors was aware of and considered these interests, among other matters, in\n2693: reaching its decision to approve, and declare advisable, the merger agreement and the merger. The material interests are summarized below.\n2694: Equity-Based Awards\n2695: The following table identifies for each of our executive officers and directors the number of shares subject to his or her outstanding\n2696: equity awards (stock options and restricted stock units), the weighted average exercise price, if any, of all equity awards and the value of such equity awards in the merger. All equity awards,\n2697: including those held by our executive officers and directors, will be cashed out in connection with the merger. The following table assumes that the closing of the merger occurs on March 1,\n2698: 2014 and that no options are exercised, no restricted stock units are settled or forfeited and\n2699: 54\n2700: \n2701: <<<PAGE 61 folio=55>>>\n2702: Table of Contents\n2703: no\n2704: dividends are paid with respect to the common stock between the date hereof and the closing of the merger.\n2705: Vested Options\n2706: Unvested Options\n2707: Restricted Stock\n2708: Units\n2709: Aggregate\n2710: Number of\n2711: Shares\n2712: Subject to\n2713: Outstanding\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 2714]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 240, \"offset\": 2474, \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824356694,"end":1789824356872}}}}
