{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824358999,"sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9d859a4001bGQ1cEklBk22LU","sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","messageID":"msg_0b9d85211001FY0Vofp8GI60Go","type":"tool","id":"call_00_WrWbenxsociNfo0McHiM3622","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":200,"offset":3086,"path":"/tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt"},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt, lines 3086-3285\n3086: <<<PAGE 66 folio=60>>>\n3087: Table of Contents\n3088: THE MERGER AGREEMENT\n3089: The summary of the material provisions of the merger agreement below and elsewhere in this proxy statement is\n3090: qualified in its entirety by reference to the merger agreement, a copy of which is attached to this proxy statement as Annex A and which we incorporate by reference into this document. This\n3091: summary does not purport to be complete and may not contain all of the information about the merger agreement that is important to you. We encourage you to read the merger agreement carefully in its\n3092: entirety.\n3093: The Merger\n3094: The merger agreement provides that, subject to the terms and conditions of the merger agreement and in accordance with Delaware law, at\n3095: the effective time of the merger, Merger Subsidiary will merge with and into Mac-Gray. As a result of the merger, Mac-Gray will be the\n3096: surviving corporation, the separate corporate existence of Merger Subsidiary will cease and Mac-Gray will continue as a wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent. As the surviving corporation, Mac-Gray will\n3097: possess the rights, powers, privileges, immunities and franchises and be subject to all of the obligations, liabilities, restrictions and disabilities of Mac-Gray and Merger Subsidiary, all as\n3098: provided under Delaware law.\n3099: The\n3100: closing of the merger will occur as soon as practicable but in any event within two business days after satisfaction or, to the extent permitted by the terms of the merger agreement,\n3101: waiver of all of the conditions set forth in the merger agreement and described under \"—Conditions to the Merger\" unless another time or date is agreed to in writing by the parties to the\n3102: merger agreement.\n3103: The\n3104: merger will become effective when the certificate of merger has been duly filed with the Secretary of State of the State of Delaware or at such later time and date as agreed to by\n3105: the parties in writing and specified in the certificate of merger. The merger is expected to be completed in the first half of 2014. However, the parties cannot predict the exact timing of the\n3106: completion of the merger or whether the merger will be completed at an earlier or later time, as agreed by the parties, or at all.\n3107: The Merger Consideration and the Conversion of Capital Stock\n3108: Immediately prior to the effective time of the merger, each share of Mac-Gray common stock outstanding immediately prior to the\n3109: effective time of the merger will be canceled and converted into the right to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest, other than:\n3110: •\n3111: shares of Mac-Gray common stock owned by Mac-Gray as treasury stock or shares owned by any Buyer Entity, Merger Subsidiary\n3112: or their wholly owned subsidiaries, which will be canceled, and no payment will be made with respect thereto; and\n3113: •\n3114: shares of Mac-Gray common stock held by a stockholder who has properly exercised, and has not failed to perfect, withdrawn\n3115: or otherwise lost, appraisal rights in accordance with Delaware law.\n3116: The\n3117: price to be paid for each share of Mac-Gray common stock in the merger will be adjusted appropriately to reflect the effect of any change in the outstanding shares of capital stock\n3118: of Mac-Gray, including by reason of any reclassification, recapitalization, stock split (including reverse stock split) or combination, exchange or readjustment of shares, or any stock dividend, that\n3119: occurs prior to the effective time of the merger.\n3120: Each\n3121: share of common stock of Merger Subsidiary outstanding immediately prior to the effective time of the merger will be converted into and become one fully paid, nonassessable share of\n3122: common stock, par value $0.01 per share, of the surviving corporation with the same rights, powers and privileges as the shares so converted and will constitute the only outstanding shares of capital\n3123: stock of the surviving corporation.\n3124: 60\n3125: \n3126: <<<PAGE 67 folio=61>>>\n3127: Table of Contents\n3128: Mac-Gray Equity-Based Awards\n3129: Immediately prior to the effective time of the merger, and without any action on the part of the holders thereof, each Mac-Gray stock\n3130: option, whether or not vested and exercisable, that is outstanding and unexercised immediately prior to the effective time of the merger, will be automatically converted into the right to receive from\n3131: Parent or the surviving corporation immediately after the effective time of the merger an amount in cash equal to the product obtained by multiplying (i) the excess, if any, of $21.25 over the\n3132: per share exercise price of such Mac-Gray stock option, by (ii) the aggregate number of shares of Mac-Gray common stock that were issuable upon exercise or settlement of such Mac-Gray stock\n3133: option immediately prior to the effective time of the merger. If the exercise price per share of any Mac-Gray stock option equals or exceeds $21.25, the amount to be paid for such Mac-Gray stock\n3134: option will be zero.\n3135: Immediately\n3136: prior to the effective time of the merger, and without any action on the part of the holders thereof each outstanding Mac-Gray restricted stock award or restricted stock unit\n3137: under any Mac-Gray stock plans will become fully vested, will not be assumed by Parent or Merger Subsidiary in the merger and will be canceled and extinguished as of the effective time of the merger\n3138: and, in exchange therefor, each former holder of any such restricted stock award or restricted stock unit will have the right to receive from Parent or the surviving corporation an amount in cash\n3139: equal to the product obtained by multiplying (i) the maximum number of shares of Mac-Gray common stock subject to such restricted stock award or restricted stock unit by (ii) the $21.25.\n3140: From and after the effective time of the merger, any Mac-Gray restricted stock award or restricted stock unit will no longer\n3141: represent the right to receive shares of Mac-Gray common stock by the former holder thereof, but will only entitle such holder to the payment described above, if any.\n3142: Mac-Gray Employee Stock Purchase Plan\n3143: As soon as practicable following the date of the merger agreement, but not later than the day immediately prior to the date on which\n3144: the first offering period that is regularly scheduled to commence under the ESPP, after the date of the merger agreement is scheduled to commence, Mac-Gray will take all actions necessary or required\n3145: under the ESPP and applicable law to (1) suspend the ESPP, (2) end the last offering period that commenced period to the date of the merger agreement on the earlier to occur of its\n3146: regularly scheduled end date under the terms of the ESPP or three calendar days prior to the effective date of the merger, and (3) cause the ESPP to terminate as of the effective date of the\n3147: merger such that no further rights will be granted or exercised under the ESPP thereafter.\n3148: Payment Procedures\n3149: Prior to the effective time of the merger, Parent will appoint an exchange agent reasonably acceptable to Mac-Gray for the purpose of\n3150: exchanging for the merger consideration the certificated and uncertificated shares of Mac-Gray common stock. At or prior to the effective time of the merger, Parent will deposit, or cause to be\n3151: deposited, with the exchange agent the aggregate merger consideration to be paid in respect of the certificated and uncertificated shares of Mac-Gray common stock. To the extent such fund diminishes\n3152: for any reason below the level required to make prompt payment of the merger consideration, Parent and the surviving corporation will promptly replace or restore the lost portion of such fund so as to\n3153: ensure that it is, at all times, maintained at a level sufficient to make such payments.\n3154: Each\n3155: holder of shares of Mac-Gray common stock that have been converted into the right to receive the merger consideration will be entitled to receive the merger consideration in respect\n3156: of their shares of Mac-Gray common stock upon (1) surrender to the exchange agent of a certificate, together with a duly completed and validly executed letter of transmittal and such other\n3157: documents as may\n3158: 61\n3159: \n3160: <<<PAGE 68 folio=62>>>\n3161: Table of Contents\n3162: reasonably\n3163: be requested by the exchange agent, or (2) receipt of an \"agent's message\" by the exchange agent (or such other evidence, if any, of transfer as the exchange agent may reasonably\n3164: request) in the case of a book-entry transfer of uncertificated shares of Mac-Gray common stock. Until so surrendered or transferred, each such certificated or uncertificated share will represent\n3165: after the effective time of the merger for all purposes only the right to receive such merger consideration. No interest will be paid or accrued on the cash payable upon the surrender or transfer of\n3166: such certificated or uncertificated share.\n3167: If\n3168: any portion of the merger consideration is to be paid to a person other than the person in whose name the surrendered certificate or the transferred uncertificated share is\n3169: registered, it will be a condition to such payment that (1) either such certificate will be properly endorsed or will otherwise be in proper form for transfer or such uncertificated share will\n3170: be properly transferred and (2) the person requesting such payment will pay to the exchange agent any transfer or other tax required as a result of such payment to a person other than the\n3171: registered holder of such certificate or uncertificated share or establish to the satisfaction of the exchange agent that such tax has been paid or is not payable.\n3172: All\n3173: merger consideration paid upon the surrender of certificated or uncertificated shares in accordance with the terms of the merger agreement will be deemed to have been paid in full\n3174: satisfaction of all rights pertaining to the shares of Mac-Gray common stock formerly represented by such certificated or uncertificated shares. From and after the effective time of the merger, there\n3175: will be no further registration of transfers of shares of Mac-Gray common stock on the stock transfer books of the surviving corporation. If, after the effective time of the merger, certificated or\n3176: uncertificated shares of Mac-Gray common stock are presented to the surviving corporation, they will be canceled and exchanged for the merger consideration in accordance with the procedures described\n3177: in the two paragraphs immediately above.\n3178: Any\n3179: portion of the payment fund deposited with the exchange agent that remains unclaimed by the holders of shares of Company common stock twelve months after the effective time of the\n3180: merger will be delivered to the surviving corporation, upon demand, and any such holder who has not exchanged shares of Mac-Gray common stock for the merger consideration in accordance with the merger\n3181: agreement prior to that time will thereafter look only to Parent or the surviving corporation for payment of the merger consideration, without interest.\n3182: Mac-Gray Representations and Warranties\n3183: The merger agreement contains representations and warranties made by Mac-Gray to Parent and Merger Subsidiary and representations and\n3184: warranties made by Parent and Merger Subsidiary to Mac-Gray. The assertions embodied in those representations and warranties were made for purposes of the merger agreement and are subject to\n3185: qualifications and limitations agreed to by the respective parties in connection with negotiating the terms of the merger agreement, including information contained in confidential disclosure\n3186: schedules that the parties exchanged in connection with signing the merger agreement. Accordingly, investors and security holders should not rely on such representations and warranties as\n3187: characterizations of the actual state of facts or circumstances, since they were only made as of a specific date and are modified in important part by the underlying disclosure schedules. In addition,\n3188: certain representations and warranties may be subject to a contractual standard of materiality different from what might be viewed as material to stockholders, or may have been used for purposes of\n3189: allocating risk between the respective parties rather than establishing matters of fact. Moreover, information concerning the subject matter of such representations and warranties may change after the\n3190: date of the merger agreement, which subsequent information may or may not be fully reflected in Mac-Gray's or Parent's public disclosures.\n3191: 62\n3192: \n3193: <<<PAGE 69 folio=63>>>\n3194: Table of Contents\n3195: In\n3196: the merger agreement, Mac-Gray has made representations and warranties to Parent and Merger Subsidiary with respect to, among other\n3197: things:\n3198: •\n3199: the due incorporation, valid existence, good standing and power of Mac-Gray;\n3200: •\n3201: its power and authority to enter into the merger agreement and to complete the transactions contemplated by the merger\n3202: agreement and the enforceability of the merger agreement against Mac-Gray;\n3203: •\n3204: the required consents and approvals of governmental authorities in connection with the transactions contemplated by the\n3205: merger agreement;\n3206: •\n3207: the absence of conflicts with, violations or defaults under Mac-Gray's governing documents, applicable laws or certain\n3208: agreements as a result of entering into the merger agreement and the consummation of the merger;\n3209: •\n3210: its capitalization, including in particular the number of outstanding shares of Mac-Gray common stock and preferred stock,\n3211: and the number of shares of common stock issuable upon the exercise of stock options, restricted stock units and other equity awards;\n3212: •\n3213: its subsidiaries and their due incorporation or organization, valid existence, good standing, power and authority;\n3214: •\n3215: its SEC filings since January 1, 2011, including financial statements contained in such filings, internal controls\n3216: and compliance with the Sarbanes-Oxley Act of 2002;\n3217: •\n3218: conduct of business and absence of certain changes, except as contemplated by the merger agreement, including that there\n3219: has not been any event, development or circumstance that has had or would reasonably be expected to have, individually or in the aggregate, a material adverse effect on Mac-Gray;\n3220: •\n3221: the absence of undisclosed material liabilities;\n3222: •\n3223: the absence of certain litigation;\n3224: •\n3225: Mac-Gray's and its subsidiaries' compliance with applicable legal requirements since January 1, 2011;\n3226: •\n3227: matters with respect to Mac-Gray's material contracts;\n3228: •\n3229: tax matters;\n3230: •\n3231: matters related to Mac-Gray's employee benefit plans and labor and employment matters;\n3232: •\n3233: matters related to Mac-Gray's insurance policies;\n3234: •\n3235: compliance with environmental laws and regulations;\n3236: •\n3237: intellectual property and information technology;\n3238: •\n3239: matters related to real property and the absence of encumbrances;\n3240: •\n3241: related party transaction matters;\n3242: •\n3243: compliance with the U.S. Foreign Corrupt Practices Act and other anti-corruption laws;\n3244: •\n3245: the absence of undisclosed brokers' fees and expenses; and\n3246: •\n3247: receipt by the Special Committee of a fairness opinion from BofA Merrill Lynch.\n3248: Many\n3249: of the representations and warranties in the merger agreement made by Mac-Gray are qualified by a \"materiality\" or \"material adverse effect on Mac-Gray\" standard (that is, they will\n3250: not be\n3251: 63\n3252: \n3253: <<<PAGE 70 folio=64>>>\n3254: Table of Contents\n3255: deemed\n3256: to be untrue or incorrect unless their failure to be true or correct, individually or in the aggregate, would, as the case may be, be material or have a material adverse effect on Mac-Gray).\n3257: For purposes of the merger agreement, a \"material adverse effect on Mac-Gray\" means any effect, change, event, circumstance or occurrence that has a material adverse effect on (1) the business,\n3258: assets, financial condition or results of operations of Mac-Gray and its subsidiaries, taken as a whole, or (2) the ability of Mac-Gray to consummate the transactions contemplated by the merger\n3259: agreement.\n3260: The\n3261: definition of \"material adverse effect on Mac-Gray\" excludes any adverse effect resulting from or arising out of:\n3262: (a)\n3263: the\n3264: announcement, pendency or consummation of the merger (including any loss of or adverse change in the relationship of Mac-Gray and its subsidiaries with\n3265: their respective employees, contractors, customers, partners or suppliers as a result thereof);\n3266: (b)\n3267: the\n3268: identity of Parent or any of its affiliates as the acquirer of Mac-Gray;\n3269: (c)\n3270: general\n3271: economic, financial market or political conditions;\n3272: (d)\n3273: general\n3274: conditions in or affecting the industry in which Mac-Gray and its subsidiaries operate or in any specific jurisdiction or geographical area in the\n3275: United States or elsewhere in the world;\n3276: (e)\n3277: any\n3278: changes (after the date of the merger agreement) in GAAP or applicable law (or interpretations thereof);\n3279: (f)\n3280: the\n3281: taking of any specific action, or refraining from taking any specific action, in each case at the written direction of Parent or as expressly required\n3282: by the merger agreement;\n3283: (g)\n3284: any\n3285: suit, claim, action, charge, complaint, litigation, arbitration, proceeding (including any civil, criminal, administrative, investigative or appellate\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 3286]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt, lines 3086-3285\n3086: <<<PAGE 66 folio=60>>>\n3087: Table of Contents\n3088: THE MERGER AGREEMENT\n3089: The summary of the material provisions of the merger agreement below and elsewhere in this proxy statement is\n3090: qualified in its entirety by reference to the merger agreement, a copy of which is attached to this proxy statement as Annex A and which we incorporate by reference into this document. This\n3091: summary does not purport to be complete and may not contain all of the information about the merger agreement that is important to you. We encourage you to read the merger agreement carefully in its\n3092: entirety.\n3093: The Merger\n3094: The merger agreement provides that, subject to the terms and conditions of the merger agreement and in accordance with Delaware law, at\n3095: the effective time of the merger, Merger Subsidiary will merge with and into Mac-Gray. As a result of the merger, Mac-Gray will be the\n3096: surviving corporation, the separate corporate existence of Merger Subsidiary will cease and Mac-Gray will continue as a wholly-owned subsidiary of Parent. As the surviving corporation, Mac-Gray will\n3097: possess the rights, powers, privileges, immunities and franchises and be subject to all of the obligations, liabilities, restrictions and disabilities of Mac-Gray and Merger Subsidiary, all as\n3098: provided under Delaware law.\n3099: The\n3100: closing of the merger will occur as soon as practicable but in any event within two business days after satisfaction or, to the extent permitted by the terms of the merger agreement,\n3101: waiver of all of the conditions set forth in the merger agreement and described under \"—Conditions to the Merger\" unless another time or date is agreed to in writing by the parties to the\n3102: merger agreement.\n3103: The\n3104: merger will become effective when the certificate of merger has been duly filed with the Secretary of State of the State of Delaware or at such later time and date as agreed to by\n3105: the parties in writing and specified in the certificate of merger. The merger is expected to be completed in the first half of 2014. However, the parties cannot predict the exact timing of the\n3106: completion of the merger or whether the merger will be completed at an earlier or later time, as agreed by the parties, or at all.\n3107: The Merger Consideration and the Conversion of Capital Stock\n3108: Immediately prior to the effective time of the merger, each share of Mac-Gray common stock outstanding immediately prior to the\n3109: effective time of the merger will be canceled and converted into the right to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest, other than:\n3110: •\n3111: shares of Mac-Gray common stock owned by Mac-Gray as treasury stock or shares owned by any Buyer Entity, Merger Subsidiary\n3112: or their wholly owned subsidiaries, which will be canceled, and no payment will be made with respect thereto; and\n3113: •\n3114: shares of Mac-Gray common stock held by a stockholder who has properly exercised, and has not failed to perfect, withdrawn\n3115: or otherwise lost, appraisal rights in accordance with Delaware law.\n3116: The\n3117: price to be paid for each share of Mac-Gray common stock in the merger will be adjusted appropriately to reflect the effect of any change in the outstanding shares of capital stock\n3118: of Mac-Gray, including by reason of any reclassification, recapitalization, stock split (including reverse stock split) or combination, exchange or readjustment of shares, or any stock dividend, that\n3119: occurs prior to the effective time of the merger.\n3120: Each\n3121: share of common stock of Merger Subsidiary outstanding immediately prior to the effective time of the merger will be converted into and become one fully paid, nonassessable share of\n3122: common stock, par value $0.01 per share, of the surviving corporation with the same rights, powers and privileges as the shares so converted and will constitute the only outstanding shares of capital\n3123: stock of the surviving corporation.\n3124: 60\n3125: \n3126: <<<PAGE 67 folio=61>>>\n3127: Table of Contents\n3128: Mac-Gray Equity-Based Awards\n3129: Immediately prior to the effective time of the merger, and without any action on the part of the holders thereof, each Mac-Gray stock\n3130: option, whether or not vested and exercisable, that is outstanding and unexercised immediately prior to the effective time of the merger, will be automatically converted into the right to receive from\n3131: Parent or the surviving corporation immediately after the effective time of the merger an amount in cash equal to the product obtained by multiplying (i) the excess, if any, of $21.25 over the\n3132: per share exercise price of such Mac-Gray stock option, by (ii) the aggregate number of shares of Mac-Gray common stock that were issuable upon exercise or settlement of such Mac-Gray stock\n3133: option immediately prior to the effective time of the merger. If the exercise price per share of any Mac-Gray stock option equals or exceeds $21.25, the amount to be paid for such Mac-Gray stock\n3134: option will be zero.\n3135: Immediately\n3136: prior to the effective time of the merger, and without any action on the part of the holders thereof each outstanding Mac-Gray restricted stock award or restricted stock unit\n3137: under any Mac-Gray stock plans will become fully vested, will not be assumed by Parent or Merger Subsidiary in the merger and will be canceled and extinguished as of the effective time of the merger\n3138: and, in exchange therefor, each former holder of any such restricted stock award or restricted stock unit will have the right to receive from Parent or the surviving corporation an amount in cash\n3139: equal to the product obtained by multiplying (i) the maximum number of shares of Mac-Gray common stock subject to such restricted stock award or restricted stock unit by (ii) the $21.25.\n3140: From and after the effective time of the merger, any Mac-Gray restricted stock award or restricted stock unit will no longer\n3141: represent the right to receive shares of Mac-Gray common stock by the former holder thereof, but will only entitle such holder to the payment described above, if any.\n3142: Mac-Gray Employee Stock Purchase Plan\n3143: As soon as practicable following the date of the merger agreement, but not later than the day immediately prior to the date on which\n3144: the first offering period that is regularly scheduled to commence under the ESPP, after the date of the merger agreement is scheduled to commence, Mac-Gray will take all actions necessary or required\n3145: under the ESPP and applicable law to (1) suspend the ESPP, (2) end the last offering period that commenced period to the date of the merger agreement on the earlier to occur of its\n3146: regularly scheduled end date under the terms of the ESPP or three calendar days prior to the effective date of the merger, and (3) cause the ESPP to terminate as of the effective date of the\n3147: merger such that no further rights will be granted or exercised under the ESPP thereafter.\n3148: Payment Procedures\n3149: Prior to the effective time of the merger, Parent will appoint an exchange agent reasonably acceptable to Mac-Gray for the purpose of\n3150: exchanging for the merger consideration the certificated and uncertificated shares of Mac-Gray common stock. At or prior to the effective time of the merger, Parent will deposit, or cause to be\n3151: deposited, with the exchange agent the aggregate merger consideration to be paid in respect of the certificated and uncertificated shares of Mac-Gray common stock. To the extent such fund diminishes\n3152: for any reason below the level required to make prompt payment of the merger consideration, Parent and the surviving corporation will promptly replace or restore the lost portion of such fund so as to\n3153: ensure that it is, at all times, maintained at a level sufficient to make such payments.\n3154: Each\n3155: holder of shares of Mac-Gray common stock that have been converted into the right to receive the merger consideration will be entitled to receive the merger consideration in respect\n3156: of their shares of Mac-Gray common stock upon (1) surrender to the exchange agent of a certificate, together with a duly completed and validly executed letter of transmittal and such other\n3157: documents as may\n3158: 61\n3159: \n3160: <<<PAGE 68 folio=62>>>\n3161: Table of Contents\n3162: reasonably\n3163: be requested by the exchange agent, or (2) receipt of an \"agent's message\" by the exchange agent (or such other evidence, if any, of transfer as the exchange agent may reasonably\n3164: request) in the case of a book-entry transfer of uncertificated shares of Mac-Gray common stock. Until so surrendered or transferred, each such certificated or uncertificated share will represent\n3165: after the effective time of the merger for all purposes only the right to receive such merger consideration. No interest will be paid or accrued on the cash payable upon the surrender or transfer of\n3166: such certificated or uncertificated share.\n3167: If\n3168: any portion of the merger consideration is to be paid to a person other than the person in whose name the surrendered certificate or the transferred uncertificated share is\n3169: registered, it will be a condition to such payment that (1) either such certificate will be properly endorsed or will otherwise be in proper form for transfer or such uncertificated share will\n3170: be properly transferred and (2) the person requesting such payment will pay to the exchange agent any transfer or other tax required as a result of such payment to a person other than the\n3171: registered holder of such certificate or uncertificated share or establish to the satisfaction of the exchange agent that such tax has been paid or is not payable.\n3172: All\n3173: merger consideration paid upon the surrender of certificated or uncertificated shares in accordance with the terms of the merger agreement will be deemed to have been paid in full\n3174: satisfaction of all rights pertaining to the shares of Mac-Gray common stock formerly represented by such certificated or uncertificated shares. From and after the effective time of the merger, there\n3175: will be no further registration of transfers of shares of Mac-Gray common stock on the stock transfer books of the surviving corporation. If, after the effective time of the merger, certificated or\n3176: uncertificated shares of Mac-Gray common stock are presented to the surviving corporation, they will be canceled and exchanged for the merger consideration in accordance with the procedures described\n3177: in the two paragraphs immediately above.\n3178: Any\n3179: portion of the payment fund deposited with the exchange agent that remains unclaimed by the holders of shares of Company common stock twelve months after the effective time of the\n3180: merger will be delivered to the surviving corporation, upon demand, and any such holder who has not exchanged shares of Mac-Gray common stock for the merger consideration in accordance with the merger\n3181: agreement prior to that time will thereafter look only to Parent or the surviving corporation for payment of the merger consideration, without interest.\n3182: Mac-Gray Representations and Warranties\n3183: The merger agreement contains representations and warranties made by Mac-Gray to Parent and Merger Subsidiary and representations and\n3184: warranties made by Parent and Merger Subsidiary to Mac-Gray. The assertions embodied in those representations and warranties were made for purposes of the merger agreement and are subject to\n3185: qualifications and limitations agreed to by the respective parties in connection with negotiating the terms of the merger agreement, including information contained in confidential disclosure\n3186: schedules that the parties exchanged in connection with signing the merger agreement. Accordingly, investors and security holders should not rely on such representations and warranties as\n3187: characterizations of the actual state of facts or circumstances, since they were only made as of a specific date and are modified in important part by the underlying disclosure schedules. In addition,\n3188: certain representations and warranties may be subject to a contractual standard of materiality different from what might be viewed as material to stockholders, or may have been used for purposes of\n3189: allocating risk between the respective parties rather than establishing matters of fact. Moreover, information concerning the subject matter of such representations and warranties may change after the\n3190: date of the merger agreement, which subsequent information may or may not be fully reflected in Mac-Gray's or Parent's public disclosures.\n3191: 62\n3192: \n3193: <<<PAGE 69 folio=63>>>\n3194: Table of Contents\n3195: In\n3196: the merger agreement, Mac-Gray has made representations and warranties to Parent and Merger Subsidiary with respect to, among other\n3197: things:\n3198: •\n3199: the due incorporation, valid existence, good standing and power of Mac-Gray;\n3200: •\n3201: its power and authority to enter into the merger agreement and to complete the transactions contemplated by the merger\n3202: agreement and the enforceability of the merger agreement against Mac-Gray;\n3203: •\n3204: the required consents and approvals of governmental authorities in connection with the transactions contemplated by the\n3205: merger agreement;\n3206: •\n3207: the absence of conflicts with, violations or defaults under Mac-Gray's governing documents, applicable laws or certain\n3208: agreements as a result of entering into the merger agreement and the consummation of the merger;\n3209: •\n3210: its capitalization, including in particular the number of outstanding shares of Mac-Gray common stock and preferred stock,\n3211: and the number of shares of common stock issuable upon the exercise of stock options, restricted stock units and other equity awards;\n3212: •\n3213: its subsidiaries and their due incorporation or organization, valid existence, good standing, power and authority;\n3214: •\n3215: its SEC filings since January 1, 2011, including financial statements contained in such filings, internal controls\n3216: and compliance with the Sarbanes-Oxley Act of 2002;\n3217: •\n3218: conduct of business and absence of certain changes, except as contemplated by the merger agreement, including that there\n3219: has not been any event, development or circumstance that has had or would reasonably be expected to have, individually or in the aggregate, a material adverse effect on Mac-Gray;\n3220: •\n3221: the absence of undisclosed material liabilities;\n3222: •\n3223: the absence of certain litigation;\n3224: •\n3225: Mac-Gray's and its subsidiaries' compliance with applicable legal requirements since January 1, 2011;\n3226: •\n3227: matters with respect to Mac-Gray's material contracts;\n3228: •\n3229: tax matters;\n3230: •\n3231: matters related to Mac-Gray's employee benefit plans and labor and employment matters;\n3232: •\n3233: matters related to Mac-Gray's insurance policies;\n3234: •\n3235: compliance with environmental laws and regulations;\n3236: •\n3237: intellectual property and information technology;\n3238: •\n3239: matters related to real property and the absence of encumbrances;\n3240: •\n3241: related party transaction matters;\n3242: •\n3243: compliance with the U.S. Foreign Corrupt Practices Act and other anti-corruption laws;\n3244: •\n3245: the absence of undisclosed brokers' fees and expenses; and\n3246: •\n3247: receipt by the Special Committee of a fairness opinion from BofA Merrill Lynch.\n3248: Many\n3249: of the representations and warranties in the merger agreement made by Mac-Gray are qualified by a \"materiality\" or \"material adverse effect on Mac-Gray\" standard (that is, they will\n3250: not be\n3251: 63\n3252: \n3253: <<<PAGE 70 folio=64>>>\n3254: Table of Contents\n3255: deemed\n3256: to be untrue or incorrect unless their failure to be true or correct, individually or in the aggregate, would, as the case may be, be material or have a material adverse effect on Mac-Gray).\n3257: For purposes of the merger agreement, a \"material adverse effect on Mac-Gray\" means any effect, change, event, circumstance or occurrence that has a material adverse effect on (1) the business,\n3258: assets, financial condition or results of operations of Mac-Gray and its subsidiaries, taken as a whole, or (2) the ability of Mac-Gray to consummate the transactions contemplated by the merger\n3259: agreement.\n3260: The\n3261: definition of \"material adverse effect on Mac-Gray\" excludes any adverse effect resulting from or arising out of:\n3262: (a)\n3263: the\n3264: announcement, pendency or consummation of the merger (including any loss of or adverse change in the relationship of Mac-Gray and its subsidiaries with\n3265: their respective employees, contractors, customers, partners or suppliers as a result thereof);\n3266: (b)\n3267: the\n3268: identity of Parent or any of its affiliates as the acquirer of Mac-Gray;\n3269: (c)\n3270: general\n3271: economic, financial market or political conditions;\n3272: (d)\n3273: general\n3274: conditions in or affecting the industry in which Mac-Gray and its subsidiaries operate or in any specific jurisdiction or geographical area in the\n3275: United States or elsewhere in the world;\n3276: (e)\n3277: any\n3278: changes (after the date of the merger agreement) in GAAP or applicable law (or interpretations thereof);\n3279: (f)\n3280: the\n3281: taking of any specific action, or refraining from taking any specific action, in each case at the written direction of Parent or as expressly required\n3282: by the merger agreement;\n3283: (g)\n3284: any\n3285: suit, claim, action, charge, complaint, litigation, arbitration, proceeding (including any civil, criminal, administrative, investigative or appellate\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 3286]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 200, \"offset\": 3086, \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824358820,"end":1789824358999}}}}
