 33\nrow('bid_partyC_sep10', '09/10/2013', 'Party C (financial bidder)', 'Bid', 1, 2, 'Financial',\n    'Revised oral indication of interest in a telephone call to BofA Merrill Lynch: all-cash $16.00\\u2013$17.00 per share; no firm financing commitment.',\n    'Informal', 'Heavy',\n    [('Stated oral indication', [('P-049', 'in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch, a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share')]),\n     ('No firm commitment', [('P-049', 'Neither Party A\\u2019s nor Party C\\u2019s revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment')])],\n    count=1, date_from=D(2013,9,10), date_to=D(2013,9,10), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    price_low=16.0, price_high=17.0, price_kind='Bidder range', price_origin='Stated', currency='USD',\n    all_cash='Yes', cond_detail=CC.format('not committed','not stated','yes','not stated'),\n    page=35, review='Q4')\n\n# 34\nrow('macdonald_brief', '09/11/2013 (limited overview) \\u2013 09/12/2013 (detailed briefing)',\n    'Mac-Gray Transaction Committee / BofA Merrill Lynch \\u2194 Mr. MacDonald', 'Material process update',\n    1, 2, None,\n    'Mr. MacDonald\\u2019s rollover question resolved: in a limited-overview call (no bidder identities or prices) he said he was not interested in rolling over any shares; the Special Committee agreed he should be fully briefed because any potential acquiror was seen as unlikely to proceed without knowing he would support the transaction; a 09/12/2013 detailed briefing followed, after which he voiced general support while urging a higher value.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated rollover position', [('P-049', 'During this call, Mr. MacDonald indicated that he had decided that he was not interested in rolling over any of his shares in any transaction')]),\n     ('Stated support premise', [('P-050', 'it was unlikely that any of these parties would move forward in the process without the express support of Mr. MacDonald')]),\n     ('Stated briefing and stance', [('P-051', 'Although Mr. MacDonald voiced his general support for continuing with the process, he expressed his view that Mac-Gray should continue to seek a higher value for stockholders')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,9,11), date_to=D(2013,9,12), date_basis='Reported interval', date_method='Assigned: bound',\n    page=35, related='R016; R049; R041 (his 09/19 support at $21.25)', review='Q6; Q7')\n\n# 35\nrow('r3_open', '09/11/2013', 'Mac-Gray Special Committee (via BofA Merrill Lynch) \\u2192 Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona',\n    'Round opened', 1, 3, None,\n    'First request for final indications of interest: BofA Merrill Lynch called each of the four bidders on 09/11/2013, as instructed, requesting final indications by 09/18/2013 and signaling that Mac-Gray would consider a short exclusive negotiation with one bidder depending on price and deal certainty. Invited bidders unchanged. Round finality: Announced as final \\u2014 the target asked for \"final indications of interest\".',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated instruction', [('P-050', 'the Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to call each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013 and to indicate that Mac-Gray would consider engaging in a short period of exclusive negotiations with one of the bidders depending upon, among other things, the proposed purchase price and the level of deal certainty indicated in the bidder\\u2019s final proposal')]),\n     ('Calls made same day', [('P-050', 'representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch called each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona on September 11, 2013 with such instructions')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,9,11), date_to=D(2013,9,11), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    due_date=D(2013,9,18), round_finality='Announced as final',\n    page=36, related='R036', review='Q1')\n\n# 36\nrow('deadline_0918', '09/18/2013', 'N/A \\u2014 solicitation deadline', 'Deadline', 1, 3, None,\n    'Final-indication due date reached. Three bidders responded on 09/18/2013 (CSC/Pamplona $20.75; Party A best-and-final reiteration; Party B $21.50 package); Party C did not submit (R040). The Special Committee took its next step on the bids in hand at its 09/19/2013 meeting \\u2014 selection of CSC/Pamplona and authorization to offer exclusivity at $21.25. Treatment: Enforced.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Due date and responses', [('P-050', 'to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013'),\n       ('P-053', 'On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share')]),\n     ('Next step on the bids in hand', [('P-055', 'the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,9,18), date_to=D(2013,9,18), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    due_date=D(2013,9,18), deadline_treatment='Enforced',\n    page=36, related='R035', review='Q2')\n\n# 37\nrow('bid_csc_sep18', '09/18/2013', 'CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder)', 'Bid', 1, 3, 'Strategic',\n    'Final-solicited proposal: all-cash $20.75 per share; Pamplona reiterated it was committed to provide 100% of the capital required; requested two-week exclusive negotiations.',\n    'Formal', 'Light',\n    [('Stated proposal and commitment', [('P-053', 'On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share, reiterating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to engage in exclusive negotiations for two weeks')]),\n     ('Formal signal \\u2014 response on the requested basis to the final solicitation', [('P-050', 'to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013')])],\n    count=1, date_from=D(2013,9,18), date_to=D(2013,9,18), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    price_low=20.75, price_high=20.75, price_kind='Point', price_origin='Stated', currency='USD',\n    all_cash='Yes', cash_close=20.75, cond_detail=CC.format('committed','not stated','yes','requested (2 wks)'),\n    page=36, related='R042 (Sept 21 increase); R035', review='Q4')\n\n# 38\nrow('bid_partyA_sep18', '09/18/2013', 'Party A (strategic bidder)', 'Bid reaffirmed', 1, 3, 'Strategic',\n    'Reaffirmed by: price confirmed \\u2014 telephone reiteration that its earlier all-cash $18.00\\u2013$19.00 indication was Party A\\u2019s best and final offer; price carried forward from R032, not restated. Financing basis unchanged (outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity; no firm commitment).',\n    'Formal', 'Heavy',\n    [('Stated reaffirmation', [('P-053', 'Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer')]),\n     ('Formal signal \\u2014 best-and-final response; standing conditions unchanged', [('P-049', 'Neither Party A\\u2019s nor Party C\\u2019s revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment')])],\n    count=1, date_from=D(2013,9,18), date_to=D(2013,9,18), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    price_low=18.0, price_high=19.0, price_kind='Bidder range', price_origin='Carried forward', currency='USD',\n    all_cash='Yes', cond_detail=CC.format('not committed','not stated','yes','not stated'),\n    page=36, related='R032 (carried price); R042 (later Party A dropped)', review='Q4; Q5')\n\n# 39\nrow('bid_partyB_sep18', '09/18/2013', 'Party B (financial bidder)', 'Bid', 1, 3, 'Financial',\n    'Revised indication valued by Party B at $21.50 per share: $19.00 cash at closing plus options representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B\\u2019s initial cost basis; options to vest over five years on achievement of the base-case management projections (excluding future acquisitions); Party B valued the options at $2.50 per share. Package value, not guaranteed cash; financing remained without a firm commitment.',\n    'Formal', 'Heavy',\n    [('Stated package and option terms', [('P-053', 'Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing and the remaining per share price to be paid in the form of options to be issued to Mac-Gray stockholders, representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B\\u2019s initial cost basis. These options, which we refer to as the Party B options, would vest on the achievement of the base case management projections ( i.e. , over five years), excluding any future acquisitions. Party B\\u2019s proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share')]),\n     ('Financing not committed; formal signal \\u2014 final-solicitation response', [('P-049', 'Neither Party A\\u2019s nor Party C\\u2019s revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment')])],\n    count=1, date_from=D(2013,9,18), date_to=D(2013,9,18), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    price_low=21.50, price_high=21.50, price_kind='Point', price_origin='Stated', currency='USD',\n    all_cash='No', cash_close=19.00, cond_detail=CC.format('not committed','not stated','yes','not stated'),\n    page=36, related='R031 (prior priced bid)', review='Q4; Q5')\n\n# 40\nrow('dns_partyC', 'by 09/18/2013 (final-indication deadline passed with no submission)',\n    'Party C (financial bidder)', 'Did not submit', 1, 3, 'Financial',\n    'Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior $16.00\\u2013$17.00 indication in response to the 09/11/2013 final request, and the filing states it gave no reasons. Closed at this transition; no further Party C participation is reported.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated non-submission', [('P-053', 'Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share nor did it specify any reasons in connection therewith')])],\n    count=1, date_from=None, date_to=D(2013,9,18), date_basis='Relative only', date_method='Assigned: deadline',\n    decided_by='Unknown', exit_reason='Not stated', outcome_basis='Stated',\n    page=36, review='Q3')\n\n# 41\nrow('sep19_decision', '09/19/2013', 'Mac-Gray Special Committee', 'Target decision', 1, 3, None,\n    'Preferred-bidder decision: the Special Committee concluded CSC/Pamplona\\u2019s indication offered the most value, greater certainty and less risk (Party B\\u2019s options were contingent and complex and Party B would likely need third-party debt); it concluded CSC/Pamplona should be able to raise above $20.75 and authorized the Transaction Committee to offer exclusivity at $21.25; Mr. MacDonald indicated he would support $21.25.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated conclusion', [('P-055', 'the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications')]),\n     ('Price requirement and exclusivity authorization', [('P-055', 'the Special Committee also concluded that, primarily in view of potential synergies between Mac-Gray and CSC, CSC/Pamplona should be in a position to increase their offer price above $20.75. The Special Committee then authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share'),\n       ('P-055', 'at this meeting Mr. MacDonald indicated that he would be supportive of a price of $21.25 per share')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,9,19), date_to=D(2013,9,19), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    page=37, related='R042; R043')\n\n# 42\nrow('bid_csc_sep21', '09/21/2013', 'CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder)', 'Bid', 1, 3, 'Strategic',\n    'Price increase to $21.25 per share all-cash as a last and best offer, provided Mac-Gray agreed to a two-week exclusive negotiation; CSC/Pamplona also requested a customary voting agreement over Mr. MacDonald\\u2019s and his immediate family\\u2019s shares. This is the price component of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal (no financing contingency; Pamplona committing 100% of the capital needed for closing).',\n    'Formal', 'Light',\n    [('Stated confirmation', [('P-056', 'the representative of CSC/Pamplona called the members of the Transaction Committee to confirm that CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer, provided that Mac-Gray agree to a two week period of exclusive negotiations')]),\n     ('Voting agreement request', [('P-056', 'The representative of CSC/Pamplona also requested that shares of Mac-Gray common stock owned beneficially and of record by Mr. MacDonald and his immediate family be subject to a customary voting agreement, which we refer to as the MacDonald voting agreements')]),\n     ('Final proposal terms', [('P-057', 'the inclusion of a $15 million \"reverse\" termination fee payable by CSC/Pamplona to Mac-Gray in the event regulatory clearance is not obtained, which we refer to as the CSC reverse termination fee, agreements regarding certain post-signing covenants, the fact that there would be no financing contingency and that Pamplona was committing to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing')])],\n    count=0, date_from=D(2013,9,21), date_to=D(2013,9,21), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    price_low=21.25, price_high=21.25, price_kind='Point', price_origin='Stated', currency='USD',\n    all_cash='Yes', cash_close=21.25, cond_detail=CC.format('committed','not stated','yes','requested (2 wks)'),\n    page=37, related='R037 (revises R037); R043', review='Q4')\n\n# 43\nrow('sep23_excl_auth', '09/23/2013', 'Mac-Gray Special Committee; CSC/Pamplona', 'Exclusivity changed',\n    1, 3, None,\n    'Authorized: the Special Committee authorized Mac-Gray to enter an exclusivity agreement providing exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013 on the CSC/Pamplona final proposal terms ($21.25 per share cash; $15 million CSC reverse termination fee if regulatory clearance is not obtained; no financing contingency; Pamplona to fund 100% of closing capital); the agreement would automatically terminate if CSC or Pamplona adversely changed the final proposal terms.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated authorization', [('P-059', 'After discussion, the Special Committee authorized Mac-Gray to enter into an exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013 on the terms included in the CSC/Pamplona final proposal')]),\n     ('Stated terms and condition', [('P-058', 'The parties also agreed that the exclusivity agreement would automatically terminate if CSC or Pamplona adversely changed any of the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,9,23), date_to=D(2013,9,23), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    page=38, related='R044; R042', review='Q8')\n\n# 44\nrow('sep24_excl_exec', '09/24/2013', 'CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray', 'Exclusivity changed', 1, 3, None,\n    'Executed: CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement \\u2014 exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013, subject to certain conditions including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the final proposal terms. This execution is the transition into the definitive-negotiation stage (R047).',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated execution', [('P-061', 'On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, subject to certain conditions, including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,9,24), date_to=D(2013,9,24), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    page=38, related='R043; R047; R045; R046', review='Q8')\n\n# 45\nrow('dropped_partyA', 'by 09/24/2013 (exclusivity execution)', 'Party A (strategic bidder)', 'Dropped by target',\n    1, 3, 'Strategic',\n    'Inferred: exclusivity \\u2014 Party A was still live after the final round (its best-and-final reiteration of 09/18/2013) when Mac-Gray executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013; the filing reports no notice to Party A and states no reason. Closed at this transition.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Exclusivity execution', [('P-061', 'On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013')]),\n     ('Last participation', [('P-053', 'Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer')])],\n    count=1, date_from=None, date_to=D(2013,9,24), date_basis='Relative only', date_method='Assigned: decision day',\n    decided_by='Target', exit_reason='Not stated', outcome_basis='Inferred: exclusivity',\n    page=38, related='R038; R044', review='Q3')\n\n# 46\nrow('dropped_partyB', 'by 09/24/2013 (exclusivity execution)', 'Party B (financial bidder)', 'Dropped by target',\n    1, 3, 'Financial',\n    'Inferred: exclusivity \\u2014 Party B was still live after the final round (its 09/18/2013 $21.50 package) when Mac-Gray executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013; the filing reports no notice to Party B and states no reason. Closed at this transition.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Exclusivity execution', [('P-061', 'On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013')]),\n     ('Last participation', [('P-053', 'Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share')])],\n    count=1, date_from=None, date_to=D(2013,9,24), date_basis='Relative only', date_method='Assigned: decision day',\n    decided_by='Target', exit_reason='Not stated', outcome_basis='Inferred: exclusivity',\n    page=38, related='R039; R044', review='Q3')\n\n# 47\nrow('r4_open', '09/24/2013', 'Mac-Gray \\u2194 CSC/Pamplona', 'Round opened', 1, 4, None,\n    'Definitive-negotiation stage opens with the 09/24/2013 exclusivity execution (R044); Goodwin Procter delivered the initial merger-agreement draft to Kirkland & Ellis on 09/25/2013 (R048) and CSC/Pamplona were granted full data-site and management access for confirmatory diligence. Selected bidder CSC/Pamplona remains live; all other bidders are already closed. Round finality: Inferred final \\u2014 no announcement, but the target moved to definitive negotiation with the selected bidder.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Draft delivered and confirmatory diligence', [('P-062', 'On September 25, 2013, Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement'),\n       ('P-062', 'CSC and Pamplona were granted full access to the electronic data site and access to certain members of management and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence on Mac-Gray')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,9,24), date_to=D(2013,9,24), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    round_finality='Inferred final',\n    page=38, related='R044; R048; R043; R035', review='Q1')\n\n# 48\nrow('kirkland', '09/25/2013', 'Kirkland & Ellis LLP (outside legal counsel, CSC/Pamplona)', 'Adviser service observed',\n    1, 4, None,\n    'First shown acting on the CSC/Pamplona mandate when Goodwin Procter delivered the initial merger-agreement draft to Kirkland; engagement date not disclosed. Kirkland negotiated the merger agreement and the Pamplona commitment letter for CSC/Pamplona.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Earliest observed service', [('P-062', 'On September 25, 2013, Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,9,25), date_to=D(2013,9,25), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    page=38)\n\n# 49\nrow('rollover_resolve', 'after 09/23/2013; reported 10/07/2013', 'Moab Partners; CSC/Pamplona; Mac-Gray Special Committee',\n    'Material process update', 1, 4, None,\n    'Moab rollover resolved without a rollover: the Special Committee had allowed Mr. Rothenberg on 09/23/2013 to resume discussions with CSC/Pamplona about a possible rollover of Moab\\u2019s shares; after those discussions it was determined that Moab would not roll over any shares in the transaction, as reported to the Special Committee on 10/07/2013.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated permission', [('P-059', 'to provide Moab with the opportunity to resume discussions with CSC/Pamplona regarding a possible equity rollover of Moab\\u2019s shares in the transaction if Moab still had an interest in such a rollover')]),\n     ('Stated discussion period', [('P-062', 'Mr. Rothenberg engaged in various discussions with representatives of Pamplona during this time to discuss a possible rollover of Moab shares')]),\n     ('Stated determination reported 10/07/2013', [('P-066', 'Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,9,23), date_to=D(2013,10,7), date_basis='Approximate window', date_method='Assigned: bound',\n    page=39, related='R016 (denial); R010', review='Q6; Q7')\n\n# 50\nrow('oct9_excl_auth', '10/09/2013', 'Mac-Gray Special Committee; CSC/Pamplona', 'Exclusivity changed',\n    1, 4, None,\n    'Extension authorized: the Special Committee authorized the Transaction Committee to negotiate the open issues within parameters and to extend exclusivity to 10/15/2013; CSC/Pamplona had requested extension of the 5 p.m. ET 10/12 expiry to allow continued negotiations.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated request and authorization', [('P-069', 'Kirkland had requested on behalf of CSC/Pamplona that the exclusivity agreement, due to expire at 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, be extended to allow for continued negotiations of these open issues. After discussion, the Special Committee authorized the Transaction Committee to negotiate the open issues within certain parameters and in connection therewith to extend exclusivity to October 15, 2013')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,10,9), date_to=D(2013,10,9), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    page=40, related='R051', review='Q8')\n\n# 51\nrow('oct12_excl_ext', '10/12/2013', 'CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray', 'Exclusivity changed', 1, 4, None,\n    'Extended: letter agreement executed extending exclusivity to 11:59 p.m. ET on 10/15/2013. The extension was authorized subject to CSC/Pamplona agreeing to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million; CSC/Pamplona agreed on 10/11/2013.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated execution', [('P-072', 'On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013')]),\n     ('Stated condition and agreement', [('P-071', 'the Special Committee confirmed that the Transaction Committee and representatives of Mac-Gray were authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million'),\n       ('P-071', 'the representative of CSC/Pamplona telephoned Mr. Daoust and agreed to the $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,10,12), date_to=D(2013,10,12), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    page=41, related='R050', review='Q8')\n\n# 52\nrow('oct14_decision', '10/14/2013', 'Mac-Gray Special Committee; Mac-Gray Board of Directors', 'Target decision',\n    1, 4, None,\n    'BofA Merrill Lynch delivered its oral fairness opinion (confirmed in writing, dated 10/14/2013); the Special Committee unanimously determined to recommend the merger agreement; the Board, on that recommendation, unanimously approved and adopted the merger agreement and recommends stockholder adoption.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated opinion', [('P-075', 'BofA Merrill Lynch reviewed with the Special Committee its financial analysis of the consideration and delivered to the Special Committee an oral opinion, which was confirmed by delivery of a written opinion dated, October 14, 2013')]),\n     ('Stated recommendations', [('P-076', 'the Board (upon the recommendation of the Special Committee) unanimously determined that the merger agreement and the merger were advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray\\u2019s stockholders, approved the merger on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the merger agreement, adopted the merger agreement and recommended that the Mac-Gray stockholders adopt and approve the merger agreement')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,10,14), date_to=D(2013,10,14), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    page=41, related='R053', review='Q5')\n\n# 53\nrow('signed', '10/14/2013', 'Mac-Gray; CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.; CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.; Spin Holdco Inc.; CSC Fenway, Inc.',\n    'Merger agreement signed', 1, 4, None,\n    'Executed: Agreement and Plan of Merger dated as of 10/14/2013 (Mac-Gray; Holdings; CSC; Spin Holdco/Parent; CSC Fenway/Merger Subsidiary). Agreed consideration: $21.25 per share in cash, without interest, less applicable withholding. Pamplona commitment letter ($594 million) delivered; no financing condition to the Buyer Entities\\u2019 obligations; Mac-Gray termination fee $11 million; CSC reverse termination fee $15 million; Pamplona damages liability capped at $50 million (Buyer Entities unlimited). Moab voting agreement executed and the MacDonald voting agreements became effective (\\u224815% of shares subject to voting agreements). No go-shop; the Board retained a fiduciary out to accept a superior proposal on payment of the $11 million fee.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated execution and related documents', [('P-077', 'Later in the day, on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective')]),\n     ('Consideration', [('X-001', 'will be automatically converted into the right to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest and less applicable withholding taxes')]),\n     ('Termination fees', [('X-005', 'Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances'),\n                            ('X-025', 'then Parent will pay Mac-Gray the $15 million Parent termination fee')]),\n     ('Financing', [('X-019', 'The merger agreement does not contain any condition to the obligations of the Buyer Entities or Merger Subsidiary relating to the receipt of financing by the Buyer Entities'),\n                     ('X-020', 'an aggregate of $594 million of capital (the Pamplona commitment amount)')]),\n     ('Voting agreements', [('X-026', 'Approximately 15% of the outstanding Mac-Gray shares on the record date for the special meeting are subject to the voting agreements')])],\n    page=41, related='R052; R054; R044', review='Q5')\n\n# 54\nrow('announced', '10/15/2013', 'Mac-Gray and CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.', 'Merger announced', 1, 'post', None,\n    'Joint announcement of the execution of the merger agreement, before U.S. stock markets opened. The merger was announced as expected to close in January 2014 (first half of 2014 per the merger-agreement section); no completion is observed in this filing.',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated announcement', [('P-078', 'On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement')]),\n     ('Expected timing', [('X-008', 'We currently expect the merger to be completed in January 2014')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,10,15), date_to=D(2013,10,15), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    page=41, related='R053')\n\n# 55\nrow('mackenzie', '12/04/2013', 'MacKenzie Partners, Inc. (proxy solicitor, Mac-Gray)', 'Adviser service observed',\n    1, 'post', None,\n    'Proxy solicitor for the special meeting; the proxy statement states Mac-Gray expects to retain MacKenzie Partners for the solicitation for a fee of approximately $15,000 plus out-of-pocket expenses and indemnification (expected retention, not a stated executed engagement).',\n    None, None,\n    [('Stated expected retention', [('X-010', 'we expect to retain MacKenzie Partners, Inc. to assist in the solicitation for a fee of approximately $15,000')])],\n    date_from=D(2013,12,4), date_to=D(2013,12,4), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\n    page=23)\n\nprint('rows defined:', len(ROWS), '| X passages:', len(XPASS))\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- data checks & dump\nproblems = []\nfor r in ROWS:\n    for label, quotes in [(r['why_parts'][i][0] if i < len(r['why_parts']) else '', None) for i in range(0)]:\n        pass\n# resolve quotes\nfor r in ROWS:\n    resolved = []\n    for label, qs in r.get('why_parts', []):\n        for sid, quote in qs:\n            raw, err = q(sid, quote)\n            if err:\n                problems.append((r['key'], label, err))\n            else:\n                src = SOURCES[sid]\n                resolved.append({'label': label, 'source': sid, 'page': src['page'], 'quote': raw})\n    r['resolved'] = resolved\n\n# date/order checks\ndef key_ord(r):\n    if not r.get('date_from') and r.get('date_to'):\n        return r['date_to'].toordinal()\n    return (r.get('date_from') or r.get('date_to')).toordinal()\n\nbad = []\nfor i in range(1, len(ROWS)):\n    a, b = ROWS[i-1], ROWS[i]\n    # working date derived later; check here using rules: reported days use their date; else assigned\n    pass\n\nprint('quote problems:', len(problems))\nfor p in problems:\n    print(' *', p)\n\n# dump\njson.dump({'rows': ROWS, 'paras': PARAS, 'xpass': XPASS,\n           'problems': [list(map(str, p)) for p in problems]},\n          open(OUT, 'w'), ensure_ascii=False, default=str, indent=1)\nprint('dumped', OUT)\n","path":"/tmp/opencode/build_data.py"},"output":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/build_data.py","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/build_data.py"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Build and verify the Mac-Gray deal-ledger data (rows, questions, summary, source text).\\n\\nOutputs /tmp/opencode/ledger_data.json with fully resolved quotes and dates.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport re, json, unicodedata, difflib\\nfrom datetime import date\\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\\n\\nSRC = 'raw_filing/mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm'\\nPAGES = '/tmp/opencode/filing_pages.txt'\\nOUT = '/tmp/opencode/ledger_data.json'\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- source loading\\nhtml = open(SRC, encoding='utf-8', errors='replace').read()\\nmarkers = list(re.finditer(r\\\"<!--\\\\s*ZEQ\\\\.=\\\\d+,SEQ=\\\\d+,.*?-->\\\", html))\\nparts = re.split(r'<!--\\\\s*ZEQ\\\\.=\\\\d+,SEQ=\\\\d+,.*?-->', html)\\nfolios = [re.search(r\\\"FOLIO='([^']*)'\\\", m.group(0)).group(1) for m in markers]\\n\\n# page texts from the pre-extracted file (line list per component)\\nlines = open(PAGES, encoding='utf-8').read().split('\\\\n')\\ncomp_text = []          # list of (folio, raw_text_joined_with_spaces)\\ncurrent = None\\nfor ln in lines:\\n    m = re.match(r'<<<PAGE (\\\\d+) folio=(\\\\S+)>>>', ln)\\n    if m:\\n        current = []\\n        comp_text.append((m.group(2), current))\\n        continue\\n    if current is not None and ln.strip():\\n        current.append(ln.strip())\\ncomp_text = [(f, ' '.join(ls)) for f, ls in comp_text]\\nALL = ' '.join(t for _, t in comp_text)\\n\\n# background paragraphs (same logic as make_source.py)\\ndef norm(s):\\n    s = s.replace('\\\\xa0', ' ')\\n    s = re.sub(r'\\\\s+', ' ', s)\\n    return s.strip()\\n\\nstart_comp = end_comp = None\\nfor i, p in enumerate(parts):\\n    t = norm(re.sub(r'<[^>]+>', ' ', p))\\n    if start_comp is None and 'Background of the Merger.' in t and i > 5:\\n        start_comp = i\\n    if 'Reasons for the Merger and Recommendation of our Board' in t and start_comp is not None:\\n        end_comp = i\\n        break\\nraw = []\\nfor ci in range(start_comp, end_comp + 1):\\n    folio = folios[ci]\\n    soup = BeautifulSoup(parts[ci], 'lxml')\\n    for p in soup.find_all('p'):\\n        t = norm(p.get_text(' '))\\n        if not t or t == 'Table of Contents' or re.fullmatch(r'[\\\\d\\\\s]+', t):\\n            continue\\n        if 'Reasons for the Merger and Recommendation' in t:\\n            break\\n        if t in ('Background of the Merger', 'Background of the Merger.', 'THE MERGER'):\\n            continue\\n        raw.append({'page': folio, 'text': t})\\nmerged = []\\nfor item in raw:\\n    if merged and re.match(r'^[a-z0-9$]', item['text']) and not merged[-1]['text'].rstrip().endswith(('.', ';', ':', ',')):\\n        merged[-1]['text'] = merged[-1]['text'].rstrip() + ' ' + item['text']\\n        if merged[-1]['page'] != item['page']:\\n            merged[-1]['page'] = f\\\"{merged[-1]['page']}-{item['page']}\\\"\\n    else:\\n        merged.append(dict(item))\\nPARAS = []\\nfor i, item in enumerate(merged, 1):\\n    PARAS.append({'id': f'P-{i:03d}', 'section': 'THE MERGER — Background of the Merger',\\n                  'page': item['page'], 'text': item['text']})\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- X passages\\nX_DEFS = [\\n ('X-001', 'Summary Term Sheet', 5,\\n  'If the merger is completed, at the effective time of the merger, each outstanding share of Mac-Gray common stock',\\n  'We refer to this amount in this proxy statement as the merger consideration.'),\\n ('X-002', 'Questions and Answers', 13,\\n  'The merger consideration of $21.25 per share to be received by Mac-Gray stockholders represents:',\\n  'an approximately 44% premium to the $14.72 closing price of our common stock on October 11, 2013'),\\n ('X-003', 'Summary Term Sheet', 5,\\n  'The Mac-Gray Board of Directors formed a special committee of six disinterested and independent directors',\\n  'recommends that Mac-Gray stockholders adopt the merger agreement.'),\\n ('X-004', 'Summary Term Sheet', 6,\\n  'The merger agreement does not contain any condition to the obligations of the Buyer Entities or Merger Subsidiary relating to the receipt of financing',\\n  'dated as of October 14, 2013, which we refer to as the Pamplona commitment letter.'),\\n ('X-005', 'Summary Term Sheet', 10,\\n  'Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances',\\n  'which we refer to as the Parent termination fee.'),\\n ('X-006', 'Summary Term Sheet', 11,\\n  'As of November 27, 2013, the record date for the special meeting, the stockholders of Mac-Gray that entered into the voting agreements collectively owned approximately 15%',\\n  'entitled to vote at the special meeting.'),\\n ('X-007', 'Questions and Answers', 13,\\n  'The closing sale price of a share of Mac-Gray common stock on the New York Stock Exchange on November 27, 2013 was $21.30.',\\n  'was $21.30.'),\\n ('X-008', 'Questions and Answers', 14,\\n  'We currently expect the merger to be completed in January 2014.',\\n  'we cannot assure you that we will complete the merger on this schedule or at all.'),\\n ('X-009', 'Questions and Answers', 15,\\n  'As of the record date, there were approximately 14,758,306 shares of Mac-Gray common stock issued and outstanding held collectively by approximately 104 stockholders of record.',\\n  'stockholders of record.'),\\n ('X-010', 'The Special Meeting — Solicitation of Proxies', 23,\\n  'we expect to retain MacKenzie Partners, Inc. to assist in the solicitation for a fee of approximately $15,000',\\n  'indemnification against certain losses, costs and expenses.'),\\n ('X-011', 'Proposals Submitted to Mac-Gray Stockholders', 24,\\n  'Under applicable law, we cannot complete the merger without the vote of a majority of the outstanding shares',\\n  'it will have the same effect as a vote against the proposal to adopt the merger agreement.'),\\n ('X-012', 'Proposals Submitted to Mac-Gray Stockholders', 24,\\n  'Section 951 of the Dodd-Frank Act and Rule 14a-21(c) under the Exchange Act require that Mac-Gray seek a non-binding advisory vote',\\n  'in connection with the merger.'),\\n ('X-013', 'The Companies', 26,\\n  'Mac-Gray Corporation is the second largest laundry facilities management contractor in the United States.',\\n  'through our product sales division.'),\\n ('X-014', 'The Merger — Reasons for the Merger', 43,\\n  'the fact that the $21.25 per share to be paid as the consideration in the merger represents a premium of approximately 36%',\\n  'the last trading day prior to the date our Board of Directors approved the merger agreement;'),\\n ('X-015', 'The Merger — Reasons for the Merger', 43,\\n  'the Pamplona commitment letter, pursuant to which Pamplona has committed to fund up to $594 million',\\n  'awarded to Mac-Gray in certain circumstances involving litigation brought pursuant to the merger agreement;'),\\n ('X-016', 'The Merger — Opinion of Mac-Gray\\\\u2019s Financial Advisor', 45,\\n  'On October 14, 2013, at a meeting of the Special Committee held to evaluate the merger, BofA Merrill Lynch delivered to the Special Committee an oral opinion',\\n  'was fair, from a financial point of view, to such holders.'),\\n ('X-017', 'The Merger — Opinion of Mac-Gray\\\\u2019s Financial Advisor', 48,\\n  'This analysis indicated the following approximate implied per share equity value reference ranges for Mac-Gray',\\n  '21.25'),\\n ('X-018', 'Projected Financial Information', 53,\\n  'The Projections were prepared in June 2013 in the context of the business, economic, regulatory, market and financial conditions that existed at that time, and have not been updated',\\n  'that was not anticipated at the time the projections were prepared.'),\\n ('X-019', 'Financing of the Merger', 58,\\n  'The merger agreement does not contain any condition to the obligations of the Buyer Entities or Merger Subsidiary relating to the receipt of financing by the Buyer Entities.',\\n  'relating to the receipt of financing by the Buyer Entities.'),\\n ('X-020', 'Financing of the Merger', 59,\\n  'for purposes of funding the merger consideration an aggregate of $594 million of capital (the Pamplona commitment amount)',\\n  'provided further that the liability of Buyer Entities shall be unlimited).'),\\n ('X-021', 'The Merger Agreement — The Merger Consideration', 60,\\n  'Immediately prior to the effective time of the merger, each share of Mac-Gray common stock outstanding immediately prior to the effective time of the merger will be canceled and converted into the right to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest, other than:',\\n  'without interest, other than:'),\\n ('X-022', 'The Merger Agreement — Non-Solicitation; Competing Acquisition Proposals', 69,\\n  'Mac-Gray has agreed that neither Mac-Gray nor any of its subsidiaries will, nor will Mac-Gray authorize or knowingly permit',\\n  'be returned or destroyed.'),\\n ('X-023', 'The Merger Agreement — Non-Solicitation; Competing Acquisition Proposals', 69,\\n  'Notwithstanding the restrictions described above, if, prior to the adoption of the merger agreement by Mac-Gray stockholders, Mac-Gray receives an unsolicited bona fide acquisition',\\n  'the failure to take such action would be reasonably likely to be inconsistent with the directors\\\\u2019 fiduciary duties under applicable laws'),\\n ('X-024', 'The Merger Agreement — Termination Fees and Expenses', 80,\\n  'then Mac-Gray will pay to Parent the $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee',\\n  'on the date that is the first to occur of Mac-Gray'),\\n ('X-025', 'The Merger Agreement — Termination Fees and Expenses', 81,\\n  'then Parent will pay Mac-Gray the $15 million Parent termination fee, by wire transfer of same-day funds on the first business day following such termination.',\\n  'first business day following such termination.'),\\n ('X-026', 'The Voting Agreements', 82,\\n  'In connection with the execution of the merger agreement, certain stockholders entered into voting agreements with Parent. Approximately 15% of the outstanding Mac-Gray shares on the record date for the special meeting are subject to the voting agreements.',\\n  'are subject to the voting agreements.'),\\n ('X-027', 'Regulatory Matters', 85,\\n  'Parent and Mac-Gray each filed pre-merger notifications with the U.S. antitrust authorities pursuant to the HSR Act on October 29, 2013',\\n  'the waiting period expired on November 27, 2013.'),\\n ('X-028', 'Litigation Related to the Merger', 85,\\n  'On November 21, 2013, a putative class action lawsuit was filed',\\n  'attorneys\\\\u2019 and expert fees and costs.'),\\n ('X-029', 'Current Market Price of Common Stock', 89,\\n  'The following table sets forth the closing sale prices per share of Mac-Gray common stock',\\n  '21.30'),\\n ('X-030', 'Security Ownership of Management and Certain Beneficial Owners', 91,\\n  'Stewart G. MacDonald, Jr.(3)(4)(5)',\\n  'Polaris Capital Management, Inc.(12) 918,488 6.22 %'),\\n]\\n\\ndef find_passage(start, end):\\n    for folio, text in comp_text:\\n        i = text.find(start)\\n        if i >= 0:\\n            j = text.find(end, i + len(start))\\n            if j >= 0:\\n                return folio, text[i:j + len(end)]\\n    return None, None\\n\\nXPASS = []\\nfor xid, section, page, start, end in X_DEFS:\\n    folio, txt = find_passage(start, end)\\n    if txt is None:\\n        print('X PASSAGE NOT FOUND:', xid, '| start:', start[:60], '| end:', end[:60])\\n        continue\\n    XPASS.append({'id': xid, 'section': section, 'page': page, 'text': txt})\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- quote resolution\\ndef ascii_norm(s):\\n    s = s.replace('\\\\u2019', \\\"'\\\").replace('\\\\u2018', \\\"'\\\").replace('\\\\u201c', '\\\"').replace('\\\\u201d', '\\\"')\\n    s = s.replace('\\\\u2014', '--').replace('\\\\u2013', '-').replace('\\\\xa0', ' ')\\n    s = re.sub(r'\\\\s+', ' ', s)\\n    return s.strip()\\n\\ndef build_index(text):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Map normalized positions to raw positions.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    norm_chars, pos = [], []\\n    i = 0\\n    while i < len(text):\\n        ch = text[i]\\n        if ch.isspace():\\n            j = i\\n            while j < len(text) and text[j].isspace():\\n                j += 1\\n            norm_chars.append(' ')\\n            pos.append((i, j))\\n            i = j\\n        else:\\n            c = ch\\n            if c in '\\\\u2019\\\\u2018':\\n                c = \\\"'\\\"\\n            elif c in '\\\\u201c\\\\u201d':\\n                c = '\\\"'\\n            elif c == '\\\\u2014':\\n                c = '--'\\n                pos.append((i, i + 1))\\n                norm_chars.append('-')\\n                pos[-1] = (i, i + 1)\\n                norm_chars.append('-')\\n                i += 1\\n                continue\\n            elif c == '\\\\u2013':\\n                c = '-'\\n            norm_chars.append(c)\\n            pos.append((i, i + 1))\\n            i += 1\\n    return ''.join(norm_chars), pos\\n\\ndef resolve(raw_text, quote):\\n    nq = ascii_norm(quote)\\n    nt, pos = build_index(raw_text)\\n    k = nt.find(nq)\\n    if k < 0:\\n        return None\\n    start = pos[k][0]\\n    end = pos[k + len(nq) - 1][1]\\n    return raw_text[start:end]\\n\\nSOURCES = {p['id']: p for p in PARAS}\\nfor x in XPASS:\\n    SOURCES[x['id']] = x\\n\\ndef q(source_id, quote):\\n    src = SOURCES.get(source_id)\\n    if src is None:\\n        return None, f'unknown source {source_id}'\\n    raw = resolve(src['text'], quote)\\n    if raw is None:\\n        return None, f'quote not found in {source_id}: {quote[:90]}'\\n    return raw, None\\n\\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------- ledger rows\\nD = date\\nROWS = []\\nADD = ROWS.append\\n\\ndef row(key, when, who, what, process, round_, type_, terms, formality, cond_level,\\n        why_parts, count=None, date_from=None, date_to=None, date_basis=None, date_method=None,\\n        price_low=None, price_high=None, price_kind=None, price_origin=None, currency=None,\\n        all_cash=None, cash_close=None, cond_detail=None, due_date=None, deadline_treatment=None,\\n        round_finality=None, decided_by=None, exit_reason=None, outcome_basis=None, page=None,\\n        related=None, review=None):\\n    ADD(dict(key=key, when=when, who=who, what=what, process=process, round=round_, type=type_,\\n             terms=terms, formality=formality, cond_level=cond_level, why_parts=why_parts,\\n             count=count, date_from=date_from, date_to=date_to, date_basis=date_basis,\\n             date_method=date_method, price_low=price_low, price_high=price_high,\\n             price_kind=price_kind, price_origin=price_origin, currency=currency,\\n             all_cash=all_cash, cash_close=cash_close, cond_detail=cond_detail,\\n             due_date=due_date, deadline_treatment=deadline_treatment,\\n             round_finality=round_finality, decided_by=decided_by, exit_reason=exit_reason,\\n             outcome_basis=outcome_basis, page=page, related=related, review=review))\\n\\nCC = 'Fin: {}; DD required: {}; DD open: {}; Excl: {}'\\n\\n# 1\\nrow('boA2012_engage', '10/23/2012', 'BofA Merrill Lynch (financial adviser, Mac-Gray)', 'Adviser engaged',\\n    None, 0, None,\\n    'Engaged by Mac-Gray for the 2011-2012 Discussions — the possible acquisition of CSC by Mac-Gray (target-as-acquirer mandate); pre-process context, not a sale of Mac-Gray.',\\n    None, None,\\n    [('Stated engagement', [('P-002', 'Mac-Gray engaged BofA Merrill Lynch on October 23, 2012')])],\\n    date_from=D(2012,10,23), date_to=D(2012,10,23), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\\n    page=27, related='R006; R007 (later mandates)')\\n\\n# 2\\nrow('apr5', '04/05/2013', 'Mac-Gray Board of Directors', 'Target sale decision', 1, 0, None,\\n    'Board reviewed the completed CSC sale to Pamplona and industry M&A activity; authorized management to work with BofA Merrill Lynch on transactional opportunities, including with strategic party \\\"Party A\\\"; deferred further consideration to the 05/09/2013 meeting.',\\n    None, None,\\n    [('Stated decision', [('P-003', 'authorized Mac-Gray management to work with BofA Merrill Lynch to explore transactional opportunities that might be available to Mac-Gray, including opportunities with another strategic party, whom we refer to as Party A')]),\\n     ('Deferral', [('P-003', 'The Board also determined to further consider Mac-Gray\\\\u2019s strategic alternatives at its meeting scheduled for May 9, 2013')])],\\n    date_from=D(2013,4,5), date_to=D(2013,4,5), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\\n    page=27, related='R011 (rejected R1 boundary candidate)', review='Q1')\\n\\n# 3\\nrow('apr8', '04/08/2013', 'Party A (potential strategic acquirer)', 'Target interest', 1, 0, 'Strategic',\\n    'BofA Merrill Lynch, on the Board\\\\u2019s instruction, telephoned Party A about a possible business combination; Party A indicated it might consider one. First sale-related contact with Party A. Party A is inside the 15 potential strategic buyers contacted in the June 24 wave (R012, Count 15), which already counts it; Count 0 avoids double counting.',\\n    None, None,\\n    [('Stated contact and receptiveness', [('P-004', 'representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Board, telephoned a representative of Party A to discuss generally a possible business combination between Party A and Mac-Gray. During this call, the representative of Party A indicated that Party A might consider a business combination with Mac-Gray')]),\\n     ('Party A is one of the 15 strategic parties in the June 24 wave', [('P-022', '50 parties, including CSC and Pamplona, who together we refer to as CSC/Pamplona, and Party A, to solicit potential interest in a transaction with Mac-Gray, 15 of which were potential strategic buyers')])],\\n    count=0, date_from=D(2013,4,8), date_to=D(2013,4,8), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\\n    page=27, related='R012 (cohort contains Party A); R009 (Party A June 21 proposal)', review='Q3')\\n\\n# 4\\nrow('may9_board', '05/09/2013', 'Mac-Gray Board of Directors', 'Target decision', 1, 0, None,\\n    'Board discussed whether to approach third parties about a potential sale; formed the Transaction Committee (Thomas Bullock and Paul Daoust) to recommend and engage a financial adviser; concluded to revisit the review at its next meeting.',\\n    None, None,\\n    [('Stated discussion', [('P-006', 'the Board engaged in a general discussion concerning whether it might be advisable to approach and discuss a potential sale transaction with third parties at this time as a means by which to deliver value to the stockholders of Mac-Gray')]),\\n     ('Transaction Committee formed', [('P-007', 'the Board formed a transaction committee at this meeting, which we refer to as the Transaction Committee, and appointed Thomas Bullock and Paul Daoust, both independent directors, to serve as its members')]),\\n     ('Deferral', [('P-007', 'The Board concluded that it would discuss the review of strategic alternatives, including engaging in a potential sale process, at its next meeting')])],\\n    date_from=D(2013,5,9), date_to=D(2013,5,9), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\\n    page=28, related='R007', review='Q1')\\n\\n# 5\\nrow('goodwin', '05/09/2013', 'Goodwin Procter LLP (outside legal counsel, Mac-Gray)', 'Adviser service observed',\\n    1, 0, None,\\n    'Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, first shown acting on the strategic-alternatives mandate at the May 9, 2013 Board meeting (fiduciary-duty overview); engagement date and engagement letter not disclosed.',\\n    None, None,\\n    [('Earliest observed service', [('P-005', 'representatives from BofA Merrill Lynch and Goodwin Procter LLP, outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray, were also in attendance for all or portions of the meeting')]),\\n     ('Fiduciary overview and further service', [('P-007', 'a representative of Goodwin Procter provided an overview of the Board\\\\u2019s fiduciary duties')])],\\n    date_from=D(2013,5,9), date_to=D(2013,5,9), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\\n    page=27, related='R004')\\n\\n# 6\\nrow('boA2012_end', '05/15/2013', 'BofA Merrill Lynch (financial adviser, Mac-Gray)', 'Adviser ended',\\n    None, 0, None,\\n    'Termination of the 10/23/2012 engagement for the 2011-2012 Discussions: Transaction Committee determined to terminate on 05/14/2013; letter sent 05/15/2013. BofA Merrill Lynch was simultaneously a candidate for the new strategic-alternatives mandate.',\\n    None, None,\\n    [('Stated determination and letter', [('P-009', 'the Transaction Committee determined to terminate BofA Merrill Lynch\\\\u2019s engagement letter entered into for purposes of the 2011-2012 Discussions'),\\n                                          ('P-010', 'On May 15, 2013, Mac-Gray sent a letter to BofA Merrill Lynch terminating their engagement in connection with the 2011-2012 Discussions')])],\\n    date_from=D(2013,5,15), date_to=D(2013,5,15), date_basis='Reported day', date_method='Reported',\\n    page=29, related='R001; R007')\\n\\n# 7\\nrow('boA_engage', '05/30/2013 (Board approval) \\\\u2013 05/31/2013 (engagement letter)',\\n    'BofA Merrill Lynch (financial adviser, Mac-Gray)', 'Adviser engaged', 1, 0, None,\\n    'Board unanimously approved engaging BofA Merrill Lynch as financial adviser for the strategic-alternatives review (three banks invited 05/10/2013; presentations 05/22 and 05/29/2013); engagement letter entered 05/31/2013, including a restriction on BofA Merrill Lynch sourcing buyer acquisition financing without Mac-Gray\\\\u2019s prior written consent.',\\n    None, None,\\n    [('Selection process', [('P-008', 'determined to invite three nationally recognized investment banks to submit proposals')]),\\n     ('Board approval', [('P-014', 'Based on the recommendation of the Transaction Committee, the Board unanimously approved the engagement of BofA Merrill Lynch on the terms discussed at this meeting')]),\\n     ('Engagement letter and restriction', [('P-016', 'On May 31, 2013, Mac-Gray entered into an engagement letter with BofA Merrill Lynch with respect to the Board\\\\u2019s undertaking a review of strategic alternatives, including a potential sale process, and in which BofA Merrill 