 Lynch (financial adviser, Mac-Gray) | Adviser engaged | proc 1 round 0 type None\n   Terms: Board unanimously approved engaging BofA Merrill Lynch as financial adviser for the strategic-alternatives review (three banks invited 05/10/2013; presentations 05/22 and 05/29/2013); engagement letter entered 05/31/2013, including a restriction on BofA Merrill Lynch sourcing buyer acquisition financing without Mac-Gray’s prior written consent.\n   Why: — Selection process: \"determined to invite three nationally recognized investment banks to submit proposals\" (p.28).— Board approval: \"Based on the recommendation of the Transaction Committee, the Board unanimously approved the engagement of BofA Merrill Lynch on the terms discussed at this meeting\" (p.29).— Engagement letter and restriction: \"On May 31, 2013, Mac-Gray entered into an engagement letter with BofA Merrill Lynch with respect to the Board's undertaking a review of strategic alternatives, including a potential sale process, and in which BofA Merrill Lynch agreed not to engage as a possible source of new acquisition financing for any potential buyers in connection with any such sale process without Mac-Gray's prior written consent\" (p.30). Engagement timing: Board approval 05/30/2013; engagement letter 05/31/2013 (Working date assigned to the first day; Assigned: bound).\n   Source: P-008; P-014; P-016 | Page: 29 | Review: Q1 | Related: R004; R006\n\n### R008 #8 | 05/30/2013 | Moab Partners, L.P. and affiliates (activist stockholder); Mac-Gray | Activist involvement | proc 1 round 0 type None\n   Terms: Moab’s proxy contest: Moab-nominated Michael M. Rothenberg (Moab co-founder and General Partner) and James E. Hyman elected as directors in place of incumbent nominees; Board size reduced to seven; Moab held approximately 9% of shares. Rothenberg was later excluded from the sale-process evaluation because Moab sought a possible equity rollover (R010, R016).\n   Why: — Stated election and proxy contest: \"the Mac-Gray stockholders elected as directors Michael M. Rothenberg and James E. Hyman, candidates nominated by Mac-Gray's stockholder, Moab Partners, L.P. and certain of its affiliates, which we refer collectively to as Moab. Mac-Gray and Moab engaged in a proxy contest leading up to the annual meeting\" (p.29).— Moab stake at the June 12 orientation: \"At the time of this meeting, Moab beneficially owned approximately 9% of Mac-Gray's outstanding common stock\" (p.30).\n   Source: P-015; P-017 | Page: 29 | Review: None | Related: R010; R016\n\n### R009 #9 | 06/21/2013 | Party A (potential strategic acquirer) | Bid | proc 1 round 0 type Strategic\n   Terms: Unsolicited all-cash proposal to purchase Mac-Gray at $17.00–$19.00 per share. Made before any NDA or substantive diligence access (NDA signed 08/05/2013, R027); first contact was the 04/08/2013 call (R003). Still standing when round 1 was evaluated, so Party A counts as a round-1 participant although this bid row sits in round 0.\n   Formality: Informal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: not stated\n   Count=1 Price=17-19 kind=Bidder range origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n   Why: — Stated proposal: \"On June 21, 2013, Party A submitted an unsolicited proposal to the Mac-Gray Board of Directors offering to purchase Mac-Gray for an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $19.00 per share, which we refer to as the Party A June 21 proposal\" (p.30).— No formal signal and no substantive access yet: \"outside counsel to Party A and representatives of Goodwin Procter negotiated the terms of a confidentiality and standstill agreement, but did not come to agreement on the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions\" (p.33). Formality: preliminary exploratory proposal, no supported formal signal — Informal. Conditions: Heavy by context — made before any NDA or substantive diligence access.\n   Source: P-018; P-030 | Page: 30 | Review: Q4 | Related: R003 (first contact); R012/R011 (round-1 participation); R027 (NDA)\n\n### R010 #10 | 06/24/2013 | Mac-Gray Board of Directors | Target decision | proc 1 round 0 type None\n   Terms: Board established the Special Committee of six independent and disinterested directors (Bullock, Daoust, Hyman, Meagher, Percelay, Robinson; Bullock chairman) and excluded Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg from the Board’s evaluation of strategic alternatives because they could be asked to partner with a potential acquirer; Transaction Committee became a sub-committee.\n   Why: — Stated establishment: \"the Board then established the Special Committee, comprised of the six independent and disinterested members of the Board (namely, Mr. Bullock, Mr. Daoust, Mr. Hyman, William F. Meagher, Bruce A. Percelay and Alastair G. Robinson)\" (p.30).— Exclusions: \"the Board decided, and Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg agreed, that it would be appropriate to exclude Mr. MacDonald and Mr. Rothenberg from the Board's evaluation of strategic alternatives and any negotiations with third parties that might take place\" (p.30).\n   Source: P-019 | Page: 30 | Review: Q1 | Related: R011\n\n### R011 #11 | 06/24/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee | Round opened | proc 1 round 1 type None\n   Terms: R1 anchor: Special Committee’s 06/24/2013 determination to consider a potential sale and to approach 50 parties (15 potential strategic buyers; 35 potential financial buyers), executed by BofA Merrill Lynch outreach beginning within days (first NDA 06/28/2013). Other candidate anchors: R002 (04/05/2013 authorization), R003 (04/08/2013 Party A call), R007 (05/31/2013 engagement letter), R012–R013 (first outreach wave), R014 (06/28/2013 first NDA). Purpose: solicit preliminary indications of interest, with packages furnished to NDA signers and IOIs instructed by 07/23/2013 (R017). Round-1 participant set: Party A (round-0 proposal standing, R009), Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona.\n   Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=Not final outb=None by=None reason=None\n   Why: — Stated determination and approach scope: \"the Special Committee concluded that it would be in the best interests of stockholders to consider a potential sale of Mac-Gray\" (p.31). \"the Special Committee determined to approach a total of 50 parties, including CSC and Pamplona, who together we refer to as CSC/Pamplona, and Party A, to solicit potential interest in a transaction with Mac-Gray, 15 of which were potential strategic buyers and 35 of which were potential financial buyers, including private equity firms\" (p.31-32).\n   Source: P-021; P-022 | Page: 31 | Review: Q1 | Related: R009; R010; R002; R003; R007; R012–R014\n\n### R012 #12 | after 06/24/2013; late June through August 2013 (individual contact dates not disclosed) | Mac-Gray (via BofA Merrill Lynch) → 15 potential strategic buyers | Contact | proc 1 round 1 type Strategic\n   Terms: Outreach to the 15 potential strategic buyers identified at the June 24 Special Committee meeting, in accordance with its directives. Parties contacted include Party A (first contacted 04/08/2013, R003 — Count 0 there) and CSC/Pamplona. Count 15 = the cohort as described; treated as a single contact wave.\n   Count=15 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n   Why: — Stated outreach: \"During the next several weeks, in accordance with the directives of the Special Committee, BofA Merrill Lynch contacted the strategic and financial parties identified at the June 24th Special Committee meeting\" (p.32).— Cohort size and composition: \"15 of which were potential strategic buyers\" (p.31-32). Working date convention: the wave began after the 06/24/2013 directive; individual contact dates are not disclosed (Assigned: bound to the first day of the reported window).\n   Source: P-023; P-022 | Page: 32 | Review: Q3; Q7 | Related: R003 (Party A, Count 0 there); R011; R013\n\n### R013 #13 | after 06/24/2013; late June through August 2013 (individual contact dates not disclosed) | Mac-Gray (via BofA Merrill Lynch) → 35 potential financial buyers | Contact | proc 1 round 1 type Financial\n   Terms: Outreach to the 35 potential financial buyers including private equity firms, in accordance with the Special Committee’s directives. Includes Party B and Party C, later recorded individually at the NDA stage. Count 35 = the cohort as described.\n   Count=35 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n   Why: — Stated outreach: \"BofA Merrill Lynch contacted the strategic and financial parties identified at the June 24th Special Committee meeting\" (p.32).— Cohort size and composition: \"35 of which were potential financial buyers, including private equity firms\" (p.31-32). Working date convention: the wave began after the 06/24/2013 directive; individual contact dates are not disclosed (Assigned: bound to the first day of the reported window).\n   Source: P-023; P-022 | Page: 32 | Review: Q3; Q7 | Related: R011; R012\n\n### R014 #14 | 06/28/2013 | Party B (financial bidder) | NDA signed | proc 1 round 1 type Financial\n   Terms: Executed a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray on Mac-Gray’s form (individually negotiated; no material variances) and received the informational package; standstill carried a sunset allowing confidential proposals on announcement of a business combination or change of control.\n   Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n   Why: — Stated execution and package: \"Later on June 28, 2013, Party B, entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party B with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest\" (p.32).— Form and standstill terms: \"entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray on a form provided by Mac-Gray, the terms of which were individually negotiated with potential bidders, but did not vary materially from the form provided\" (p.32).\n   Source: P-025; P-023 | Page: 32 | Review: None | Related: None\n\n### R015 #15 | 06/30/2013 | Party C (financial bidder) | NDA signed | proc 1 round 1 type Financial\n   Terms: Executed a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and received the informational package on the same basis as the other signers.\n   Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /home/uctpiaj/work && python3 - <<'EOF' > /tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt\\nimport openpyxl\\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook('extraction/mac-gray.xlsx')\\nws = wb['Deal ledger']\\nH = {ws.cell(row=1, column=i).value: i for i in range(1, ws.max_column+1)}\\nfor r in range(2, ws.max_row+1):\\n    def g(h): return ws.cell(row=r, column=H[h]).value\\n    print(f\\\"### {g('Row id')} #{g('#')} | {g('When')} | {g('Who')} | {g('What happened')} | proc {g('Process')} round {g('Round')} type {g('Type')}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"   Terms: {g('Terms or outcome')}\\\")\\n    if g('Formality') or g('Conditions level'):\\n        print(f\\\"   Formality: {g('Formality')} | Conditions: {g('Conditions level')} | detail: {g('Conditions detail')}\\\")\\n    if g('Count') is not None or g('Price low') is not None or g('Due date') is not None or g('Round finality') or g('Deadline treatment') or g('Outcome basis'):\\n        print(f\\\"   Count={g('Count')} Price={g('Price low')}-{g('Price high')} kind={g('Price kind')} origin={g('Price origin')} cur={g('Currency')} cash={g('All cash')}/{g('Cash at closing')} due={g('Due date')} treat={g('Deadline treatment')} finality={g('Round finality')} outb={g('Outcome basis')} by={g('Decided by')} reason={g('Exit reason')}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"   Why: {g('Why and evidence')}\\\")\\n    print(f\\\"   Source: {g('Source')} | Page: {g('Page')} | Review: {g('Review')} | Related: {g('Related rows')}\\\")\\n    print()\\nEOF\\nwc -l /tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt; sed -n '1,80p' /tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825285844,"end":1789825287479}}}}
