{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825291099,"sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e692a4001Vf0BLE6KDZPesn","sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","messageID":"msg_0b9e68544001bjmFayTI4SOLfr","type":"tool","id":"call_00_PItKrMGAo7YgncaDYGXF7226","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt","offset":80,"limit":130},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt, lines 80-209\n80:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n81:    Why: — Stated execution and package: \"On June 30, 2013, Party C entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party C with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest\" (p.32).\n82:    Source: P-026 | Page: 32 | Review: None | Related: None\n83: \n84: ### R016 #16 | 07/06/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee; Moab Partners (via Mr. Rothenberg); CSC/Pamplona | Material process update | proc 1 round 1 type None\n85:    Terms: Moab rollover request denied as premature: Mr. Rothenberg had asked that CSC/Pamplona be allowed to share bid and evaluation material with Moab, with Moab exclusively engaged with CSC/Pamplona; the Special Committee denied exclusivity so that Moab’s stake could remain available as capital for other bidders, and said rollover discussions would be permitted at a later stage.\n86:    Why: — Stated request: \"Mr. Rothenberg also informed Goodwin Procter that Pamplona would be requesting that any confidentiality agreement CSC/Pamplona execute with Mac-Gray permit CSC and Pamplona to discuss their bid and evaluation material with Moab, with Moab agreeing to exclusively engage with CSC/Pamplona\" (p.32).— Stated denial and rationale: \"the Special Committee decided to deny the exclusivity request at this stage of the process so that the potential equity rollover of Moab's shares could be available as a source of capital for other potential bidders\" (p.32-33).— Deferral: \"it was premature for Mac-Gray to permit Moab to engage in equity rollover discussions with any party, including CSC/Pamplona, but that such discussions would be permitted at a later stage of the sale process\" (p.32-33).\n87:    Source: P-027; P-028 | Page: 32 | Review: Q6 | Related: R049 (resolution); R010\n88: \n89: ### R017 #17 | between 06/28/2013 and 07/23/2013 (communication date not disclosed) | Mac-Gray (informational package) → NDA signers | Deadline set | proc 1 round 1 type None\n90:    Terms: Informational-package letter instructed NDA signers to submit preliminary indications of interest by 07/23/2013, addressing valuation, sources and structures of financing, material conditions (including required approvals) and due-diligence focus areas. Communication date not disclosed: the package was furnished to each party as it signed; first signer 06/28/2013.\n91:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-07-23 00:00:00 treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n92:    Why: — Stated instruction: \"Parties that had entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with Mac-Gray were furnished an informational package for the purpose of providing potential bidders with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest, which they were instructed to submit by July 23, 2013\" (p.32).— Requested proposal content: \"The letter requested that the proposals address, among other things, valuation, sources and structures of financing, material conditions, including required approvals, and focus areas for due diligence\" (p.32). Working date convention: communication window 06/28–07/23/2013; midpoint used as a sort key (Assigned: midpoint).\n93:    Source: P-023 | Page: 32 | Review: Q2; Q7 | Related: R020 (due date reached)\n94: \n95: ### R018 #18 | 07/11/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder) | NDA signed | proc 1 round 1 type Strategic\n96:    Terms: CSC and Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray jointly (one bidder unit) and received the informational package.\n97:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n98:    Why: — Stated execution and package: \"On July 11, 2013, CSC/Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and were provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing CSC/Pamplona with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest\" (p.33).\n99:    Source: P-029 | Page: 33 | Review: None | Related: None\n100: \n101: ### R019 #19 | late June through late August 2013 (individual dates not disclosed) | 16 remaining financial bidders (residual cohort) | NDA signed | proc 1 round 1 type Financial\n102:    Terms: Residual cohort: 20 potential bidders signed confidentiality and standstill agreements over roughly two months; four are individually recorded (Party A 08/05/2013, Party B 06/28/2013, Party C 06/30/2013, CSC/Pamplona 07/11/2013) and the remaining 16 signers are represented by this one cohort row. The cohort’s Working date is moved earlier to 07/23/2013 (inside its window) so that it precedes its inferred non-submission row (R021) — Assigned: sequence.\n103:    Count=16 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n104:    Why: — Stated total and split: \"Over the next two months a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray\" (p.32). Working date convention: the cohort’s signing window (late June to late August) straddles the 07/23/2013 solicitation; the date was moved earlier inside that window so the entry row precedes its inferred non-submission outcome (Assigned: sequence).\n105:    Source: P-023 | Page: 32 | Review: Q3; Q7 | Related: R014; R015; R018; R027; R021 (inferred non-submission)\n106: \n107: ### R020 #20 | 07/23/2013 | N/A — solicitation deadline | Deadline | proc 1 round 1 type None\n108:    Terms: Preliminary-indication due date reached. CSC/Pamplona submitted on 07/23/2013; Party B submitted 07/24/2013 and Party C 07/24–07/25/2013, and the Special Committee reviewed all of them on 07/25/2013 with no revision of the due date. Treatment: Late bids accepted.\n109:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-07-23 00:00:00 treat=Late bids accepted finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n110:    Why: — Due date: \"instructed to submit by July 23, 2013\" (p.32).— Late submissions considered: \"On July 25, 2013, the Board held a regularly scheduled in-person meeting\" (p.33). \"representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch reviewed the preliminary indications of interest received from Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona as well as the Party A June 21 proposal\" (p.33).\n111:    Source: P-023; P-033 | Page: 32 | Review: Q2 | Related: R017\n112: \n113: ### R021 #21 | by 07/23/2013 (solicitation due date passed with no submission) | 16 remaining financial bidders (residual cohort) | Did not submit | proc 1 round 1 type Financial\n114:    Terms: Inferred: residual — 20 NDA signers − 4 individually recorded signers (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) = 16 remaining signers, all financial; none is reported to have submitted a July 23 indication. Base assumes each of the 20 signers was covered by the July 23 solicitation; if any signed later than that deadline, the non-submitting set is smaller (flagged in Q3). Inferred from arithmetic only — no dates, motives or identities inferred.\n115:    Count=16 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=Inferred: residual by=Unknown reason=Not stated\n116:    Why: — Base population: \"a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray\" (p.32).— Continuing set named at the next transition: \"reach out to each of the four interested bidders and arrange management meetings\" (p.33-34).— Solicitation due date: \"instructed to submit by July 23, 2013\" (p.32). Outcome basis: arithmetic residual only — no dates, motives, identities or voluntary withdrawal inferred. Count = stated base − accounted participants.\n117:    Source: P-023; P-034 | Page: 32 | Review: Q3 | Related: R019 (entry); R020\n118: \n119: ### R022 #22 | 07/23/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 1 type Strategic\n120:    Terms: Preliminary indication of interest: all-cash $18.50 per share, submitted on the 07/23/2013 due date after a preliminary review (07/11–07/23) but before data-room or management access; financing not described at this stage.\n121:    Formality: Informal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n122:    Count=1 Price=18.5-18.5 kind=Point origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/18.5 due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n123:    Why: — Stated indication: \"On July 23, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share\" (p.33).— Substantive access not yet given: \"Between July 11, 2013 and July 23, 2013, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona engaged in a preliminary review of Mac-Gray and the potential acquisition opportunity\" (p.33). Conditions: Heavy by context — preliminary indication made before data-room or management access; financing not yet described.\n124:    Source: P-031; P-030 | Page: 33 | Review: Q4 | Related: R030 (Sept 9 revision); R037; R042\n125: \n126: ### R023 #23 | 07/24/2013 | Party B (financial bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 1 type Financial\n127:    Terms: Preliminary indication of interest: all-cash $17.00–$18.00 per share, submitted one day after the 07/23/2013 instruction and considered at the 07/25/2013 Special Committee meeting.\n128:    Formality: Informal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n129:    Count=1 Price=17-18 kind=Bidder range origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n130:    Why: — Stated indication: \"On July 24, 2013, Party B submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $17.00 to $18.00 per share\" (p.33). Conditions: Heavy by context — preliminary indication before substantive diligence access, and no financing commitment reported.\n131:    Source: P-032 | Page: 33 | Review: Q4 | Related: R031 (Sept 9 revision)\n132: \n133: ### R024 #24 | 07/24/2013 (oral indication) – 07/25/2013 (written indication) | Party C (financial bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 1 type Financial\n134:    Terms: One bid, two communications: an oral preliminary indication on 07/24/2013 at $15.00–$17.00 per share, then a written indication on 07/25/2013 at $16.00–$16.50 per share. Recorded as a single bid under the one-communication convention; the written range is recorded in the price cells and both values are stated here. All-cash; financing not described.\n135:    Formality: Informal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n136:    Count=1 Price=16-16.5 kind=Bidder range origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n137:    Why: — Oral indication: \"representatives from Party C called BofA Merrill Lynch and presented an oral preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $15.00 to $17.00 per share\" (p.33).— Written indication: \"Later on July 25, 2013, Party C submitted a written indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $16.50 per share\" (p.34). Conditions: Heavy by context — preliminary indication before substantive diligence access. One bid, two communications (see Terms or outcome).\n138:    Source: P-032; P-035 | Page: 33 | Review: Q5; Q7 | Related: R033 (Sept 10 revision)\n139: \n140: ### R025 #25 | 07/25/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee | Target decision | proc 1 round 1 type None\n141:    Terms: Preliminary indications judged lower than expected; the Special Committee advanced the four interested bidders (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) to a second stage — staged information disclosure and management meetings — to drive improved offers. The Special Committee also directed that Mr. Rothenberg recuse himself from Board meetings for the duration of the sale process (Moab rollover conflict).\n142:    Why: — Advancement decision: \"the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure as discussed at this meeting and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders and arrange management meetings\" (p.33-34).— Recusal: \"The Special Committee then discussed the potential conflict of interest arising from Moab's continuing desire to consider an equity rollover and decided that Mr. Rothenberg should be asked to recuse himself from participating in Board meetings for the duration of the sale process\" (p.33).\n143:    Source: P-034; P-033 | Page: 34 | Review: Q1 | Related: R026; R011\n144: \n145: ### R026 #26 | 07/25/2013 (decision); implemented 08/06/2013–08/27/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee; Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona | Information access changed | proc 1 round 1 type None\n146:    Terms: Differentiated (tiered) access among live bidders: Party B and Party C, as financial bidders, were given broad access to the electronic data site; Party A and CSC/Pamplona, as strategic bidders, were given somewhat limited access, with customer data (including customer locations) withheld until a later stage; management presentations were held for all four bidders (08/06, 08/08, 08/12, 08/14). Stated rationale: concern over access to and potential misuse of sensitive competitive information, especially by strategic bidders; staging by demonstrated seriousness.\n147:    Why: — Stated access split and withholding: \"Party B and Party C, in light of the fact that they were financial bidders, were given broad access to an electronic data site, and Party A and CSC/Pamplona, in light of the fact that they were strategic bidders, were given somewhat limited access to this electronic data site, with access to customer data, including customer locations, being reserved until later in the process as part of the staging discussed at the July 25 th Special Committee meeting\" (p.34).— Stated rationale: \"expressed concern over permitting access to and the potential misuse of sensitive and competitive information, including customer terms and locations, especially by strategic bidders\" (p.33-34).— Presentations for all four: \"On August 6, 2013, representatives of Party B attended a management presentation\" (p.34). \"On August 14, 2013, representatives of Party A attended a management presentation at the Boston office of Goodwin Procter\" (p.34).\n148:    Source: P-042; P-034; P-037; P-040 | Page: 34 | Review: None | Related: R025\n149: \n150: ### R027 #27 | 08/05/2013 | Party A (strategic bidder) | NDA signed | proc 1 round 1 type Strategic\n151:    Terms: Executed after NDA negotiations stalled over customer and employee non-solicitation provisions; discussions resumed 07/27/2013 (the filing states \"July 27, 2103\" — source typo; intended 2013) and the agreement was executed 08/05/2013; informational package furnished so Party A could potentially improve its June 21 proposal.\n152:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n153:    Why: — Stated execution: \"On August 5, 2013, Party A entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party A with data to potentially improve the terms of the Party A June 21 proposal\" (p.34).— Stalled negotiation and source typo retained: \"Discussions with Party A resumed on July 27, 2103 and Party A and the Transaction Committee agreed to the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions\" (p.34). \"did not come to agreement on the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions\" (p.33).\n154:    Source: P-036; P-030 | Page: 34 | Review: None | Related: None\n155: \n156: ### R028 #28 | 08/27/2013 | Mac-Gray (BofA Merrill Lynch) → Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona | Round opened | proc 1 round 2 type None\n157:    Terms: Second-stage solicitation: letter to all four bidders once all four’s diligence was substantially complete, instructing revised written proposals no later than 09/09/2013 to continue to in-depth evaluation and confirmatory due diligence, addressing valuation, financing, regulatory approvals, post-signing covenants and diligence focus. Authorized at the 08/15/2013 Special Committee meeting; same-day follow-up diligence call with Party B. Round finality: Not final.\n158:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-09-09 00:00:00 treat=None finality=Not final outb=None by=None reason=None\n159:    Why: — Stated authorization: \"the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to send a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona once all four of the bidders' due diligence was substantially complete requesting that, in light of the results of the respective party's due diligence, such party submit a revised written proposal in order to continue in the process, including to engage in more in-depth and confirmatory due diligence of Mac-Gray\" (p.34).— Stated letter and deadline: \"On August 27, 2013, BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Special Committee, sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013 if such bidders wished to proceed further in the process to pursue an in-depth evaluation of Mac-Gray with the objective of making a revised offer\" (p.35).\n160:    Source: P-041; P-043 | Page: 35 | Review: Q1 | Related: R025; R029\n161: \n162: ### R029 #29 | 09/09/2013 | N/A — solicitation deadline | Deadline | proc 1 round 2 type None\n163:    Terms: Revised-proposal due date reached. CSC/Pamplona and Party B submitted on 09/09/2013; Party A and Party C submitted revised indications on 09/10/2013 and were reviewed at the 09/11/2013 Special Committee meeting with no revision of the due date. Treatment: Late bids accepted.\n164:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-09-09 00:00:00 treat=Late bids accepted finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n165:    Why: — Due date and on-time submissions: \"instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013\" (p.35). \"On September 9, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share\" (p.35).— Late submissions reviewed: \"On September 10, 2013, Party A submitted a revised indication of interest\" (p.35). \"the Special Committee held a telephonic meeting to review the revised indications of interest submitted by Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona\" (p.35-36).\n166:    Source: P-043; P-047; P-048; P-050 | Page: 35 | Review: Q2 | Related: R028\n167: \n168: ### R030 #30 | 09/09/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 2 type Strategic\n169:    Terms: Revised indication of interest: all-cash $19.50 per share; Pamplona indicated