one treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n193:    Why: — Stated oral indication: \"in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch, a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share\" (p.35).— No firm commitment: \"Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment\" (p.35). Conditions: Heavy — no firm financing commitment reported.\n194:    Source: P-048 | Page: 35 | Review: Q4 | Related: None\n195: \n196: ### R034 #34 | 09/11/2013 (limited overview) – 09/12/2013 (detailed briefing) | Mac-Gray Transaction Committee / BofA Merrill Lynch ↔ Mr. MacDonald | Material process update | proc 1 round 2 type None\n197:    Terms: Mr. MacDonald’s rollover question resolved: in a limited-overview call (no bidder identities or prices) he said he was not interested in rolling over any shares; the Special Committee agreed he should be fully briefed because any potential acquiror was seen as unlikely to proceed without knowing he would support the transaction; a 09/12/2013 detailed briefing followed, after which he voiced general support while urging a higher value.\n198:    Why: — Stated rollover position: \"During this call, Mr. MacDonald indicated that he had decided that he was not interested in rolling over any of his shares in any transaction\" (p.35).— Stated support premise: \"it was unlikely that any of these parties would move forward in the process without the express support of Mr. MacDonald\" (p.35-36).— Stated briefing and stance: \"Although Mr. MacDonald voiced his general support for continuing with the process, he expressed his view that Mac-Gray should continue to seek a higher value for stockholders\" (p.36). Working date convention: reported interval 09/11–09/12/2013; first day used (Assigned: bound).\n199:    Source: P-049; P-050; P-051 | Page: 35 | Review: Q6; Q7 | Related: R016; R049; R041 (his 09/19 support at $21.25)\n200: \n201: ### R035 #35 | 09/11/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee (via BofA Merrill Lynch) → Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona | Round opened | proc 1 round 3 type None\n202:    Terms: First request for final indications of interest: BofA Merrill Lynch called each of the four bidders on 09/11/2013, as instructed, requesting final indications by 09/18/2013 and signaling that Mac-Gray would consider a short exclusive negotiation with one bidder depending on price and deal certainty. Invited bidders unchanged. Round finality: Announced as final — the target asked for \"final indications of interest\".\n203:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-09-18 00:00:00 treat=None finality=Announced as final outb=None by=None reason=None\n204:    Why: — Stated instruction: \"the Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to call each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013 and to indicate that Mac-Gray would consider engaging in a short period of exclusive negotiations with one of the bidders depending upon, among other things, the proposed purchase price and the level of deal certainty indicated in the bidder's final proposal\" (p.35-36).— Calls made same day: \"representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch called each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona on September 11, 2013 with such instructions\" (p.35-36).\n205:    Source: P-050 | Page: 36 | Review: Q1 | Related: R036\n206: \n207: ### R036 #36 | 09/18/2013 | N/A — solicitation deadline | Deadline | proc 1 round 3 type None\n208:    Terms: Final-indication due date reached. Three bidders responded on 09/18/2013 (CSC/Pamplona $20.75; Party A best-and-final reiteration; Party B $21.50 package); Party C did not submit (R040). The Special Committee took its next step on the bids in hand at its 09/19/2013 meeting — selection of CSC/Pamplona and authorization to offer exclusivity at $21.25. Treatment: Enforced.\n209:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-09-18 00:00:00 treat=Enforced finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 210]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt, lines 80-209\n80:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n81:    Why: — Stated execution and package: \"On June 30, 2013, Party C entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party C with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest\" (p.32).\n82:    Source: P-026 | Page: 32 | Review: None | Related: None\n83: \n84: ### R016 #16 | 07/06/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee; Moab Partners (via Mr. Rothenberg); CSC/Pamplona | Material process update | proc 1 round 1 type None\n85:    Terms: Moab rollover request denied as premature: Mr. Rothenberg had asked that CSC/Pamplona be allowed to share bid and evaluation material with Moab, with Moab exclusively engaged with CSC/Pamplona; the Special Committee denied exclusivity so that Moab’s stake could remain available as capital for other bidders, and said rollover discussions would be permitted at a later stage.\n86:    Why: — Stated request: \"Mr. Rothenberg also informed Goodwin Procter that Pamplona would be requesting that any confidentiality agreement CSC/Pamplona execute with Mac-Gray permit CSC and Pamplona to discuss their bid and evaluation material with Moab, with Moab agreeing to exclusively engage with CSC/Pamplona\" (p.32).— Stated denial and rationale: \"the Special Committee decided to deny the exclusivity request at this stage of the process so that the potential equity rollover of Moab's shares could be available as a source of capital for other potential bidders\" (p.32-33).— Deferral: \"it was premature for Mac-Gray to permit Moab to engage in equity rollover discussions with any party, including CSC/Pamplona, but that such discussions would be permitted at a later stage of the sale process\" (p.32-33).\n87:    Source: P-027; P-028 | Page: 32 | Review: Q6 | Related: R049 (resolution); R010\n88: \n89: ### R017 #17 | between 06/28/2013 and 07/23/2013 (communication date not disclosed) | Mac-Gray (informational package) → NDA signers | Deadline set | proc 1 round 1 type None\n90:    Terms: Informational-package letter instructed NDA signers to submit preliminary indications of interest by 07/23/2013, addressing valuation, sources and structures of financing, material conditions (including required approvals) and due-diligence focus areas. Communication date not disclosed: the package was furnished to each party as it signed; first signer 06/28/2013.\n91:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-07-23 00:00:00 treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n92:    Why: — Stated instruction: \"Parties that had entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with Mac-Gray were furnished an informational package for the purpose of providing potential bidders with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest, which they were instructed to submit by July 23, 2013\" (p.32).— Requested proposal content: \"The letter requested that the proposals address, among other things, valuation, sources and structures of financing, material conditions, including required approvals, and focus areas for due diligence\" (p.32). Working date convention: communication window 06/28–07/23/2013; midpoint used as a sort key (Assigned: midpoint).\n93:    Source: P-023 | Page: 32 | Review: Q2; Q7 | Related: R020 (due date reached)\n94: \n95: ### R018 #18 | 07/11/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder) | NDA signed | proc 1 round 1 type Strategic\n96:    Terms: CSC and Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray jointly (one bidder unit) and received the informational package.\n97:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n98:    Why: — Stated execution and package: \"On July 11, 2013, CSC/Pamplona entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and were provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing CSC/Pamplona with data to formulate a preliminary indication of interest\" (p.33).\n99:    Source: P-029 | Page: 33 | Review: None | Related: None\n100: \n101: ### R019 #19 | late June through late August 2013 (individual dates not disclosed) | 16 remaining financial bidders (residual cohort) | NDA signed | proc 1 round 1 type Financial\n102:    Terms: Residual cohort: 20 potential bidders signed confidentiality and standstill agreements over roughly two months; four are individually recorded (Party A 08/05/2013, Party B 06/28/2013, Party C 06/30/2013, CSC/Pamplona 07/11/2013) and the remaining 16 signers are represented by this one cohort row. The cohort’s Working date is moved earlier to 07/23/2013 (inside its window) so that it precedes its inferred non-submission row (R021) — Assigned: sequence.\n103:    Count=16 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n104:    Why: — Stated total and split: \"Over the next two months a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray\" (p.32). Working date convention: the cohort’s signing window (late June to late August) straddles the 07/23/2013 solicitation; the date was moved earlier inside that window so the entry row precedes its inferred non-submission outcome (Assigned: sequence).\n105:    Source: P-023 | Page: 32 | Review: Q3; Q7 | Related: R014; R015; R018; R027; R021 (inferred non-submission)\n106: \n107: ### R020 #20 | 07/23/2013 | N/A — solicitation deadline | Deadline | proc 1 round 1 type None\n108:    Terms: Preliminary-indication due date reached. CSC/Pamplona submitted on 07/23/2013; Party B submitted 07/24/2013 and Party C 07/24–07/25/2013, and the Special Committee reviewed all of them on 07/25/2013 with no revision of the due date. Treatment: Late bids accepted.\n109:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-07-23 00:00:00 treat=Late bids accepted finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n110:    Why: — Due date: \"instructed to submit by July 23, 2013\" (p.32).— Late submissions considered: \"On July 25, 2013, the Board held a regularly scheduled in-person meeting\" (p.33). \"representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch reviewed the preliminary indications of interest received from Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona as well as the Party A June 21 proposal\" (p.33).\n111:    Source: P-023; P-033 | Page: 32 | Review: Q2 | Related: R017\n112: \n113: ### R021 #21 | by 07/23/2013 (solicitation due date passed with no submission) | 16 remaining financial bidders (residual cohort) | Did not submit | proc 1 round 1 type Financial\n114:    Terms: Inferred: residual — 20 NDA signers − 4 individually recorded signers (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) = 16 remaining signers, all financial; none is reported to have submitted a July 23 indication. Base assumes each of the 20 signers was covered by the July 23 solicitation; if any signed later than that deadline, the non-submitting set is smaller (flagged in Q3). Inferred from arithmetic only — no dates, motives or identities inferred.\n115:    Count=16 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=Inferred: residual by=Unknown reason=Not stated\n116:    Why: — Base population: \"a total of 20 potential bidders, including two strategic bidders (Party A and CSC/Pamplona) and 18 financial bidders (including Party B and Party C), entered into confidentiality agreements with Mac-Gray\" (p.32).— Continuing set named at the next transition: \"reach out to each of the four interested bidders and arrange management meetings\" (p.33-34).— Solicitation due date: \"instructed to submit by July 23, 2013\" (p.32). Outcome basis: arithmetic residual only — no dates, motives, identities or voluntary withdrawal inferred. Count = stated base − accounted participants.\n117:    Source: P-023; P-034 | Page: 32 | Review: Q3 | Related: R019 (entry); R020\n118: \n119: ### R022 #22 | 07/23/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 1 type Strategic\n120:    Terms: Preliminary indication of interest: all-cash $18.50 per share, submitted on the 07/23/2013 due date after a preliminary review (07/11–07/23) but before data-room or management access; financing not described at this stage.\n121:    Formality: Informal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n122:    Count=1 Price=18.5-18.5 kind=Point origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/18.5 due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n123:    Why: — Stated indication: \"On July 23, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a preliminary indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share\" (p.33).— Substantive access not yet given: \"Between July 11, 2013 and July 23, 2013, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona engaged in a preliminary review of Mac-Gray and the potential acquisition opportunity\" (p.33). Conditions: Heavy by context — preliminary indication made before data-room or management access; financing not yet described.\n124:    Source: P-031; P-030 | Page: 33 | Review: Q4 | Related: R030 (Sept 9 revision); R037; R042\n125: \n126: ### R023 #23 | 07/24/2013 | Party B (financial bidder)