ten indication of interest at an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $16.50 per share\" (p.34). Conditions: Heavy by context — preliminary indication before substantive diligence access. One bid, two communications (see Terms or outcome).\n138:    Source: P-032; P-035 | Page: 33 | Review: Q5; Q7 | Related: R033 (Sept 10 revision)\n139: \n140: ### R025 #25 | 07/25/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee | Target decision | proc 1 round 1 type None\n141:    Terms: Preliminary indications judged lower than expected; the Special Committee advanced the four interested bidders (Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona) to a second stage — staged information disclosure and management meetings — to drive improved offers. The Special Committee also directed that Mr. Rothenberg recuse himself from Board meetings for the duration of the sale process (Moab rollover conflict).\n142:    Why: — Advancement decision: \"the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to proceed with the staged disclosure as discussed at this meeting and to reach out to each of the four interested bidders and arrange management meetings\" (p.33-34).— Recusal: \"The Special Committee then discussed the potential conflict of interest arising from Moab's continuing desire to consider an equity rollover and decided that Mr. Rothenberg should be asked to recuse himself from participating in Board meetings for the duration of the sale process\" (p.33).\n143:    Source: P-034; P-033 | Page: 34 | Review: Q1 | Related: R026; R011\n144: \n145: ### R026 #26 | 07/25/2013 (decision); implemented 08/06/2013–08/27/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee; Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona | Information access changed | proc 1 round 1 type None\n146:    Terms: Differentiated (tiered) access among live bidders: Party B and Party C, as financial bidders, were given broad access to the electronic data site; Party A and CSC/Pamplona, as strategic bidders, were given somewhat limited access, with customer data (including customer locations) withheld until a later stage; management presentations were held for all four bidders (08/06, 08/08, 08/12, 08/14). Stated rationale: concern over access to and potential misuse of sensitive competitive information, especially by strategic bidders; staging by demonstrated seriousness.\n147:    Why: — Stated access split and withholding: \"Party B and Party C, in light of the fact that they were financial bidders, were given broad access to an electronic data site, and Party A and CSC/Pamplona, in light of the fact that they were strategic bidders, were given somewhat limited access to this electronic data site, with access to customer data, including customer locations, being reserved until later in the process as part of the staging discussed at the July 25 th Special Committee meeting\" (p.34).— Stated rationale: \"expressed concern over permitting access to and the potential misuse of sensitive and competitive information, including customer terms and locations, especially by strategic bidders\" (p.33-34).— Presentations for all four: \"On August 6, 2013, representatives of Party B attended a management presentation\" (p.34). \"On August 14, 2013, representatives of Party A attended a management presentation at the Boston office of Goodwin Procter\" (p.34).\n148:    Source: P-042; P-034; P-037; P-040 | Page: 34 | Review: None | Related: R025\n149: \n150: ### R027 #27 | 08/05/2013 | Party A (strategic bidder) | NDA signed | proc 1 round 1 type Strategic\n151:    Terms: Executed after NDA negotiations stalled over customer and employee non-solicitation provisions; discussions resumed 07/27/2013 (the filing states \"July 27, 2103\" — source typo; intended 2013) and the agreement was executed 08/05/2013; informational package furnished so Party A could potentially improve its June 21 proposal.\n152:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n153:    Why: — Stated execution: \"On August 5, 2013, Party A entered into a confidentiality and standstill agreement with Mac-Gray and was provided with an informational package for the purpose of providing Party A with data to potentially improve the terms of the Party A June 21 proposal\" (p.34).— Stalled negotiation and source typo retained: \"Discussions with Party A resumed on July 27, 2103 and Party A and the Transaction Committee agreed to the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions\" (p.34). \"did not come to agreement on the terms of the customer and employee non-solicitation provisions\" (p.33).\n154:    Source: P-036; P-030 | Page: 34 | Review: None | Related: None\n155: \n156: ### R028 #28 | 08/27/2013 | Mac-Gray (BofA Merrill Lynch) → Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona | Round opened | proc 1 round 2 type None\n157:    Terms: Second-stage solicitation: letter to all four bidders once all four’s diligence was substantially complete, instructing revised written proposals no later than 09/09/2013 to continue to in-depth evaluation and confirmatory due diligence, addressing valuation, financing, regulatory approvals, post-signing covenants and diligence focus. Authorized at the 08/15/2013 Special Committee meeting; same-day follow-up diligence call with Party B. Round finality: Not final.\n158:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-09-09 00:00:00 treat=None finality=Not final outb=None by=None reason=None\n159:    Why: — Stated authorization: \"the Special Committee authorized and instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to send a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona once all four of the bidders' due diligence was substantially complete requesting that, in light of the results of the respective party's due diligence, such party submit a revised written proposal in order to continue in the process, including to engage in more in-depth and confirmatory due diligence of Mac-Gray\" (p.34).— Stated letter and deadline: \"On August 27, 2013, BofA Merrill Lynch, as instructed by the Special Committee, sent a letter to each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013 if such bidders wished to proceed further in the process to pursue an in-depth evaluation of Mac-Gray with the objective of making a revised offer\" (p.35).\n160:    Source: P-041; P-043 | Page: 35 | Review: Q1 | Related: R025; R029\n161: \n162: ### R029 #29 | 09/09/2013 | N/A — solicitation deadline | Deadline | proc 1 round 2 type None\n163:    Terms: Revised-proposal due date reached. CSC/Pamplona and Party B submitted on 09/09/2013; Party A and Party C submitted revised indications on 09/10/2013 and were reviewed at the 09/11/2013 Special Committee meeting with no revision of the due date. Treatment: Late bids accepted.\n164:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-09-09 00:00:00 treat=Late bids accepted finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n165:    Why: — Due date and on-time submissions: \"instructing such bidders to submit revised written proposals no later than September 9, 2013\" (p.35). \"On September 9, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share\" (p.35).— Late submissions reviewed: \"On September 10, 2013, Party A submitted a revised indication of interest\" (p.35). \"the Special Committee held a telephonic meeting to review the revised indications of interest submitted by Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona\" (p.35-36).\n166:    Source: P-043; P-047; P-048; P-050 | Page: 35 | Review: Q2 | Related: R028\n167: \n168: ### R030 #30 | 09/09/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 2 type Strategic\n169:    Terms: Revised indication of interest: all-cash $19.50 per share; Pamplona indicated it was committed to provide 100% of the capital required; CSC/Pamplona requested a two-week exclusive negotiation.\n170:    Formality: Informal | Conditions: Light | detail: Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\n171:    Count=1 Price=19.5-19.5 kind=Point origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/19.5 due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n172:    Why: — Stated indication and committed capital: \"On September 9, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $19.50 per share, indicating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to exclusive negotiations for two weeks\" (p.35).— Diligence still running: \"Between September 11, 2013 and September 18, 2013, Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona continued to conduct business and legal due diligence\" (p.36). Conditions: Light — committed financing reported (Pamplona, 100% of required capital) and no diligence condition attached to the bid; diligence remained open on the narrative.\n173:    Source: P-047; P-052 | Page: 35 | Review: Q4 | Related: R037 (Sept 18 revision)\n174: \n175: ### R031 #31 | 09/09/2013 | Party B (financial bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 2 type Financial\n176:    Terms: Revised indication of interest: all-cash $18.50 per share, proposed to be financed with equity from affiliated funds and third-party debt; no firm financing commitment.\n177:    Formality: Informal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n178:    Count=1 Price=18.5-18.5 kind=Point origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/18.5 due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n179:    Why: — Stated indication and financing: \"On September 9, 2013, Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.50 per share and proposed to finance the transaction with a combination of equity from affiliated funds and third party debt. Party B's revised indication of interest did not include a firm financing commitment\" (p.35). Conditions: Heavy — no firm financing commitment reported; third-party debt contemplated.\n180:    Source: P-047 | Page: 35 | Review: Q4 | Related: R039 (Sept 18 revision)\n181: \n182: ### R032 #32 | 09/10/2013 | Party A (strategic bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 2 type Strategic\n183:    Terms: Revised indication of interest: all-cash $18.00–$19.00 per share, to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources; no firm financing commitment.\n184:    Formality: Informal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n185:    Count=1 Price=18-19 kind=Bidder range origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n186:    Why: — Stated indication: \"On September 10, 2013, Party A submitted a revised indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share, to be financed by outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity sources\" (p.35).— No firm commitment: \"Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment\" (p.35). Conditions: Heavy — no firm financing commitment reported.\n187:    Source: P-048 | Page: 35 | Review: Q4 | Related: R038 (Sept 18 best-and-final reiteration)\n188: \n189: ### R033 #33 | 09/10/2013 | Party C (financial bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 2 type Financial\n190:    Terms: Revised oral indication of interest in a telephone call to BofA Merrill Lynch: all-cash $16.00–$17.00 per share; no firm financing commitment.\n191:    Formality: Informal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n192:    Count=1 Price=16-17 kind=Bidder range origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n193:    Why: — Stated oral indication: \"in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch, a representative of Party C indicated that it was submitting a revised oral indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share\" (p.35).— No firm commitment: \"Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment\" (p.35). Conditions: Heavy — no firm financing commitment reported.\n194:    Source: P-048 | Page: 35 | Review: Q4 | Related: None\n195: \n196: ### R034 #34 | 09/11/2013 (limited overview) – 09/12/2013 (detailed briefing) | Mac-Gray Transaction Committee / BofA Merrill Lynch ↔ Mr. MacDonald | Material process update | proc 1 round 2 type None\n197:    Terms: Mr. MacDonald’s rollover question resolved: in a limited-overview call (no bidder identities or prices) he said he was not interested in rolling over any shares; the Special Committee agreed he should be fully briefed because any potential acquiror was seen as unlikely to proceed without knowing he would support the transaction; a 09/12/2013 detailed briefing followed, after which he voiced general support while urging a higher value.\n198:    Why: — Stated rollover position: \"During this call, Mr. MacDonald indicated that he had decided that he was not interested in rolling over any of his shares in any transaction\" (p.35).— Stated support premise: \"it was unlikely that any of these parties would move forward in the process without the express support of Mr. MacDonald\" (p.35-36).— Stated briefing and stance: \"Although Mr. MacDonald voiced his general support for continuing with the process, he expressed his view that Mac-Gray should continue to seek a higher value for stockholders\" (p.36). Working date convention: reported interval 09/11–09/12/2013; first day used (Assigned: bound).\n199:    Source: P-049; P-050; P-051 | Page: 35 | Review: Q6; Q7 | Related: R016; R049; R041 (his 09/19 support at $21.25)\n200: \n201: ### R035 #35 | 09/11/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee (via BofA Merrill Lynch) → Party A, Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona | Round opened | proc 1 round 3 type None\n202:    Terms: First request for final indications of interest: BofA Merrill Lynch called each of the four bidders on 09/11/2013, as instructed, requesting final indications by 09/18/2013 and signaling that Mac-Gray would consider a short exclusive negotiation with one bidder depending on price and deal certainty. Invited bidders unchanged. Round finality: Announced as final — the target asked for \"final indications of interest\".\n203:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=2013-09-18 00:00:00 treat=None finality=Announced as final outb=None by=None reason=None\n204:    Why: — Stated instruction: \"the Special Committee instructed BofA Merrill Lynch to call each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013 and to indicate that Mac-Gray would consider engaging in a short period of exclusive negotiations with one of the bidders depending upon, among other things, the proposed purchase price and the level of deal certainty indicated in the bidder's final proposal\" (p.35-36).— Calls made same day: \"representatives of BofA Merrill Lynch called each of Party A, Party B, Party C and CSC/Pamplona on September 11, 2013 with such instructions\" (p.35-36).\n205:    Source: P-050 | Page: 36 | Review: Q1 | Related: R036\n206: \n207: ### R036 #36 | 09/18/2013 | N/A — solicitation deadline | Deadline | proc 1 round 3 type None\n208:    Terms: Final-indication due date reached. Three bidders responded on 09/18/2013 (CSC/Pamplona $20.75; Party A best-and-final reiteration; Party B $21.50 package); Party C did not submit (R040). The Special Committee took its next step on the bids in hand at its 09/19/2013 meeting — selection of CSC/Pamplona and authorization to offer exclusivity at $21.25. 