{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825295966,"sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e6a5b8001toS59vuN3SCgHK","sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","messageID":"msg_0b9e6936e001pUwhxg689XbwlQ","type":"tool","id":"call_00_pYtzpELRVIIobPGOJt2y9973","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"limit":115,"offset":210,"path":"/tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt"},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt, lines 210-319\n210:    Why: — Due date and responses: \"to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013\" (p.35-36). \"On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share\" (p.36).— Next step on the bids in hand: \"the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications\" (p.37).\n211:    Source: P-050; P-053; P-055 | Page: 36 | Review: Q2 | Related: R035\n212: \n213: ### R037 #37 | 09/18/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 3 type Strategic\n214:    Terms: Final-solicited proposal: all-cash $20.75 per share; Pamplona reiterated it was committed to provide 100% of the capital required; requested two-week exclusive negotiations.\n215:    Formality: Formal | Conditions: Light | detail: Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\n216:    Count=1 Price=20.75-20.75 kind=Point origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/20.75 due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n217:    Why: — Stated proposal and commitment: \"On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share, reiterating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to engage in exclusive negotiations for two weeks\" (p.36).— Formal signal — response on the requested basis to the final solicitation: \"to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013\" (p.35-36). Formality: Formal — response on the requested basis to the target’s final-indications request (signal 2). Conditions: Light — committed financing, no diligence condition attached; diligence still open.\n218:    Source: P-053; P-050 | Page: 36 | Review: Q4 | Related: R042 (Sept 21 increase); R035\n219: \n220: ### R038 #38 | 09/18/2013 | Party A (strategic bidder) | Bid reaffirmed | proc 1 round 3 type Strategic\n221:    Terms: Reaffirmed by: price confirmed — telephone reiteration that its earlier all-cash $18.00–$19.00 indication was Party A’s best and final offer; price carried forward from R032, not restated. Financing basis unchanged (outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity; no firm commitment).\n222:    Formality: Formal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n223:    Count=1 Price=18-19 kind=Bidder range origin=Carried forward cur=USD cash=Yes/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n224:    Why: — Stated reaffirmation: \"Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer\" (p.36).— Formal signal — best-and-final response; standing conditions unchanged: \"Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment\" (p.35). Formality: Formal — supported best-and-final response (signal 2; oral confirmation). Conditions: Heavy — carried financing basis with no firm commitment at this date (see R032).\n225:    Source: P-053; P-048 | Page: 36 | Review: Q4; Q5 | Related: R032 (carried price); R042 (later Party A dropped)\n226: \n227: ### R039 #39 | 09/18/2013 | Party B (financial bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 3 type Financial\n228:    Terms: Revised indication valued by Party B at $21.50 per share: $19.00 cash at closing plus options representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B’s initial cost basis; options to vest over five years on achievement of the base-case management projections (excluding future acquisitions); Party B valued the options at $2.50 per share. Package value, not guaranteed cash; financing remained without a firm commitment.\n229:    Formality: Formal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n230:    Count=1 Price=21.5-21.5 kind=Point origin=Stated cur=USD cash=No/19 due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n231:    Why: — Stated package and option terms: \"Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing and the remaining per share price to be paid in the form of options to be issued to Mac-Gray stockholders, representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B's initial cost basis. These options, which we refer to as the Party B options, would vest on the achievement of the base case management projections ( i.e. , over five years), excluding any future acquisitions. Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share\" (p.36).— Financing not committed; formal signal — final-solicitation response: \"Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment\" (p.35). Formality: Formal — final-solicitation response (signal 2). Conditions: Heavy — no firm financing commitment; option consideration adds contingency. Price: package value, not guaranteed cash.\n232:    Source: P-053; P-048 | Page: 36 | Review: Q4; Q5 | Related: R031 (prior priced bid)\n233: \n234: ### R040 #40 | by 09/18/2013 (final-indication deadline passed with no submission) | Party C (financial bidder) | Did not submit | proc 1 round 3 type Financial\n235:    Terms: Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior $16.00–$17.00 indication in response to the 09/11/2013 final request, and the filing states it gave no reasons. Closed at this transition; no further Party C participation is reported.\n236:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=Stated by=Unknown reason=Not stated\n237:    Why: — Stated non-submission: \"Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share nor did it specify any reasons in connection therewith\" (p.36). Outcome basis: Stated — the filing directly reports the non-submission and that no reasons were given.\n238:    Source: P-053 | Page: 36 | Review: Q3 | Related: None\n239: \n240: ### R041 #41 | 09/19/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee | Target decision | proc 1 round 3 type None\n241:    Terms: Preferred-bidder decision: the Special Committee concluded CSC/Pamplona’s indication offered the most value, greater certainty and less risk (Party B’s options were contingent and complex and Party B would likely need third-party debt); it concluded CSC/Pamplona should be able to raise above $20.75 and authorized the Transaction Committee to offer exclusivity at $21.25; Mr. MacDonald indicated he would support $21.25.\n242:    Why: — Stated conclusion: \"the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications\" (p.37).— Price requirement and exclusivity authorization: \"the Special Committee also concluded that, primarily in view of potential synergies between Mac-Gray and CSC, CSC/Pamplona should be in a position to increase their offer price above $20.75. The Special Committee then authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share\" (p.37). \"at this meeting Mr. MacDonald indicated that he would be supportive of a price of $21.25 per share\" (p.37).\n243:    Source: P-055 | Page: 37 | Review: None | Related: R042; R043\n244: \n245: ### R042 #42 | 09/21/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 3 type Strategic\n246:    Terms: Price increase to $21.25 per share all-cash as a last and best offer, provided Mac-Gray agreed to a two-week exclusive negotiation; CSC/Pamplona also requested a customary voting agreement over Mr. MacDonald’s and his immediate family’s shares. This is the price component of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal (no financing contingency; Pamplona committing 100% of the capital needed for closing).\n247:    Formality: Formal | Conditions: Light | detail: Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\n248:    Count=0 Price=21.25-21.25 kind=Point origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/21.25 due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n249:    Why: — Stated confirmation: \"the representative of CSC/Pamplona called the members of the Transaction Committee to confirm that CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer, provided that Mac-Gray agree to a two week period of exclusive negotiations\" (p.37).— Voting agreement request: \"The representative of CSC/Pamplona also requested that shares of Mac-Gray common stock owned beneficially and of record by Mr. MacDonald and his immediate family be subject to a customary voting agreement, which we refer to as the MacDonald voting agreements\" (p.37).— Final proposal terms: \"the inclusion of a $15 million \"reverse\" termination fee payable by CSC/Pamplona to Mac-Gray in the event regulatory clearance is not obtained, which we refer to as the CSC reverse termination fee, agreements regarding certain post-signing covenants, the fact that there would be no financing contingency and that Pamplona was committing to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing\" (p.37-38). Formality: carries forward from R037 (continuing proposal; no return to a preliminary basis). Conditions: Light — Pamplona committed 100% of closing capital; no financing contingency.\n250:    Source: P-056; P-057 | Page: 37 | Review: Q4 | Related: R037 (revises R037); R043\n251: \n252: ### R043 #43 | 09/23/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee; CSC/Pamplona | Exclusivity changed | proc 1 round 3 type None\n253:    Terms: Authorized: the Special Committee authorized Mac-Gray to enter an exclusivity agreement providing exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013 on the CSC/Pamplona final proposal terms ($21.25 per share cash; $15 million CSC reverse termination fee if regulatory clearance is not obtained; no financing contingency; Pamplona to fund 100% of closing capital); the agreement would automatically terminate if CSC or Pamplona adversely changed the final proposal terms.\n254:    Why: — Stated authorization: \"After discussion, the Special Committee authorized Mac-Gray to enter into an exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013 on the terms included in the CSC/Pamplona final proposal\" (p.38).— Stated terms and condition: \"The parties also agreed that the exclusivity agreement would automatically terminate if CSC or Pamplona adversely changed any of the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal\" (p.37-38).\n255:    Source: P-059; P-057 | Page: 38 | Review: Q8 | Related: R044; R042\n256: \n257: ### R044 #44 | 09/24/2013 | CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray | Exclusivity changed | proc 1 round 3 type None\n258:    Terms: Executed: CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement — exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013, subject to certain conditions including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the final proposal terms. This execution is the transition into the definitive-negotiation stage (R047).\n259:    Why: — Stated execution: \"On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, subject to certain conditions, including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal\" (p.38).\n260:    Source: P-060 | Page: 38 | Review: Q8 | Related: R043; R047; R045; R046\n261: \n262: ### R045 #45 | by 09/24/2013 (exclusivity execution) | Party A (strategic bidder) | Dropped by target | proc 1 round 3 type Strategic\n263:    Terms: Inferred: exclusivity — Party A was still live after the final round (its best-and-final reiteration of 09/18/2013) when Mac-Gray executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013; the filing reports no notice to Party A and states no reason. Closed at this transition.\n264:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=Inferred: exclusivity by=Target reason=Not stated\n265:    Why: — Exclusivity execution: \"On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\" (p.38).— Last participation: \"Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer\" (p.36). Outcome basis and agency: Inferred solely from the exclusivity execution; Decided by Target for the transition; the filing states no reason or notice.\n266:    Source: P-060; P-053 | Page: 38 | Review: Q3 | Related: R038; R044\n267: \n268: ### R046 #46 | by 09/24/2013 (exclusivity execution) | Party B (financial bidder) | Dropped by target | proc 1 round 3 type Financial\n269:    Terms: Inferred: exclusivity — Party B was still live after the final round (its 09/18/2013 $21.50 package) when Mac-Gray executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013; the filing reports no notice to Party B and states no reason. Closed at this transition.\n270:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=Inferred: exclusivity by=Target reason=Not stated\n271:    Why: — Exclusivity execution: \"On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\" (p.38).— Last participation: \"Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share\" (p.36). Outcome basis and agency: Inferred solely from the exclusivity execution; Decided by Target for the transition; the filing states no reason or notice.\n272:    Source: P-060; P-053 | Page: 38 | Review: Q3 | Related: R039; R044\n273: \n274: ### R047 #47 | 09/24/2013 | Mac-Gray ↔ CSC/Pamplona | Round opened | proc 1 round 4 type None\n275:    Terms: Definitive-negotiation stage opens with the 09/24/2013 exclusivity execution (R044); Goodwin Procter delivered the initial merger-agreement draft to Kirkland & Ellis on 09/25/2013 (R048) and CSC/Pamplona were granted full data-site and management access for confirmatory diligence. Selected bidder CSC/Pamplona remains live; all other bidders are already closed. Round finality: Inferred final — no announcement, but the target moved to definitive negotiation with the selected bidder.\n276:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=Inferred final outb=None by=None reason=None\n277:    Why: — Draft delivered and confirmatory diligence: \"On September 25, 2013, Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement\" (p.38). \"CSC and Pamplona were granted full access to the electronic data site and access to certain members of management and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence on Mac-Gray\" (p.38).\n278:    Source: P-061 | Page: 38 | Review: Q1 | Related: R044; R048; R043; R035\n279: \n280: ### R048 #48 | 09/25/2013 | Kirkland & Ellis LLP (outside legal counsel, CSC/Pamplona) | Adviser service observed | proc 1 round 4 type None\n281:    Terms: First shown acting on the CSC/Pamplona mandate when Goodwin Procter delivered the initial merger-agreement draft to Kirkland; engagement date not disclosed. Kirkland negotiated the merger agreement and the Pamplona commitment letter for CSC/Pamplona.\n282:    Why: — Earliest observed service: \"On September 25, 2013, Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement\" (p.38).\n283:    Source: P-061 | Page: 38 | Review: None | Related: None\n284: \n285: ### R049 #49 | after 09/23/2013; reported 10/07/2013 | Moab Partners; CSC/Pamplona; Mac-Gray Special Committee | Material process update | proc 1 round 4 type None\n286:    Terms: Moab rollover resolved without a rollover: the Special Committee had allowed Mr. Rothenberg on 09/23/2013 to resume discussions with CSC/Pamplona about a possible rollover of Moab’s shares; after those discussions it was determined that Moab would not roll over any shares in the transaction, as reported to the Special Committee on 10/07/2013.\n287:    Why: — Stated permission: \"to provide Moab with the opportunity to resume discussions with CSC/Pamplona regarding a possible equity rollover of Moab's shares in the transaction if Moab still had an interest in such a rollover\" (p.38).— Stated discussion period: \"Mr. Rothenberg engaged in various discussions with representatives of Pamplona during this time to discuss a possible rollover of Moab shares\" (p.38).— Stated determination reported 10/07/2013: \"Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction\" (p.39). Working date convention: the determination date is not disclosed; it is reported at the 10/07/2013 Special Committee meeting (Assigned: bound to the report).\n288:    Source: P-058; P-061; P-065 | Page: 39 | Review: Q6; Q7 | Related: R016 (denial); R010\n289: \n290: ### R050 #50 | 10/09/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee; CSC/Pamplona | Exclusivity changed | proc 1 round 4 type None\n291:    Terms: Extension authorized: the Special Committee authorized the Transaction Committee to negotiate the open issues within parameters and to extend exclusivity to 10/15/2013; CSC/Pamplona had requested extension of the 5 p.m. ET 10/12 expiry to allow continued negotiations.\n292:    Why: — Stated request and authorization: \"Kirkland had requested on behalf of CSC/Pamplona that the exclusivity agreement, due to expire at 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, be extended to allow for continued negotiations of these open issues. After discussion, the Special Committee authorized the Transaction Committee to negotiate the open issues within certain parameters and in connection therewith to extend exclusivity to October 15, 2013\" (p.40).\n293:    Source: P-069 | Page: 40 | Review: Q8 | Related: R051\n294: \n295: ### R051 #51 | 10/12/2013 | CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray | Exclusivity changed | proc 1 round 4 type None\n296:    Terms: Extended: letter agreement executed extending exclusivity to 11:59 p.m. ET on 10/15/2013. The extension was authorized subject to CSC/Pamplona agreeing to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million; CSC/Pamplona agreed on 10/11/2013.\n297:    Why: — Stated execution: \"On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013\" (p.41).— Stated condition and agreement: \"The Special Committee confirmed that the Transaction Committee and representatives of Mac-Gray were authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million\" (p.40). \"the representative of CSC/Pamplona telephoned Mr. Daoust and agreed to the $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee\" (p.40-41).\n298:    Source: P-072; P-070; P-071 | Page: 41 | Review: Q8 | Related: R050\n299: \n300: ### R052 #52 | 10/14/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee; Mac-Gray Board of Directors | Target decision | proc 1 round 4 type None\n301:    Terms: BofA Merrill Lynch delivered its oral fairness opinion (confirmed in writing, dated 10/14/2013); the Special Committee unanimously determined to recommend the merger agreement; the Board, on that recommendation, unanimously approved and adopted the merger agreement and recommends stockholder adoption.\n302:    Why: — Stated opinion: \"BofA Merrill Lynch reviewed with the Special Committee its financial analysis of the consideration and delivered to the Special Committee an oral opinion, which was confirmed by delivery of a written opinion dated, October 14, 2013\" (p.41).— Stated recommendations: \"the Board (upon the recommendation of the Special Committee) unanimously determined that the merger agreement and the merger were advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray's stockholders, approved the merger on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the merger agreement, adopted the merger agreement and recommended that the Mac-Gray stockholders adopt and approve the merger agreement\" (p.41).\n303:    Source: P-075; P-076 | Page: 41 | Review: Q5 | Related: R053\n304: \n305: ### R053 #53 | 10/14/2013 | Mac-Gray; CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.; CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.; Spin Holdco Inc.; CSC Fenway, Inc. | Merger agreement signed | proc 1 round 4 type None\n306:    Terms: Executed: Agreement and Plan of Merger dated as of 10/14/2013 (Mac-Gray; Holdings; CSC; Spin Holdco/Parent; CSC Fenway/Merger Subsidiary). Agreed consideration: $21.25 per share in cash, without interest, less applicable withholding. Pamplona commitment letter ($594 million) delivered; no financing condition to the Buyer Entities’ obligations; Mac-Gray termination fee $11 million; CSC reverse termination fee $15 million; Pamplona damages liability capped at $50 million (Buyer Entities unlimited). Moab voting agreement executed and the MacDonald voting agreements became effective (≈15% of shares subject to voting agreements). No go-shop is reported; the Board retained a fiduciary out to accept a superior proposal on payment of the $11 million fee.\n307:    Why: — Stated execution and related documents: \"Later in the day, on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective\" (p.41).— Consideration: \"will be automatically converted into the right to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest and less applicable withholding taxes\" (p.5).— Termination fees: \"Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances\" (p.10). \"then Parent will pay Mac-Gray the $15 million Parent termination fee\" (p.81).— Financing: \"The merger agreement does not contain any condition to the obligations of the Buyer Entities or Merger Subsidiary relating to the receipt of financing by the Buyer Entities\" (p.58). \"an aggregate of $594 million of capital (the Pamplona commitment amount)\" (p.59).— Voting agreements: \"Approximately 15% of the outstanding Mac-Gray shares on the record date for the special meeting are subject to the voting agreements\" (p.82).\n308:    Source: P-077; X-001; X-005; X-025; X-019; X-020; X-026 | Page: 41 | Review: Q5 | Related: R052; R054; R044\n309: \n310: ### R054 #54 | 10/15/2013 | Mac-Gray and CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. | Merger announced | proc 1 round post type None\n311:    Terms: Joint announcement of the execution of the merger agreement, before U.S. stock markets opened. The merger was announced as expected to close in January 2014 (first half of 2014 per the merger-agreement section); no completion is observed in this filing.\n312:    Why: — Stated announcement: \"On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement\" (p.41).— Expected timing: \"We currently expect the merger to be completed in January 2014\" (p.14).\n313:    Source: P-078; X-008 | Page: 41 | Review: None | Related: R053\n314: \n315: ### R055 #55 | 12/04/2013 | MacKenzie Partners, Inc. (proxy solicitor, Mac-Gray) | Adviser service observed | proc 1 round post type None\n316:    Terms: Proxy solicitor for the special meeting; the proxy statement states Mac-Gray expects to retain MacKenzie Partners for the solicitation for a fee of approximately $15,000 plus out-of-pocket expenses and indemnification (expected retention, not a stated executed engagement).\n317:    Why: — Stated expected retention: \"we expect to retain MacKenzie Partners, Inc. to assist in the solicitation for a fee of approximately $15,000\" (p.23).\n318:    Source: X-010 | Page: 23 | Review: None | Related: None\n319: ","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt, lines 210-319\n210:    Why: — Due date and responses: \"to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013\" (p.35-36). \"On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share\" (p.36).— Next step on the bids in hand: \"the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications\" (p.37).\n211:    Source: P-050; P-053; P-055 | Page: 36 | Review: Q2 | Related: R035\n212: \n213: ### R037 #37 | 09/18/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 3 type Strategic\n214:    Terms: Final-solicited proposal: all-cash $20.75 per share; Pamplona reiterated it was committed to provide 100% of the capital required; requested two-week exclusive negotiations.\n215:    Formality: Formal | Conditions: Light | detail: Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\n216:    Count=1 Price=20.75-20.75 kind=Point origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/20.75 due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n217:    Why: — Stated proposal and commitment: \"On September 18, 2013, CSC/Pamplona submitted a proposal for an all-cash purchase price of $20.75 per share, reiterating that Pamplona was committed to provide 100% of the capital required to consummate the transaction and requesting that CSC/Pamplona and Mac-Gray agree to engage in exclusive negotiations for two weeks\" (p.36).— Formal signal — response on the requested basis to the final solicitation: \"to request final indications of interest by September 18, 2013\" (p.35-36). Formality: Formal — response on the requested basis to the target’s final-indications request (signal 2). Conditions: Light — committed financing, no diligence condition attached; diligence still open.\n218:    Source: P-053; P-050 | Page: 36 | Review: Q4 | Related: R042 (Sept 21 increase); R035\n219: \n220: ### R038 #38 | 09/18/2013 | Party A (strategic bidder) | Bid reaffirmed | proc 1 round 3 type Strategic\n221:    Terms: Reaffirmed by: price confirmed — telephone reiteration that its earlier all-cash $18.00–$19.00 indication was Party A’s best and final offer; price carried forward from R032, not restated. Financing basis unchanged (outstanding credit facilities or affiliated equity; no firm commitment).\n222:    Formality: Formal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n223:    Count=1 Price=18-19 kind=Bidder range origin=Carried forward cur=USD cash=Yes/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n224:    Why: — Stated reaffirmation: \"Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer\" (p.36).— Formal signal — best-and-final response; standing conditions unchanged: \"Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment\" (p.35). Formality: Formal — supported best-and-final response (signal 2; oral confirmation). Conditions: Heavy — carried financing basis with no firm commitment at this date (see R032).\n225:    Source: P-053; P-048 | Page: 36 | Review: Q4; Q5 | Related: R032 (carried price); R042 (later Party A dropped)\n226: \n227: ### R039 #39 | 09/18/2013 | Party B (financial bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 3 type Financial\n228:    Terms: Revised indication valued by Party B at $21.50 per share: $19.00 cash at closing plus options representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B’s initial cost basis; options to vest over five years on achievement of the base-case management projections (excluding future acquisitions); Party B valued the options at $2.50 per share. Package value, not guaranteed cash; financing remained without a firm commitment.\n229:    Formality: Formal | Conditions: Heavy | detail: Fin: not committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated\n230:    Count=1 Price=21.5-21.5 kind=Point origin=Stated cur=USD cash=No/19 due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n231:    Why: — Stated package and option terms: \"Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share, including $19.00 of cash to be paid at closing and the remaining per share price to be paid in the form of options to be issued to Mac-Gray stockholders, representing 10% of the new equity with a strike price equal to Party B's initial cost basis. These options, which we refer to as the Party B options, would vest on the achievement of the base case management projections ( i.e. , over five years), excluding any future acquisitions. Party B's proposal stated that it valued the Party B options at $2.50 of incremental value per share\" (p.36).— Financing not committed; formal signal — final-solicitation response: \"Neither Party A's nor Party C's revised indication of interest included a firm financing commitment\" (p.35). Formality: Formal — final-solicitation response (signal 2). Conditions: Heavy — no firm financing commitment; option consideration adds contingency. Price: package value, not guaranteed cash.\n232:    Source: P-053; P-048 | Page: 36 | Review: Q4; Q5 | Related: R031 (prior priced bid)\n233: \n234: ### R040 #40 | by 09/18/2013 (final-indication deadline passed with no submission) | Party C (financial bidder) | Did not submit | proc 1 round 3 type Financial\n235:    Terms: Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior $16.00–$17.00 indication in response to the 09/11/2013 final request, and the filing states it gave no reasons. Closed at this transition; no further Party C participation is reported.\n236:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=Stated by=Unknown reason=Not stated\n237:    Why: — Stated non-submission: \"Party C did not submit a revised indication of interest or reiterate its prior indication of interest of an all-cash purchase price of $16.00 to $17.00 per share nor did it specify any reasons in connection therewith\" (p.36). Outcome basis: Stated — the filing directly reports the non-submission and that no reasons were given.\n238:    Source: P-053 | Page: 36 | Review: Q3 | Related: None\n239: \n240: ### R041 #41 | 09/19/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee | Target decision | proc 1 round 3 type None\n241:    Terms: Preferred-bidder decision: the Special Committee concluded CSC/Pamplona’s indication offered the most value, greater certainty and less risk (Party B’s options were contingent and complex and Party B would likely need third-party debt); it concluded CSC/Pamplona should be able to raise above $20.75 and authorized the Transaction Committee to offer exclusivity at $21.25; Mr. MacDonald indicated he would support $21.25.\n242:    Why: — Stated conclusion: \"the Special Committee concluded that the revised indication of interest submitted by CSC/Pamplona had the potential of delivering the most value to stockholders, provided greater certainty and involved less potential risk than the other indications\" (p.37).— Price requirement and exclusivity authorization: \"the Special Committee also concluded that, primarily in view of potential synergies between Mac-Gray and CSC, CSC/Pamplona should be in a position to increase their offer price above $20.75. The Special Committee then authorized the Transaction Committee to inform CSC/Pamplona that the Special Committee would be prepared to move into exclusivity at a price of $21.25 per share\" (p.37). \"at this meeting Mr. MacDonald indicated that he would be supportive of a price of $21.25 per share\" (p.37).\n243:    Source: P-055 | Page: 37 | Review: None | Related: R042; R043\n244: \n245: ### R042 #42 | 09/21/2013 | CSC/Pamplona (strategic bidder) | Bid | proc 1 round 3 type Strategic\n246:    Terms: Price increase to $21.25 per share all-cash as a last and best offer, provided Mac-Gray agreed to a two-week exclusive negotiation; CSC/Pamplona also requested a customary voting agreement over Mr. MacDonald’s and his immediate family’s shares. This is the price component of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal (no financing contingency; Pamplona committing 100% of the capital needed for closing).\n247:    Formality: Formal | Conditions: Light | detail: Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: requested (2 wks)\n248:    Count=0 Price=21.25-21.25 kind=Point origin=Stated cur=USD cash=Yes/21.25 due=None treat=None finality=None outb=None by=None reason=None\n249:    Why: — Stated confirmation: \"the representative of CSC/Pamplona called the members of the Transaction Committee to confirm that CSC/Pamplona were willing to increase their all-cash purchase price to $21.25 per share as a last and best offer, provided that Mac-Gray agree to a two week period of exclusive negotiations\" (p.37).— Voting agreement request: \"The representative of CSC/Pamplona also requested that shares of Mac-Gray common stock owned beneficially and of record by Mr. MacDonald and his immediate family be subject to a customary voting agreement, which we refer to as the MacDonald voting agreements\" (p.37).— Final proposal terms: \"the inclusion of a $15 million \"reverse\" termination fee payable by CSC/Pamplona to Mac-Gray in the event regulatory clearance is not obtained, which we refer to as the CSC reverse termination fee, agreements regarding certain post-signing covenants, the fact that there would be no financing contingency and that Pamplona was committing to fund 100% of the capital needed for closing\" (p.37-38). Formality: carries forward from R037 (continuing proposal; no return to a preliminary basis). Conditions: Light — Pamplona committed 100% of closing capital; no financing contingency.\n250:    Source: P-056; P-057 | Page: 37 | Review: Q4 | Related: R037 (revises R037); R043\n251: \n252: ### R043 #43 | 09/23/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee; CSC/Pamplona | Exclusivity changed | proc 1 round 3 type None\n253:    Terms: Authorized: the Special Committee authorized Mac-Gray to enter an exclusivity agreement providing exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013 on the CSC/Pamplona final proposal terms ($21.25 per share cash; $15 million CSC reverse termination fee if regulatory clearance is not obtained; no financing contingency; Pamplona to fund 100% of closing capital); the agreement would automatically terminate if CSC or Pamplona adversely changed the final proposal terms.\n254:    Why: — Stated authorization: \"After discussion, the Special Committee authorized Mac-Gray to enter into an exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013 on the terms included in the CSC/Pamplona final proposal\" (p.38).— Stated terms and condition: \"The parties also agreed that the exclusivity agreement would automatically terminate if CSC or Pamplona adversely changed any of the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal\" (p.37-38).\n255:    Source: P-059; P-057 | Page: 38 | Review: Q8 | Related: R044; R042\n256: \n257: ### R044 #44 | 09/24/2013 | CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray | Exclusivity changed | proc 1 round 3 type None\n258:    Terms: Executed: CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement — exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on 10/12/2013, subject to certain conditions including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the final proposal terms. This execution is the transition into the definitive-negotiation stage (R047).\n259:    Why: — Stated execution: \"On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, subject to certain conditions, including that CSC and Pamplona not adversely change or modify the terms of the CSC/Pamplona final proposal\" (p.38).\n260:    Source: P-060 | Page: 38 | Review: Q8 | Related: R043; R047; R045; R046\n261: \n262: ### R045 #45 | by 09/24/2013 (exclusivity execution) | Party A (strategic bidder) | Dropped by target | proc 1 round 3 type Strategic\n263:    Terms: Inferred: exclusivity — Party A was still live after the final round (its best-and-final reiteration of 09/18/2013) when Mac-Gray executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013; the filing reports no notice to Party A and states no reason. Closed at this transition.\n264:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=Inferred: exclusivity by=Target reason=Not stated\n265:    Why: — Exclusivity execution: \"On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\" (p.38).— Last participation: \"Party A reiterated in a telephone call to a representative of BofA Merrill Lynch that its previous indication of interest with an all-cash purchase price of $18.00 to $19.00 per share was its best and final offer\" (p.36). Outcome basis and agency: Inferred solely from the exclusivity execution; Decided by Target for the transition; the filing states no reason or notice.\n266:    Source: P-060; P-053 | Page: 38 | Review: Q3 | Related: R038; R044\n267: \n268: ### R046 #46 | by 09/24/2013 (exclusivity execution) | Party B (financial bidder) | Dropped by target | proc 1 round 3 type Financial\n269:    Terms: Inferred: exclusivity — Party B was still live after the final round (its 09/18/2013 $21.50 package) when Mac-Gray executed exclusivity with CSC/Pamplona on 09/24/2013; the filing reports no notice to Party B and states no reason. Closed at this transition.\n270:    Count=1 Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=None outb=Inferred: exclusivity by=Target reason=Not stated\n271:    Why: — Exclusivity execution: \"On September 24, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed the exclusivity agreement providing for exclusive negotiations until 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013\" (p.38).— Last participation: \"Party B also submitted a revised indication of interest with a purchase price that Party B valued at $21.50 per share\" (p.36). Outcome basis and agency: Inferred solely from the exclusivity execution; Decided by Target for the transition; the filing states no reason or notice.\n272:    Source: P-060; P-053 | Page: 38 | Review: Q3 | Related: R039; R044\n273: \n274: ### R047 #47 | 09/24/2013 | Mac-Gray ↔ CSC/Pamplona | Round opened | proc 1 round 4 type None\n275:    Terms: Definitive-negotiation stage opens with the 09/24/2013 exclusivity execution (R044); Goodwin Procter delivered the initial merger-agreement draft to Kirkland & Ellis on 09/25/2013 (R048) and CSC/Pamplona were granted full data-site and management access for confirmatory diligence. Selected bidder CSC/Pamplona remains live; all other bidders are already closed. Round finality: Inferred final — no announcement, but the target moved to definitive negotiation with the selected bidder.\n276:    Count=None Price=None-None kind=None origin=None cur=None cash=None/None due=None treat=None finality=Inferred final outb=None by=None reason=None\n277:    Why: — Draft delivered and confirmatory diligence: \"On September 25, 2013, Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement\" (p.38). \"CSC and Pamplona were granted full access to the electronic data site and access to certain members of management and conducted confirmatory business and legal due diligence on Mac-Gray\" (p.38).\n278:    Source: P-061 | Page: 38 | Review: Q1 | Related: R044; R048; R043; R035\n279: \n280: ### R048 #48 | 09/25/2013 | Kirkland & Ellis LLP (outside legal counsel, CSC/Pamplona) | Adviser service observed | proc 1 round 4 type None\n281:    Terms: First shown acting on the CSC/Pamplona mandate when Goodwin Procter delivered the initial merger-agreement draft to Kirkland; engagement date not disclosed. Kirkland negotiated the merger agreement and the Pamplona commitment letter for CSC/Pamplona.\n282:    Why: — Earliest observed service: \"On September 25, 2013, Goodwin Procter delivered to Kirkland & Ellis LLP, outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona, whom we refer to as Kirkland, the initial draft of the merger agreement\" (p.38).\n283:    Source: P-061 | Page: 38 | Review: None | Related: None\n284: \n285: ### R049 #49 | after 09/23/2013; reported 10/07/2013 | Moab Partners; CSC/Pamplona; Mac-Gray Special Committee | Material process update | proc 1 round 4 type None\n286:    Terms: Moab rollover resolved without a rollover: the Special Committee had allowed Mr. Rothenberg on 09/23/2013 to resume discussions with CSC/Pamplona about a possible rollover of Moab’s shares; after those discussions it was determined that Moab would not roll over any shares in the transaction, as reported to the Special Committee on 10/07/2013.\n287:    Why: — Stated permission: \"to provide Moab with the opportunity to resume discussions with CSC/Pamplona regarding a possible equity rollover of Moab's shares in the transaction if Moab still had an interest in such a rollover\" (p.38).— Stated discussion period: \"Mr. Rothenberg engaged in various discussions with representatives of Pamplona during this time to discuss a possible rollover of Moab shares\" (p.38).— Stated determination reported 10/07/2013: \"Mr. Daoust reported to the Special Committee that, after discussions between Moab and representatives of Pamplona, it was determined that Moab would not rollover any Moab shares in the transaction\" (p.39). Working date convention: the determination date is not disclosed; it is reported at the 10/07/2013 Special Committee meeting (Assigned: bound to the report).\n288:    Source: P-058; P-061; P-065 | Page: 39 | Review: Q6; Q7 | Related: R016 (denial); R010\n289: \n290: ### R050 #50 | 10/09/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee; CSC/Pamplona | Exclusivity changed | proc 1 round 4 type None\n291:    Terms: Extension authorized: the Special Committee authorized the Transaction Committee to negotiate the open issues within parameters and to extend exclusivity to 10/15/2013; CSC/Pamplona had requested extension of the 5 p.m. ET 10/12 expiry to allow continued negotiations.\n292:    Why: — Stated request and authorization: \"Kirkland had requested on behalf of CSC/Pamplona that the exclusivity agreement, due to expire at 5 p.m. ET on October 12, 2013, be extended to allow for continued negotiations of these open issues. After discussion, the Special Committee authorized the Transaction Committee to negotiate the open issues within certain parameters and in connection therewith to extend exclusivity to October 15, 2013\" (p.40).\n293:    Source: P-069 | Page: 40 | Review: Q8 | Related: R051\n294: \n295: ### R051 #51 | 10/12/2013 | CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray | Exclusivity changed | proc 1 round 4 type None\n296:    Terms: Extended: letter agreement executed extending exclusivity to 11:59 p.m. ET on 10/15/2013. The extension was authorized subject to CSC/Pamplona agreeing to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million; CSC/Pamplona agreed on 10/11/2013.\n297:    Why: — Stated execution: \"On October 12, 2013, CSC, Pamplona and Mac-Gray executed a letter agreement extending exclusivity until 11:59 p.m. ET on October 15, 2013\" (p.41).— Stated condition and agreement: \"The Special Committee confirmed that the Transaction Committee and representatives of Mac-Gray were authorized to extend the exclusivity agreement until 11:59 p.m. on ET on October 15, 2013 if CSC/Pamplona would agree to a Mac-Gray termination fee of not more than $11 million\" (p.40). \"the representative of CSC/Pamplona telephoned Mr. Daoust and agreed to the $11 million Mac-Gray termination fee\" (p.40-41).\n298:    Source: P-072; P-070; P-071 | Page: 41 | Review: Q8 | Related: R050\n299: \n300: ### R052 #52 | 10/14/2013 | Mac-Gray Special Committee; Mac-Gray Board of Directors | Target decision | proc 1 round 4 type None\n301:    Terms: BofA Merrill Lynch delivered its oral fairness opinion (confirmed in writing, dated 10/14/2013); the Special Committee unanimously determined to recommend the merger agreement; the Board, on that recommendation, unanimously approved and adopted the merger agreement and recommends stockholder adoption.\n302:    Why: — Stated opinion: \"BofA Merrill Lynch reviewed with the Special Committee its financial analysis of the consideration and delivered to the Special Committee an oral opinion, which was confirmed by delivery of a written opinion dated, October 14, 2013\" (p.41).— Stated recommendations: \"the Board (upon the recommendation of the Special Committee) unanimously determined that the merger agreement and the merger were advisable and in the best interests of Mac-Gray's stockholders, approved the merger on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the merger agreement, adopted the merger agreement and recommended that the Mac-Gray stockholders adopt and approve the merger agreement\" (p.41).\n303:    Source: P-075; P-076 | Page: 41 | Review: Q5 | Related: R053\n304: \n305: ### R053 #53 | 10/14/2013 | Mac-Gray; CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc.; CSC ServiceWorks, Inc.; Spin Holdco Inc.; CSC Fenway, Inc. | Merger agreement signed | proc 1 round 4 type None\n306:    Terms: Executed: Agreement and Plan of Merger dated as of 10/14/2013 (Mac-Gray; Holdings; CSC; Spin Holdco/Parent; CSC Fenway/Merger Subsidiary). Agreed consideration: $21.25 per share in cash, without interest, less applicable withholding. Pamplona commitment letter ($594 million) delivered; no financing condition to the Buyer Entities’ obligations; Mac-Gray termination fee $11 million; CSC reverse termination fee $15 million; Pamplona damages liability capped at $50 million (Buyer Entities unlimited). Moab voting agreement executed and the MacDonald voting agreements became effective (≈15% of shares subject to voting agreements). No go-shop is reported; the Board retained a fiduciary out to accept a superior proposal on payment of the $11 million fee.\n307:    Why: — Stated execution and related documents: \"Later in the day, on October 14, 2013, the merger agreement was executed, the Pamplona commitment letter was delivered, Moab and Parent executed the Moab voting agreement and the Mac-Donald voting agreements became effective\" (p.41).— Consideration: \"will be automatically converted into the right to receive $21.25 in cash, without interest and less applicable withholding taxes\" (p.5).— Termination fees: \"Mac-Gray has agreed to pay Parent $11 million upon the termination of the merger agreement under certain circumstances\" (p.10). \"then Parent will pay Mac-Gray the $15 million Parent termination fee\" (p.81).— Financing: \"The merger agreement does not contain any condition to the obligations of the Buyer Entities or Merger Subsidiary relating to the receipt of financing by the Buyer Entities\" (p.58). \"an aggregate of $594 million of capital (the Pamplona commitment amount)\" (p.59).— Voting agreements: \"Approximately 15% of the outstanding Mac-Gray shares on the record date for the special meeting are subject to the voting agreements\" (p.82).\n308:    Source: P-077; X-001; X-005; X-025; X-019; X-020; X-026 | Page: 41 | Review: Q5 | Related: R052; R054; R044\n309: \n310: ### R054 #54 | 10/15/2013 | Mac-Gray and CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. | Merger announced | proc 1 round post type None\n311:    Terms: Joint announcement of the execution of the merger agreement, before U.S. stock markets opened. The merger was announced as expected to close in January 2014 (first half of 2014 per the merger-agreement section); no completion is observed in this filing.\n312:    Why: — Stated announcement: \"On October 15, 2013, before the U.S. stock markets opened, Mac-Gray and CSC jointly announced the execution of the merger agreement\" (p.41).— Expected timing: \"We currently expect the merger to be completed in January 2014\" (p.14).\n313:    Source: P-078; X-008 | Page: 41 | Review: None | Related: R053\n314: \n315: ### R055 #55 | 12/04/2013 | MacKenzie Partners, Inc. (proxy solicitor, Mac-Gray) | Adviser service observed | proc 1 round post type None\n316:    Terms: Proxy solicitor for the special meeting; the proxy statement states Mac-Gray expects to retain MacKenzie Partners for the solicitation for a fee of approximately $15,000 plus out-of-pocket expenses and indemnification (expected retention, not a stated executed engagement).\n317:    Why: — Stated expected retention: \"we expect to retain MacKenzie Partners, Inc. to assist in the solicitation for a fee of approximately $15,000\" (p.23).\n318:    Source: X-010 | Page: 23 | Review: None | Related: None\n319: "}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 115, \"offset\": 210, \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/ledger_dump.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825295800,"end":1789825295966}}}}
