{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825303113,"sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e6bbb2001a4JjLWmPsSqfU9","sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","messageID":"msg_0b9e6a676001jgUUgkbSWtzYAe","type":"tool","id":"call_00_XQfMHchHZdoldLWETUsk6300","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = open('build_data.py', encoding='utf-8').read()\nold = \"page=37, related='R037 (revises R037); R043', review='Q4')\"\nnew = \"page=37, related='R037 (revises it); R043', review='Q4')\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new)\nopen('build_data.py','w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\ncd /home/uctpiaj/work && python3 /tmp/opencode/build_data.py | tail -2 && python3 /tmp/opencode/build_xlsx.py && python3 - <<'EOF' > /tmp/opencode/sumq_dump.txt\nimport openpyxl\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook('extraction/mac-gray.xlsx')\nfor name in ('Summary','Questions'):\n    ws = wb[name]\n    print('='*30, name, '='*30)\n    for r in range(1, ws.max_row+1):\n        vals = [ws.cell(row=r, column=c).value for c in range(1, ws.max_column+1)]\n        vals = [v for v in vals if v not in (None, '')]\n        if vals:\n            print(f\"[{r}] \" + \" || \".join(str(v) for v in vals))\nEOF\nhead -70 /tmp/opencode/sumq_dump.txt"},"output":"ok\nquote problems: 0\ndumped /tmp/opencode/ledger_data.json\nsaving extraction/mac-gray.xlsx\nsaved. ledger rows: 55 source rows: 109\n============================== Summary ==============================\n[1] 1. STATUS AND COMMERCIAL ACCOUNT\n[2] Status || AI first pass; not human-approved. Prepared under the supplied instruction “Reading a merger filing into a deal ledger: extraction instruction”, revision of 19 September 2026.\n[3] Source coverage || Single supplied filing: mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm — Mac-Gray Corporation DEFM14A filed 12/04/2013 (177 component pages incl. Annexes A–D). Complete Background of the Merger (printed pp.27–41) transcribed in Source text; every additional passage used is X-001–X-030. No outside sources, market data or third-party knowledge used.\n[4] Account || Mac-Gray, a NYSE-listed laundry-facilities manager (NYSE: TUC), faced activist pressure from Moab Partners (a ~9% holder that elected two directors at the 05/30/2013 annual meeting) and began a target-led sale review in mid-2013 under a Special Committee of six independent directors formed to manage insider-conflict issues. BofA Merrill Lynch approached 50 potential buyers (15 strategic, 35 financial); 20 signed confidentiality agreements, and four bid: strategic Party A (an industry party), strategic CSC/Pamplona (CSC ServiceWorks, a Pamplona portfolio company), and financial bidders Party B and Party C. Party A’s early $17.00–$19.00 proposal (06/21/2013) was overtaken as CSC/Pamplona raised through $18.50 (07/23), $19.50 (09/09) and $20.75 (09/18); Party B’s final package (valued by Party B at $21.50 = $19.00 cash plus options) and Party A’s best-and-final $18.00–$19.00 were judged less certain, and Party C stopped bidding without explanation. On 09/21/2013 CSC/Pamplona confirmed $21.25 all-cash as its last and best offer in exchange for a two-week exclusivity, and on 10/14/2013 — after negotiating the Mac-Gray termination fee down from $15 million to $11 million — the parties signed a $21.25 all-cash merger agreement, announced 10/15/2013.\n[5] Observed outcome || Signing, not closing. No post-signing competing proposal or go-shop activity is reported; HSR clearance was awaited (waiting period expired 11/27/2013), the special meeting was set for 01/08/2014 and closing was expected in January 2014 (first half of 2014 per the merger-agreement section).\n[6] Last recheck status || First delivery; no reviewer edits yet. AI original is an exact values-only copy of this ledger at delivery. Changed-cell highlighting (red bold by Row id and column vs AI original) is not implemented — an explicit Correction column is provided next to Reviewer note (see Questions, check 8).\n[7] 2. DEAL FACTS\n[8] Target || Mac-Gray Corporation, 404 Wyman Street, Suite 400, Waltham, Massachusetts 02451 (Delaware corporation; NYSE symbol TUC). Second-largest US laundry facilities management contractor; sells/services commercial laundry equipment through its product sales division.\n[9] Focal acquirer and type || CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. (CSC), a Delaware corporation and Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. portfolio company — Strategic. Acquires through Spin Holdco Inc. (Parent, wholly owned by CSC), CSC Fenway, Inc. (Merger Subsidiary), with CSC ServiceWorks Holdings, Inc. (sole stockholder of CSC). Pamplona is the owner/financier of the acquirer, not a separate bidder; parent and acquisition shells are one bidder unit.\n[10] Agreed consideration || $21.25 per share in cash, without interest, less applicable withholding — all cash; fixed cash payable at closing $21.25 (R053). Labelled calculation (not a filing-stated aggregate): 14,758,306 shares × $21.25 = $313,614,002.50.\n[11] Signing / announcement / completion || Agreement and Plan of Merger dated as of 10/14/2013 (R053); joint announcement 10/15/2013 before market open (R054); completion not observed in this filing — expected January 2014 (merger-agreement section: first half of 2014). Expected closing kept separate from the observed record.\n[12] Filing identity || Mac-Gray Corporation DEFM14A, filed 12/04/2013; source file mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm; Background of the Merger at printed pp.27–41; merger agreement Annex A; BofA fairness opinion Annex B; DGCL §262 Annex C; form of voting agreement Annex D.\n[13] Vote and process protections || Merger agreement adoption requires a majority of outstanding shares; voting agreements covered ≈15% of shares (Moab, Mr. MacDonald and family entities). Mac-Gray termination fee $11 million (≈3.2% of equity value per the filing); Parent termination fee $15 million (regulatory reverse fee); Pamplona damages liability capped at $50 million (Buyer Entities unlimited); no financing condition; no go-shop is reported, but the Board kept a fiduciary out for a superior proposal.\n[14] Special meeting items || 01/08/2014 special meeting: (1) adopt the merger agreement; (2) advisory (non-binding) \"golden parachute\" compensation vote; (3) adjournment proposal.\n[15] 3. PROCESS AND ROUND MAP\n[16] Process 1 outcome || One continuing Mac-Gray sale process (June 2013 → signing 10/14/2013). The 2011-2012 Discussions were Mac-Gray’s own attempt to acquire CSC (R001, R006) — retained only as mandate/initiation context, not a Mac-Gray sale process; no second sale attempt is observed.\n[17] Round 0 (pre-opening) || Context only, no Round-opened row: 2011-2012 Discussions; 04/05/2013 Board authorization (R002); 04/08/2013 Party A contact (R003); 06/21/2013 Party A $17.00–$19.00 proposal (R009, still standing into round 1 — Party A is a round-1 participant).\n[18] Round 1 (06/24/2013 – 07/23/2013) || Opened on the Special Committee’s 06/24/2013 decision to consider a sale and approach 50 parties — no outreach was reported before that directive, and execution began within days (first NDA 06/28/2013). Rejected boundary candidates preserved as rows: R002, R003, R007, R012–R013, R014. Purpose: preliminary indications of interest; deadline 07/23/2013 (set with the informational packages, R017) — Late bids accepted (Party B 07/24; Party C 07/24–07/25, considered 07/25). Round-1 bidders: 4 (three IOIs plus Party A’s standing proposal); 16 residual signers inferred non-submitters (R019, R021). Finality: Not final.\n[19] Round 2 (08/27/2013 – 09/09/2013) || Opened on the 08/27/2013 letter requesting revised written proposals once all four bidders’ diligence was substantially complete (authorized 08/15/2013). Deadline 09/09/2013 — Late bids accepted (Party A and Party C 09/10, reviewed 09/11). Round-2 bidders: 4. Finality: Not final.\n[20] Round 3 (09/11/2013 – 09/18/2013) || Opened on the first request for final indications of interest (calls made 09/11/2013). Deadline 09/18/2013 — Enforced (three responses; selection step 09/19). Round-3 bidders: 3 (CSC/Pamplona $20.75; Party A best-and-final reiteration; Party B $21.50 package); Party C did not submit (R040). CSC/Pamplona confirmed $21.25 last-and-best 09/21 (R042); exclusivity authorized 09/23 (R043). Finality: Announced as final.\n[21] Round 4 (09/24/2013 – 10/14/2013) || Opened on the move to exclusive definitive negotiation with the selected bidder (exclusivity executed 09/24, R044; initial merger-agreement draft 09/25, R048). Round-4 bidders: 1 (CSC/Pamplona). Finality: Inferred final. Ends with signing 10/14/2013 (R053).\n[22] Post-signing || No competing proposals or go-shop activity observed. Announcement 10/15/2013 (R054); proxy statement 12/04/2013 and special-meeting scheduling (R055). Signing is not treated as Process terminated.\n[23] Exclusivity history || Requested with the 09/09 and 09/18 bids; authorized 09/23 (R043); executed 09/24 until 5 p.m. ET 10/12 (R044); extension authorized 10/09 (R050); letter agreement 10/12 extended to 11:59 p.m. ET 10/15 (R051).\n[24] Deadline history || 07/23/2013 IOI deadline (set with the packages; R017/R020) — Late bids accepted; 09/09/2013 revised-proposal deadline (R028/R029) — Late bids accepted; 09/18/2013 final-indication deadline (R035/R036) — Enforced. No bid deadline was revised or extended; the two exclusivity expiries are not bid deadlines.\n[25] 4. PARTICIPANTS AND ADVISERS\n[26] Party A — Strategic || Anonymized strategic party in the laundry facilities management industry. First contacted 04/08/2013 (R003); unsolicited all-cash $17.00–$19.00 proposal 06/21/2013 (R009, round 0; still standing into round 1); NDA 08/05/2013 after stalled non-solicitation terms (R027); revised IOI 09/10/2013 $18.00–$19.00 (R032); best-and-final reiteration 09/18/2013 (R038, Formal, Heavy). Closed: Dropped by target at the 09/24/2013 exclusivity execution (R045; Inferred: exclusivity; Decided by Target; reason not stated).\n[27] Party B — Financial || Anonymized financial bidder. NDA 06/28/2013 (R014); IOI 07/24/2013 $17.00–$18.00 (R023); revised IOI 09/09/2013 $18.50 with no firm financing commitment (R031); final package 09/18/2013 valued by Party B at $21.50 ($19.00 cash at closing plus options worth $2.50) (R039; Formal, Heavy). Closed: Dropped by target at the 09/24/2013 exclusivity execution (R046; Inferred: exclusivity; Decided by Target; reason not stated).\n[28] Party C — Financial || Anonymized financial bidder. NDA 06/30/2013 (R015); oral IOI 07/24/2013 $15.00–$17.00 and written indication 07/25/2013 $16.00–$16.50 (R024); revised oral IOI 09/10/2013 $16.00–$17.00 (R033); did not submit or reiterate in the final round and gave no reasons. Closed: Did not submit at the 09/18/2013 deadline (R040, stated).\n[29] CSC/Pamplona — Strategic (winner) || CSC ServiceWorks, Inc. with Pamplona Capital Partners III, L.P. (one bidder unit; filing treats them as a strategic bidder pair). NDA 07/11/2013 (R018); IOIs $18.50 07/23 (R022), $19.50 09/09 with 100% capital commitment (R030), $20.75 09/18 (R037), $21.25 last-and-best 09/21 conditional on two-week exclusivity (R042); exclusivity 09/24 (R044); signed 10/14/2013 (R053). No exit row — the winner.\n[30] Residual cohort || 16 remaining financial bidders (20 signers less the four individually recorded: 2 strategic + 18 financial per the filing; Party B and Party C are individually recorded). Entry at the NDA wave (R019, Count 16); inferred non-submitters at the 07/23/2013 solicitation (R021, Count 16).\n[31] Non-entrants || 30 of the 50 approached parties did not sign confidentiality agreements or bid; no individual outcomes are disclosed and none are invented.\n[32] Ownership / country attributes (disclosed) || Moab Capital Partners, LLC / Michael M. Rothenberg ≈9.07% (1,338,127 shares); Stewart G. MacDonald, Jr. ≈16.65% (2,456,568 shares, incl. trusts); Cynthia V. Doggett 16.65%; directors and executive officers as a group (14 persons) 35.04%; all entities Delaware/US unless stated. Mr. Rothenberg is Moab’s co-founder and General Partner; the board also included a Moab-nominated director (Mr. Hyman).\n[33] Group / funding relationships || No bidding-group change occurred: no independent bidder joined (or left for) another’s bidding unit (no \"Bidding group changed\"/\"Joined group\" rows). Moab’s possible equity rollover with CSC/Pamplona was denied (07/06/2013), later permitted to be discussed and resolved without a rollover (10/07/2013) — R016, R049. Pamplona’s $594 million commitment supports the CSC bid — recorded on the bid/signing rows, not as a group change.\n[34] Advisers || BofA Merrill Lynch — financial adviser to Mac-Gray: engaged 10/23/2012 for the 2011-2012 Discussions (R001), terminated 05/15/2013 (R006), re-engaged for the strategic-alternatives review 05/30–05/31/2013 (R007); fairness opinion 10/14/2013 (R052). Goodwin Procter LLP — outside legal counsel to Mac-Gray; service observed from 05/09/2013; no engagement date disclosed (R005). Kirkland & Ellis LLP — outside legal counsel to CSC/Pamplona; service observed from 09/25/2013 (R048). MacKenzie Partners, Inc. — proxy solicitor; expected retention at ≈$15,000 reported 12/04/2013 (R055). No unclear client affiliations remain.\n[35] 5. COUNTS AND AUCTION SCREEN\n[36] Contacts (filing assertion) || 50 parties contacted: 15 potential strategic buyers and 35 potential financial buyers (R012, R013). Ledger-derived contact tally (SUMIFS, Include = Yes): \n[37] Contact total formula || =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$R:$R,'Deal ledger'!$D:$D,\"Contact\",'Deal ledger'!$E:$E,1,'Deal ledger'!$Q:$Q,\"Yes\")\n[38] Contacts — reconciliation || The SUMIFS = 50 (15 + 35). Row R003 (Party A first contact, 04/08/2013) carries Count 0 because Party A is already inside the 15-party strategic cohort — it is a first-contact record, not an additive unit; do not sum to 51.\n[39] NDAs (filing assertion)