he filing states the signer population (20).\n[49] Auction screen || Met. More than one independent prospective acquiring bidder unit executed bidder-target confidentiality agreements for the process: 20 signers including at least four independently evidenced units (Party A, CSC/Pamplona, Party B, Party C). Lender-only, adviser and rollover-holder agreements excluded (none exist here). Sample eligibility remains a research decision.\n[50] Do not add steps || Contacts (50 parties reached) ≠ submissions (round-1: 3; round-2: 4; round-3: 3) ≠ unique firms (20 entrants) ≠ outcomes (19 affected units) ≠ NDA signers (20). Different steps must not be summed.\n[51] 6. COMPARABILITY AND INPUTS\n[52] Shares and ownership || 14,758,306 shares issued and outstanding (11/27/2013); ≈104 record holders; ≈15% subject to voting agreements; Moab ≈9.07%; Mr. S. MacDonald ≈16.65%; directors and officers as a group 35.04%.\n[53] Market prices and premiums || Closing prices: $14.72 on 10/11/2013 (last trading day before Board approval); $14.93 on 10/14/2013 (last full trading day before announcement); $21.30 on 11/27/2013. 52-week high for the period ending 10/11/2013: $15.61. Stated premiums vs $21.25: ≈36% over the 52-week high and ≈44% over the $14.72 close.\n[54] Adviser analyses (not offers) || BofA implied per-share reference ranges from selected public companies: $13.50–$18.75 (2013E without acquisitions), $13.75–$19.00 (2013E with acquisitions), $13.75–$19.25 (2014E without), $12.75–$19.25 (2014E with) versus the $21.25 consideration; 20 selected precedent transactions included the May 1, 2013 Coinmach/Pamplona transaction. Analysis only — not recorded as bids.\n[55] Contingent / non-cash consideration || Party B’s 09/18/2013 package: $19.00 cash at closing plus options = 10% of new equity, strike equal to Party B’s initial cost basis, vesting over five years on achievement of base-case management projections (excluding future acquisitions); Party B valued the options at $2.50/share, for a stated package value of $21.50. All cash = No; Cash at closing = $19.00; the $2.50 option value is not guaranteed cash.\n[56] Financing inputs || Pamplona commitment letter dated 10/14/2013: $594 million of capital; no financing condition to the Buyer Entities’ obligations; Pamplona and the Buyer Entities jointly and severally liable for damages, with Pamplona capped at $50 million (Buyer Entities unlimited); CSC reverse termination fee $15 million; Mac-Gray termination fee negotiated from $15 million (Kirkland’s 10/07 proposal, ≈4.4% of equity value) to $11 million (≈3.2%).\n[57] Projections || Management Projections prepared June 2013 (without-acquisitions and with-acquisitions cases; 2013–2018), provided to the Special Committee and BofA; not updated for the merger. Used in the fairness opinion.\n[58] Other-scope proposals || None disclosed. All four bids were for the whole company; no segment, asset, minority-stake or other-scope proposals appear. The 2011-2012 Discussions concerned Mac-Gray’s possible acquisition of CSC and are not an other-scope bid for Mac-Gray.\n[59] Other inputs and normalization || Net debt, dilution and rollover treatment are not disclosed; no currency conversion or net-debt bridge has been performed (all amounts USD). The equity-value calculation above is the only labelled conversion, using the stated 14,758,306 shares.\n[60] Glossary || NDA = confidentiality/non-disclosure agreement; IOI = indication of interest; LOI = letter of intent (not used here); Party A/B/C = filing’s anonymized bidders; CSC/Pamplona = one bidder unit (CSC ServiceWorks with Pamplona as owner/financier); Round 0 = pre-opening approaches and standing proposals; Round finality = whether the round was announced/inferred final; Inferred closing = a participant closed by arithmetic/transition without a stated exit; Working date = assigned sort key with a stated method, not an observed date; Auction screen = whether >1 independent bidder unit signed bidder-ta