 (Inferred: exclusivity, Count 1 each). The 30 contacted non-signers never entered and get no outcome rows. || Base and continuing sets: p.32 (20 signers; 2 + 18 split) and p.34 (the four advanced at the 07/25/2013 meeting); Party C’s non-submission is expressly reported (p.36); exclusivity execution p.38 closes live rivals. Uncertainty: the base assumes all 20 signers were covered by the 07/23/2013 solicitation, but signings are described “over the next two months” (to late August) and Party A signed only on 08/05/2013 — if some residual signers post-date 07/23, the non-submitting set is smaller (or some should be closed at a later transition). Party A’s 04/08/2013 contact carries Count 0 because it sits inside the 15-party strategic cohort (R012). || R003, R012–R013, R019, R021, R040, R045, R046; Count fields; Summary balance || Splitting or resizing the residual cohort changes the inferred-exit count and the per-stage balance; if any of the 16 later submitted an IOI not reported in the narrative, the residual overstates non-submission — the filing’s exhaustive-sounding list (Party B, Party C, CSC/Pamplona and Party A’s standing proposal) argues against that. || Pending\n[5] Q4 || Formality and conditions borderlines || As recorded: July IOIs are Informal and Heavy by context (made before data-room/management access); September revised IOIs remain Informal except the three final-round responses, which are Formal (R037, R038, R039 — responses on the requested basis to the 09/11/2013 final-indications request), with Party A Formal on an oral best-and-final price confirmation; conditions are Heavy for Party A and Party B (no firm financing commitment), Light for CSC/Pamplona (Pamplona committed 100% of capital; no diligence condition attached) and Light for the 09/21/2013 $21.25 confirmation (carried forward). No Conditions level turns on a stated diligence period, no row is None, and there is no late reconfirmation row (the winner’s latest priced bid is Formal and sits in an Announced-as-final round, so the section 9.1 late-reconfirmation test fails). || Formality signals: final-indications request p.36; responses p.36. Conditions: no firm commitment for Party B (p.35) and Party A/Party C (p.35); Pamplona commitment (pp.35–36); pre-access IOIs (pp.33–34 data-room staging). The winner reached signing with a Formal row (R037) — no gap. || R009, R022–R024, R030–R033, R037–R039, R042; Formality, Conditions level and Conditions detail fields || Reclassifying any September IOI as Informal, or the final responses as Formal, changes the formality tallies and the Conditions detail strings; prices, outcomes and the round map are unaffected. || Pending\n[6] Q5 || Price and consideration conventions; scope || Keep as recorded: per-share cells in USD only; Party A’s ranges as Bidder range with Carried forward on the 09/18/2013 reaffirmation; Party B’s 09/18/2013 package entered as a Point at $21.50 (Party B’s stated value) with All cash = No and Cash at closing $19.00; Party C’s oral-to-written July indications treated as one bid with the written range recorded; no Bound only rows; no other-scope bids; signing row carries the agreed $21.25 in text only (no price cells). || Package value: p.36 (“Party B valued at $21.50 … $19.00 of cash … options … valued the Party B options at $2.50”); carried price p.36 (reiteration of the previous $18.00–$19.00 indication); one-communication convention applied to Party C (pp.33–34); no other-scope proposals appear anywhere in the filing. || R024, R032, R038, R039, R053; Price low/high/kind/origin, All cash, Cash at closing, Terms or outcome || If the reviewer prefers not to enter bidder-assigned package values in price cells, blank R039’s price cells and keep $21.50/$19.00/$2.50 in text; carried-forward vs restated on R038 changes Price origin only. No totals depend on these cells. || Pending\n[7] Q6 || Moab/MacDonald rollover rows and the two-row convention || Keep three rows: R016 (rollover denied as premature, 07/06/2013), R034 (Mr. MacDonald’s rollover question resolved and his support position, 09/11–09/12/2013) and R049 (Moab discussions permitted 09/23/2013 and resolved without a rollover, reported 10/07/2013). No separate row for the 09/23/2013 permission, per the instruction’s “at most one row when permitted, denied or formed and one when resolved” convention for rollover relationships. || Denial and rationale p.32–33; permission p.38; discussions and determination pp.38–39; MacDonald’s position pp.35–36. The filing never shows a formed rollover or any financing-support relationship between Moab and CSC/Pamplona, and no voting/group change results. || R016, R034, R049; Material process update rows; Summary group/funding note || Adding a fourth row for the 09/23/2013 permission changes row counts only; reclassifying these as Bidding group changed would be wrong (a rollover holder is not a bidding-unit member) and would distort the unit counts. || Pending\n[8] Q7 || Assigned Working dates and display order within rounds || Accept the disclosed conventions: R012/R013 (wave) use the first day of the reported window (06/24/2013); R017 uses the midpoint of 06/28–07/23 (07/10/2013); R019 is moved earlier inside its window to 07/23/2013 (Assigned: sequence) so the residual cohort’s entry precedes its inferred non-submission; R024 and R034 use the first day of a reported interval; R045/R046 use the transition date (Assigned: decision day); R049 uses the 10/07/2013 report bound. Sorting by Working date with # as tiebreak reproduces the reading order; no Working date falls outside its own window. Source quirks retained: the filing’s “July 27, 2103” typo (R027; intended 2013) and a duplicated sentence in the informational-package paragraph (Source text P-023). || Rules applied from the instruction, section 8.1; the order constraint drove R019’s sequence assignment (entry must precede R021’s inferred closing); each affected row’s reason states its convention. || R012, 