{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825332629,"sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e71d42001vBfM3zff8qWRMe_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f46293753ffeU5Yf7iVUgOE0mm","messageID":"msg_0b9e71d42001vBfM3zff8qWRMe","type":"text","text":"Done. The workbook is at **`extraction/mac-gray.xlsx`** — a complete, reasoned, source-supported first pass under the supplied instruction (revision of 19 September 2026), built only from `raw_filing/mac-gray_2013-12-04_DEFM14A.htm`.\n\n## What the filing shows\n\nMac-Gray (NYSE: TUC), a US laundry-facilities manager, ran a target-led sale process from mid-2013, with a six-director Special Committee formed to handle insider conflicts (CEO MacDonald's ~17% stake; activist Moab's ~9% and its rollover interest). BofA Merrill Lynch, on the Committee's June 24, 2013 directive, approached 50 parties (15 strategic + 35 financial); 20 signed confidentiality agreements. Four bid: strategic **Party A** ($17.00–$19.00 from June 21), strategic **CSC/Pamplona** (CSC ServiceWorks, a Pamplona portfolio company: $18.50 → $19.50 → $20.75), financial **Party B** ($17–18 → $18.50 → a $21.50 package of $19.00 cash plus options) and financial **Party C** (which stopped bidding). After screening a $15M fee down to $11M, Mac-Gray signed an **all-cash $21.25/share** merger agreement on **October 14, 2013** (announced October 15), after CSC/Pamplona's $21.25 \"last and best\" bought two weeks of exclusivity. The observed outcome is **signing, not closing**: HSR expired Nov 27, the special meeting was set for Jan 8, 2014, and closing was expected in January 2014.\n\n## Ledger shape\n- **55 rows** across one process and four rounds (R1 06/24, R2 08/27, R3 09/11, R4 09/24), plus round 0; 14 visible columns + collapsed expandable groups; 108 source rows (all 78 background paragraphs + 30 additional passages X-001–X-030); Quotes were programmatically matched to the source text.\n- Counts reconcile: 50 contacted (15+35), 20 NDA signers (4 named + 16 residual), round bidders 4/4/3/1, exits 2 dropped + 17 did-not-submit, ending with the winner. Auction screen: **Met**.\n\n## Most consequential review items (Q1–Q8)\n- **Q1 round map** — recommend 4 rounds; the alternative is a 3-round map folding R4 (exclusive definitive negotiation, Inferred final) into R3. Round-1 anchor candidates are preserved as rows.\n- **Q3 inferred closings** — 16 residual non-submitters (20−4) at the July 23 due date; Party A/B dropped by the Sept 24 exclusivity; base assumes all 20 signers were covered by the July 23 solicitation (some may have signed later).\n- **Q4 formality/conditions** — the three Sept 18 final-round responses are Formal (best-and-final signal); July IOIs Heavy by context; CSC/Pamplona Light (committed financing).\n- **Q2 deadlines** — July 23 and Sept 9 \"Late bids accepted\"; Sept 18 \"Enforced\". **Q7** assigned-date conventions; **Q6** rollover rows; **Q5** Party B's non-cash package; **Q8** exclusivity row granularity.\n\n## Check results and limitations\nChecks 1, 3, 6, 7 **Passed**; checks 2, 4, 5, 8 **Qualified** (residual base assumption, assigned-date conventions, judgment classifications, and workbook-operation testing). Unsupported feature: changed-cell highlighting is **not** implemented — AI original is retained as the values baseline with a Correction column beside Reviewer note, and no dependent auto-update is claimed. Formulas and hyperlinks were verified programmatically and by XML inspection, but **not recalculated in a spreadsheet application** (LibreOffice crashes in this environment; Excel unavailable).","time":{"start":1789825326410,"end":1789825332629}}}
